__kbPart({"name":"WUJI","content":{"WUJI-Developer-Guide":"---\ntype: dev-guide\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, dev-guide]\n---\n# WUJI — Developer Guide (hackathon edition)\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [Product portfolio](WUJI-Products.md) · [Roadmap and strategy](WUJI-Roadmap-and-Strategy.md)\n\n> **Scope:** WUJI is a component vendor: two 20-DoF hands (Wuji Hand gen 1, Wuji Hand 2) and a tactile + pose glove (Wuji Glove). There is no arm, base or on-board computer. Everything below is about driving the hand joints and reading the glove from your own PC. All facts are from the official docs (docs.wuji.tech, state of **2026-11-10**) and the `wuji-technology` GitHub repos unless marked.\n\n## TL;DR — how you program it\n\n- **One SDK for everything:** `pip install wuji-sdk` (Python, CPython 3.8–3.14) or the C package. Same API pattern for Hand 2, Hand gen 1 and Glove: `device.{resource}().{get|set|subscribe|publish}()`.\n- **Joint level only:** you send 20 joint targets at up to **1 kHz**. Hand 2 defaults to **MIT mode** (position + velocity + current feed-forward, per-joint kp / kd); whole-hand **position mode is Beta** and needs firmware **v3.0.0**. There is no grasp planner, no perception, no skill library.\n- **Wired, static IP:** Hand 2 and Glove talk Ethernet on `192.168.1.x` (no DHCP); Hand gen 1 is USB. Budget one wired NIC (or a switch) per team laptop.\n- **Fastest demo = glove teleop:** `examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py` mirrors a Wuji Glove onto a hand; official estimate **45 min** from unboxing. No glove free? Any source of 21 MediaPipe keypoints (webcam, VR headset) feeds the same `RetargetSession`.\n- **Develop without hardware:** `wuji-description` has URDF / MJCF / MJX / USD for all hand revisions; a MuJoCo viewer check takes **10 min**. ROS 2 drivers (`wuji-ros2`) exist but target **Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical** only.\n\n## SDKs and interfaces\n\n| SDK / repo | Language | What it controls | Link | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ✅ **Wuji SDK** (`wuji-sdk`) | Python (primary), C11 | Hand 2, Hand gen 1, Glove: discovery, connect, streams, joint commands, parameters, MCAP recording, retargeting | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) | MIT. Linux x86_64 / arm64 (glibc ≥ 2.17 Python, ≥ 2.31 C), macOS 11+ Apple silicon, Windows 10 21H2+ / 11 x64. C package also for Android aarch64. Current release **v2026.11.9** |\n| ✅ **Wuji CLI** (`wuji`) | Binary (terminal) | Scan, ping, get / set parameters, subscribe, live viewer, glove calibration, health check, logs, firmware upgrade | [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/introduction.md) · [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-cli) | Install: `curl -fsSL https://get.wuji.tech/cli \\| bash` (Linux / macOS), `irm https://get.wuji.tech/cli.ps1 \\| iex` (PowerShell). `--json` / `--jsonl` output for scripts |\n| ✅ CLI agent skills | Skill bundle | Lets an AI coding agent run the CLI (scan, calibrate, doctor, logs, upgrade, viz) | [CLI getting started](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/getting-started.md) | `npx --yes skills add wuji-technology/wuji-cli -g`. Docs warn: the agent can write parameters and move hardware — review before it runs |\n| ✅ **wuji-ros2** | C++ / ROS 2 | `wuji_hand2_driver` (states, commands, services), `wuji_glove_driver` (data only), `wuji_msgs`, `wuji_bringup`, `wuji_tools` | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) · [Hand 2 guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/ros2-integration.md) · [Glove guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/ros2-integration.md) | MIT. **ROS 2 Lyrical on Ubuntu 26.04**, x86_64 / aarch64. Source build; release notes also mention the apt package `ros-lyrical-wuji-bringup` |\n| ✅ **wuji-description** | URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD, STEP | Models of Hand gen 1, Hand 2.1, Hand 2.2 and the glove hand skeleton | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) · [loading guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/model-integration.md) | MIT. ROS 2 packages `wuji_hand2_1_description`, `wuji_hand2_2_description` |\n| ✅ SDK retargeting (`RetargetSession`) | Python, C | 21 keypoints (MediaPipe order, metres) → 20 joint angles for Hand or Hand 2 | [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md) | Built into the SDK; needs only `numpy`. Wheels with retargeting: Linux x86_64 / aarch64 and macOS arm64 — **not Windows, not Intel Mac** |\n| ✅ **wuji-mjlab** | Python (mjlab, PPO) | RL: in-hand cube reorientation (both generations), pen spinning (Hand 2), sim-to-real bridge | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) | Apache-2.0. Linux x86_64, NVIDIA GPU, CUDA 12.8, **pixi only** |\n| ✅ **wuji-isaaclab** | Python (Isaac Lab 2.3.2, rsl_rl) | Cube reorientation for Hand 2 in Isaac Sim 5.1 | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) | Apache-2.0. glibc ≥ 2.35, NVIDIA driver ≥ 580.65.06 |\n| ✅ **wuji-openpi** | Python (JAX), ROS 2 Humble | Fine-tune and deploy pi0 / pi0.5 on single- or dual-arm + Wuji Hand rigs | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | Apache-2.0 fork of Physical Intelligence openpi. Linux x86_64, CUDA 12, Python 3.11+, `uv` |\n| ✅ **toporetarget** | Python | Human hand-object motion → Wuji Hand reference motion (CPU only) | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) | MIT. Research code (CoRL 2026 paper) |\n| ✅ wuji-hand-teleop | ROS 2 Humble, Docker | Glove → hands, HTC Vive Tracker / PICO 4 → arms, stereo video to headset, MCAP capture | [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) | MIT. README: **not actively maintained**; reference arms are Tianji 7-DoF |\n| Legacy: `wujihandpy`, `wujihandros2`, Wuji Studio, HMI, Upgrader, `wuji-retargeting` | Python / ROS 2 / desktop | Hand gen 1 tooling | [archived docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/archived.md) | Superseded by SDK + CLI. `pip install wujihandpy` still works for gen 1 (Ubuntu 22.04 / 24.04) |\n\n**Low-level transport:** Hand 2 and Glove use a proprietary UDP protocol (Hand 2 port **50001**; glove examples in the docs show both `:50000` and `:50001`, so use the address `wuji devices` prints); Hand gen 1 uses a proprietary USB 2.0 protocol. No public CAN, EtherCAT, Modbus or raw-protocol spec was found — the SDK is the supported entry point.\n\n## Control levels\n\n| Level | Available? | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| Task / skill API (grasp, pinch, handover) | ✗ none | You write grasps as joint trajectories, teleoperate, or learn them |\n| Grasp planning / perception | ✗ none | Bring your own camera and planner |\n| Retargeting (human hand → 20 joints) | ✅ | `RetargetSession.for_hand(HandModel.WujiHand2, side=Handedness.Right)`, then `session.step(keypoints)` |\n| Joint position targets | ✅ | Hand 2: MIT mode with kp / kd, or position mode (Beta). Hand gen 1: position control only |\n| Joint impedance (MIT) | ✅ Hand 2 | `τ = kp·(q_d − q) + kd·(dq_d − dq) + τ_ff`; set with `hand.mit_params().set((kp, kd))` or a list of 20 |\n| Current feed-forward | ✅ Hand 2 | `JointCommand(position, velocity, effort)`; `effort` is **current in A** in MIT mode |\n| True joint-torque control / external force sensing | ✗ | `joint_states.effort` is measured current (MIT) or an estimated net torque in N·m (position mode). Docs say **do not** use it to judge contact force on 2.2 units |\n| Firmware / motor-driver access | ✗ | Closed firmware; upgrades via `wuji upgrade` |\n\n**Rates and numbers (Hand 2):**\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Device control loop | **1000 Hz × 20 axes** (one message carries all 20 joints) |\n| Command publish rate | up to **1 kHz** (`hand.joint_command().publish()`) |\n| `joint_states` stream | **1000 Hz** native; lower it with `sub.set_rate(hz)` |\n| IMU stream | **100 Hz** (angular velocity + acceleration, no orientation) |\n| GET queries | keep at or below **100 Hz** |\n| Conservative MIT start values | `effort_limit = 0.5 A` for first tests; gentle hold at `kp = 3.0`, `kd = 0.05`, `effort_limit = 1.5 A` |\n| Factory MIT defaults on new units | kp = 5.0, kd = 0.1 (per the solutions register; check the SDK log line printed on connect) |\n| Position mode (Beta) | needs firmware **v3.0.0**; limits in **N·m**, default **300 %** of each joint's rated torque; command low-pass default **40 Hz**; mode resets to MIT after every power cycle |\n| Joint order | thumb 0–3, index 4–7, middle 8–11, ring 12–15, pinky 16–19 (`{finger}_S1..S4`) |\n| Units | rad, rad/s; angles only from `joint_states` |\n\n**Hand gen 1:** position control, 1000 Hz × 20 axes, USB. It is **not back-drivable** — never force the fingers by hand. Driven by the unified SDK on Linux and Apple-silicon macOS (not Windows), or by the older `wujihandpy` (`hand.finger(1).joint(0).write_joint_target_position(1.57)`).\n\n**Editions:** no EDU / developer / pro tiers are published. Every unit exposes the same SDK. What differs is the **hardware revision**:\n\n| Revision | How to tell | What you get |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hand 2.2 Beta | serial positions 5–7 = `A01` | current firmware line (v3.0.0 on 2026-11-10), 11–13 V input, position mode (Beta), soft-pad link in the models. Built-in feed-forward compensation only on units shipped from October 2026 |\n| Hand 2.1 Beta | serial `A00` | **12 V only**, firmware frozen at v1.2.4, newer SDK features (including position mode) unavailable; use `model_revision:=1` in ROS 2 |\n| Hand gen 1 | USB device | position control, self-locking joints, optional paired tactile glove (`hand.is_tactile_attached()`) |\n\n## ROS 2 and middleware\n\n- **Official target:** Ubuntu **26.04** + ROS 2 **Lyrical**, x86_64 or aarch64. If your laptop runs Humble or Jazzy, either use a container with host networking or skip ROS and bridge the Python SDK into your own node (about 30 lines: subscribe `joint_states`, publish `JointCommand`).\n- **Build:** clone `wuji-ros2`, run `scripts/install_hand2_descriptions.sh`, `rosdep install`, `colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF`. The build downloads the C SDK (v2026.10.12); offline builds pass `-DWUJI_SDK_ROOT=<path>`.\n- **Find devices:** `ros2 run wuji_tools wuji_list`.\n\n| Hand 2 interface (namespace-relative) | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `joint_states` (pub) | `sensor_msgs/msg/JointState` | position rad, velocity rad/s, `effort` = **current in A** |\n| `joint_diagnostics` (pub) | `wuji_msgs/msg/JointDiagnosticsArray` | status words, fault codes, voltage, temperature |\n| `imu` (pub) | `sensor_msgs/msg/Imu` | no orientation (`orientation_covariance[0] = -1`) |\n| `joint_commands` (sub) | `sensor_msgs/msg/JointState` | named subset or 20 values in fixed order. **Unlisted joints are driven to zero** |\n| `set_enabled`, `clear_faults` | `wuji_msgs/srv/…` | 20-entry mask |\n| `set_effort_limit(s)`, `set_mit_params` | `wuji_msgs/srv/…` | current limits in A; 20 kp / kd values |\n| `emergency_stop` | `std_srvs/srv/Trigger` | not latched: stop publishing afterwards |\n\n- **Launch:** `ros2 launch wuji_bringup hand2_view.launch.py serial_number:=… hand_side:=… model_revision:=2 namespace:=hand` (view only, never enables), `hand2.launch.py … auto_enable:=true` (control), then `ros2 run wuji_bringup hand2_wave_demo --ros-args -r __ns:=/hand` (100 Hz wave).\n- **Glove driver:** `ros2 launch wuji_bringup glove.launch.py serial_number:=… namespace:=glove`. 10 topics: `joint_angles`, `emf_poses`, `tip_poses`, `hand_skeleton`, `imu/palm`, `tactile`, `tactile/residual`, `tactile/binary`, `tactile/zones`, `tactile/points` (PointCloud2). All **best-effort** QoS — a reliable subscriber receives nothing. The glove driver holds an **exclusive** connection (no `wuji viz` in parallel).\n- **TF:** the hand model root is `l_mount` / `r_mount` (the arm flange mount). Your arm stack must publish the transform from its tool flange to that frame.\n- **DDS:** if RViz shows no TF or demos get no data, check namespace and `ROS_DOMAIN_ID`, then try `rmw_cyclonedds_cpp`.\n- **Other middleware:** the SDK \"bridge\" (`enable_bridge=True`, default) lets several SDK processes — also on other hosts — share one device. `wuji-hand-teleop` and `wuji-openpi` use **ROS 2 Humble** inside Docker with their own topic layout, separate from `wuji-ros2`.\n\n## Simulation and digital twins\n\n| Asset | Format | How to load | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Hand 2.2 | MJCF | `python -m mujoco.viewer --mjcf=hand2/hand2_2/body/mjcf/right.xml` | MuJoCo 2.3+. 20 revolute joints; collision = convex hull per link, 27 colliding links |\n| Hand 2.2 | USD | `hand2/hand2_2/body/usd/{left,right}/wujihand2_2.usd` | Isaac Sim 2024.x+; keep the whole `usd/` folder (layered asset) |\n| Hand 2.2 | URDF (+ ROS variant) | `urdf-viz hand2/hand2_2/body/urdf/right.urdf` or RViz via `wuji_bringup` | URDF is the source of truth for the mount frame |\n| Hand 2.1, Hand gen 1 | URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD | same repo, per-revision folders | bare, cover and glove variants |\n| Glove hand skeleton | URDF (21 DoF) + EMF module STL | `urdf-viz glove/body/urdf/right.urdf` | for checking frames and data mapping |\n| CAD | STEP, A3 drawings | palm mounting interface, flange mount (69 g), full hand | re-download if fetched before 2026-11-10 (STEP files were corrected) |\n\n- **Actuator names in the models:** `{l,r}_{THJ|FFJ|MFJ|RFJ|LFJ}{0-3}`. The mapping between SDK labels `S1..S4` and model actuators `J0..J3` is **not published yet** — verify joint by joint in the viewer before trusting a sim-to-real script.\n- **Limits:** rigid-body only; fingertip soft pads are separate rigid links, no deformable simulation. Joint limits in the models match the real hand and are mirrored left / right.\n- **RL environments:** `wuji-mjlab` (MuJoCo Warp, tasks Cube Reorient and PenSpin) and `wuji-isaaclab` (`Wuji-Hand2-Reorient-v0`). Both export ONNX; the mjlab repo carries the sim-to-real deployment stack.\n- **Live digital twin:** `wuji viz` opens a Rerun web viewer where a 3D hand follows the real joint states (Hand 2) or shows skeleton + tactile matrix (Glove). One viewer page per session.\n\n## AI stack\n\n| Piece | Status | What exists | Hackathon reality |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WUJI foundation model / VLA weights | ✗ not published | none | Do not plan on a WUJI checkpoint |\n| VLA fine-tuning | ✅ `wuji-openpi` | pi0 / pi0.5 supervised fine-tuning, policy server (WebSocket / ROS 2), reference config `pi05_wuji_multi_54d` (7 + 7 arm, 20 + 20 hand = **54-D**); arm count and DoF are config values | Needs CUDA 12 GPU, upstream `pi05_base` weights and your own demos (WUJI's report used 200 per skill). Tight for 48 h |\n| LeRobot | ◐ dataset format only | `wuji-openpi` trains on **LeRobot v2.1** datasets converted from ROS 2 MCAP; expected keys `observation.state`, `observation.images.cam_high`, `cam_left_wrist`, `cam_right_wrist`, `action` | No native LeRobot robot / teleoperator plugin for Wuji devices was found. The README describes the conversion step but check the repo for the converter before you rely on it |\n| Pretrained RL policies | ✅ | `wuji-mjlab` release **v2026.10.22**: cube-reorient checkpoints per hand and five pen-spin sets (`model.pt`, `policy.onnx`), 40 motion clips, jig CAD | Replays need the camera + tag rig from the repo; a show piece, not a track solution |\n| Retargeting | ✅ | SDK `RetargetSession`; `toporetarget` for contact-preserving object manipulation references | The practical \"AI\" most teams will use |\n| Teleoperation | ✅ | Glove → hand (`1.teleop_real.py`, Python and C); hand + arm via `wuji-hand-teleop` (unmaintained) | Hand-only teleop works in under an hour; arm teleop means integrating a partner arm yourself |\n| Data collection | ✅ | `TopicRecorder` → **MCAP** (LZ4), multi-device, episodes, live metrics and alerts; glove raw data can be re-solved offline | Record `joint_states` + glove streams with device-side UTC-synced timestamps |\n| Egocentric data model | ✅ (research) | MINT: video → two-hand motion, weights and annotations for 1,021 h of video | See [papers](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md); not needed for a first build |\n\nMinimal recording pattern (Python): `recorder = TopicRecorder(compression=\"lz4\")`, `recorder.record(hand.joint_states().subscribe())`, `handle = await recorder.start(\"./data/episode_001.mcap\")`; start again with a new path for the next episode.\n\n## Compute, sensors and connectivity\n\n| Item | Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) | Hand gen 1 | Glove |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| On-board application compute | none | none | none (acquisition board on the forearm) |\n| Host | your PC / Jetson-class board; WUJI benchmarks on Jetson AGX Orin | same | same |\n| Data link | **RJ45 Ethernet 100BASE-TX**, static IP | **USB 2.0** (USB-C) | RJ45 via USB-C-to-Ethernet power adapter |\n| Default address | left `192.168.1.110`, right `192.168.1.111`, port 50001 | — (USB) | left `192.168.1.100`, right `192.168.1.101` |\n| Power | **11–13 V DC**, ≥ 200 W, XT30; 12 V 20 A adapter supplied | 12–20 V DC, XT30, ≥ 10 A, 420 W transient | USB 5 V / 1 A |\n| Sensors | joint position, velocity, current; per-joint temperature and voltage (diagnostics); IMU 100 Hz. **No tactile, no camera** | joint state; optional tactile glove accessory | 526-point tactile matrix 120 FPS; 5 EMF 6-DoF trackers 120 Hz; IMU 800 Hz |\n| Derived streams | — | — | tactile zones, binary contact, residual, 3D tactile point cloud, fingertip poses, 21-DoF joint angles, 21-keypoint skeleton, fused IMU |\n| Wireless | none | none | none |\n| Time base | device timestamps synced to host UTC by the SDK (NTP-style exchange) | host-stamped | device-stamped, synced |\n| Status light | blue breathing = self-check, white breathing = ready, solid white = enabled, red slow flash = fault, solid red = critical (power-cycle) | blue solid = firmware update in progress | see glove docs |\n\n- **Multi-client:** several SDK programs can share a device by default (visualiser + recorder + your app). The CLI falls back to read-only when another session owns the device.\n- **Telemetry:** the SDK uploads anonymous usage data by default; disable with `WUJI_TELEMETRY_DISABLE=1`.\n- **Docker:** official image recipe in `wuji-sdk/docker` (Ubuntu 22.04, Python 3.10); run with `--network host` and mount `~/.wuji` for calibration data.\n\n## First 60 minutes checklist\n\n1. **Ask WUJI staff (2 min):** which hand revision (gen 1, 2.1 or 2.2), which firmware, left or right, which flange adapters, and whether you may upgrade firmware yourself. Read the serial number: 4th character `J` = left, `K` = right.\n2. **Sim check, no hardware (10 min):** `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description.git && pip install mujoco && python -m mujoco.viewer --mjcf=wuji-description/hand2/hand2_2/body/mjcf/right.xml`. Done when 20 joints render.\n3. **Install (5 min):** `python -m pip install wuji-sdk numpy`; `curl -fsSL https://get.wuji.tech/cli | bash`; verify with `python -c \"from wuji_sdk import SdkManager\"`.\n4. **Wire Hand 2 (5 min):** RJ45 to your laptop, XT30 to the hand first, then plug in the adapter. Wait for blue → white breathing (under 30 s). Clear the finger workspace.\n5. **Network (5 min):** set your wired NIC to `192.168.1.50/24` (Linux: `sudo ip addr add 192.168.1.50/24 dev <iface>`). `ping 192.168.1.111` (right) or `.110` (left).\n6. **Verify (3 min):** `wuji devices` then `wuji ping` — note serial, firmware, IP. With several hands on one switch always pass `--sn`.\n7. **Connect and health-check (5 min):**\n   `hand = SdkManager.instance().connect(sn=\"<SN>\", device_name=\"hand\")`; `print(hand.online_joints_count().get())` must print **20**; subscribe `hand.joint_diagnostics()` and decode any `error_code_current` with `WujiHand2.describe_error(code)`.\n8. **Hello-world motion (10 min):** `hand.effort_limit().set(1.5)`; `hand.mit_params().set((3.0, 0.05))`; `hand.enable()`; read the current pose from `hand.joint_states().subscribe()`; then publish `JointCommand(position, 0.0, 0.0)` × 20 through `hand.joint_command().publish()` at 200 Hz, interpolating to zero over 1.5 s. Never send a step change. The official script is in the [Hand 2 quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/quick-start.md); ready-made motions: `examples/python/wuji_hand_2/7.mit_sweep.py` (tiny single-joint sweep) and `8.position_mode.py`.\n9. **Read sensors (5 min):** `wuji viz --sn <SN>` for the live 3D view; in code, `sub = hand.joint_states().subscribe(); frame = sub.recv()` (position, velocity, current) and `hand.imu().subscribe()`.\n10. **Glove (10 min, if you have one):** wire the acquisition board (mind the USB-C label orientation), `ping 192.168.1.101`, put the glove on with fingers relaxed, `wuji doctor`, then `sub = glove.hand_skeleton().subscribe()` and `glove.tactile().subscribe()`. Run `python examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py` (press Enter for the default SDK user; set `SIDE` for a left hand).\n11. **Stop cleanly:** `hand.disable()`; `manager.disconnect_all()`; power down only when the hand is at rest. Emergency: `hand.emergency_stop()`.\n\nHand gen 1 variant of steps 4–8: plug USB-C + power, on Linux add the udev rule from the [gen-1 SDK guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wujihandpy/latest/introduction.md), connect with `manager.connect(sn=<usb device sn>, device_name=\"wuji_hand\")` after filtering `manager.scan()` by `TransportType.Usb`.\n\n## Known gotchas and safety\n\n- **Beta hardware.** Hand 2.1 and 2.2 are prototypes: docs give **no guarantee** on durability, drop, thermal behaviour or load values, and ask you not to run long high-load tests. Treat the hand as borrowed lab equipment.\n- **No safety-rated function.** Thermal derating, over-current stop and soft limits protect the device, not people. Keep hands away from moving fingers; do not grasp fragile or valuable objects.\n- **High kp + big step = full-speed fingers.** Always ramp targets and start with a low `effort_limit`.\n- **Teleop example needs new firmware.** Since 2026-11-10 the SDK teleop examples switch Hand 2 to position mode first; on firmware older than v3.0.0 the mode switch fails and the example exits. Either upgrade (`wuji upgrade`, never cut power) or pin an SDK / example version that matches the firmware.\n- **Mode confusion.** `effort` and `effort_limit` are **A** in MIT mode and **N·m** in position mode; limits are not converted when you switch. Control mode resets to MIT at power-up.\n- **ROS 2 driver has no command watchdog.** Stopping your publisher does not stop the hand; a named `joint_commands` message drives unlisted joints to zero; `emergency_stop` is not latched.\n- **Comms loss.** With firmware v2.1.0+ a dropped link while enabled stops the motors and raises a fault; you must call `enable()` again. No hot-plugging of power or Ethernet.\n- **Static IP collisions.** All left hands ship as `.110`, all right hands as `.111`, gloves `.100` / `.101`. Two teams on one switch will collide — change the device IP (SDK device operations) or keep each rig on its own NIC. `connect(handedness=…)` raises `AmbiguousHandedness` when two same-side devices are visible.\n- **Queue lag in teleop.** `sub.recv()` returns the oldest unread frame; drain to the latest frame each loop or use callbacks.\n- **Glove tracking.** EMF degrades within **3 cm** of metal and near magnets (robot flanges, tools, laptops); the SDK warns when confidence stays below 0.85. Humidity < 55 % RH. The built-in default hand model is currently more reliable than per-user calibration — start with the default SDK user.\n- **Thermal.** Hand 2 derates total current above **85 °C** MCU temperature and stops above 100 °C; the housing gets hot. Room temperature 15–30 °C is the specified range — fine in the arena, not outdoors in November.\n- **Environment.** Dry, clean, indoor only (gen 1 is IP40; Hand 2 has no published rating). Keep the skin and soft pads fitted: the finger flex cables underneath are fragile.\n- **Platform holes.** Windows: no gen-1 hand, no retargeting, reduced examples. macOS: Apple silicon only, allow local-network access for the terminal. ROS 2: Lyrical only.\n- **Connector change announced.** The XT30 + RJ45 layout and voltage range \"will change in later versions\" — do not design a permanent mount around them.\n- **Fault help:** `wuji doctor`, `wuji logs export`, SDK log at `~/.wuji/logs/`, and `describe_error(code)`.\n\n## Community resources\n\n| Resource | Link | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Developer docs (EN / ZH, with `llms.txt` index for AI assistants) | [docs.wuji.tech](https://docs.wuji.tech) · [index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt) | Everything above, per product |\n| Release notes (fortnightly) | [release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) | Check which firmware / SDK pair you have |\n| GitHub organisation | [wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) | SDK examples, ROS 2, models, RL, VLA |\n| SDK examples | [examples/python](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk/tree/main/examples/python) · [examples/c](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk/tree/main/examples/c) | Numbered scripts per device |\n| Video guides | [docs videos page](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md) · [YouTube @WUJI_TECH](https://www.youtube.com/@WUJI_TECH/videos) | Glove calibration tutorial, demos |\n| Support | support@wuji.tech (attach a `wuji logs export` bundle) | Hardware faults |\n| Sales / partnership | sales@wuji.tech | After the hackathon |\n| Forum / Discord | not found | Ask the WUJI engineers on site |\n\nRelated in this pack: [solutions and projects](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md) · [papers and research](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md).\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) · [installation and environment](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/quick-start.md) · [device discovery and connection](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/device-connection.md) · [data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md) · [time synchronization](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/time-sync.md) · [hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md) · [Docker deployment](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/docker-deployment.md) · [best practices](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/advanced.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/quick-start.md) · [control guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/control-guide.md) · [user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md) · [electrical and network integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/electrical-network-integration.md) · [ROS 2 integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/ros2-integration.md) · [model assets and loading](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/model-integration.md) · [data streams overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference.md) · [effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md) · [position control practice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-practice/position-mode.md) · [maintenance](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/maintenance.md) · [troubleshooting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/troubleshooting.md) · [version identification and compatibility](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/user-notice.md) · [Wuji Hand SDK (wujihandpy) getting started](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wujihandpy/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji Glove quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/getting-started.md) · [data streams overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/index.md) · [ROS 2 integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/ros2-integration.md)\n- [Wuji CLI overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/introduction.md) · [getting started](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/getting-started.md) · [live visualization](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/visualization.md)\n- [Wuji Docs release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n- GitHub: [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) ([Python examples README](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk/blob/main/examples/python/README.md)) · [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) · [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) · [wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) · [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) · [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop)\n- In this pack: [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [product portfolio](WUJI-Products.md) · [solutions and projects](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md) (revision batches, default kp / kd, repo status carried over from their sources)\n","WUJI-Papers-and-Research":"---\ntype: papers\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, papers]\n---\n# WUJI — Papers and Research\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [Solutions and projects](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md) · [Developer guide](WUJI-Developer-Guide.md)\n\n> **Coverage note (read first):** this pass was built from pages opened directly (arXiv, the paper project page, the `wuji-technology` GitHub READMEs, Wuji Docs, wuji.tech). The open-web search budget for this run was exhausted before any paper hunt could be run, so **the third-party section is a lower bound, not a census**. Everything listed below was opened and checked; nothing is listed from memory.\n\n## Research footprint\n\n- **One peer-reviewed paper, a lot of open code.** The only paper tied to WUJI that could be confirmed is **TopoRetarget (CoRL 2026, arXiv 2606.16272)**. The rest of the research output ships as citable open-source repositories (RL, retargeting, teleoperation, VLA fine-tuning), not as papers.\n- **Academic link: IIIS, Tsinghua University.** The TopoRetarget paper lists a single affiliation (IIIS, Tsinghua; corresponding author **Hang Zhao**), yet the code lives in the WUJI GitHub organisation, support goes to support@wuji.tech, and the same people are the listed contributors of WUJI's own repos. Whether individual authors are WUJI employees, interns or Tsinghua students is **not stated** — ⚠️ unverified.\n- **Recurring names** across WUJI repos: **Guanqi He** and **Xiaohan Liu** (project leads of TopoRetarget), **Wentao Zhang**, **Jielin Wu**, **Shenzhe Yao**, **Han Yang**, **Xiangrui Jiang**. Guanqi He and Wentao Zhang are the cited authors of `wuji-retargeting`; Guanqi He is first cited author of `wuji-hand-teleop`.\n- **Open-source posture: strong.** 24 public repos; MIT for SDK, models, retargeting and teleop; Apache-2.0 for the RL and VLA stacks. Trained RL checkpoints, motion clips and CAD for the test rigs are published as GitHub release bundles.\n- **No research page, blog or white paper** on wuji.tech (site navigation is Hand, Hand 2, Glove, Docs, Careers, Contact). No WUJI foundation model, benchmark or large dataset was found.\n\n## Company-authored and company-affiliated papers\n\n| Paper | Authors / organisation | Venue, year | What it contributes (one line) | Artifacts (code / weights / data links) | Tracks |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [TopoRetarget: Interaction-Preserving Retargeting for Dexterous Manipulation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) | Jielin Wu*, Shenzhe Yao*, Guanqi He*‡, Xiaohan Liu*‡, Zhaoqing Zeng, Xiangrui Jiang, Han Yang, Wentao Zhang, Hang Zhao† — IIIS, Tsinghua University (code released by Wuji Technology) | CoRL 2026 (per project page and repo BibTeX); arXiv v1 2026-06-15, v2 2026-06-22 | Converts human hand-object motion (21 keypoints + object pose) into robot-hand reference motion that keeps **which parts touch the object and how**, by solving a per-frame QP over an interaction mesh; one parameter set for all clips, no training stage, CPU only. References feed a PPO tracking policy that runs **zero-shot on the real Wuji Hand** (cube reorientation, pen spinning). | [Code (MIT)](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) · [Project page](https://toporetarget2026.github.io/TopoRetarget/) · [Raw pen-spin capture bundle](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/releases/latest/download/toporetarget-assets.zip) · [RL training + checkpoints in wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) | T02 T04 (indirect: demonstration-to-robot pipeline) |\n\n\\* equal contribution · ‡ project lead · † corresponding author.\n\n**Key numbers reported for TopoRetarget** (from the arXiv abstract, paper body and project page):\n\n| Result | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Pen-spin RL training success versus existing retargeting baselines | **+40.6 percentage points** |\n| Grasp tracking on HO-Cap (32 single-hand clips) | **84.4 %** success, **0.87 cm** position error (best of compared methods) |\n| Versus baseline average (project page) | contact-precision error **−55 %**, maximum penetration **−92 %** |\n| Retargeting-quality benchmark | ContactPose, **25 of 28** grasps (3 deeply concave objects excluded) |\n| Real hardware | zero-shot cube reorientation and pen spinning on the Wuji Hand; pen kept spinning in **5 / 5** trials |\n| Own capture data | **32** pen-spin demonstrations (mocap + Wuji Glove), average **12.4 s** |\n| Baselines compared | OmniRetarget, Mink, DexPilot, GeoRT |\n| Embodiments shown | MANO, Wuji Hand, LEAP Hand |\n| Stated limitation | fails when the human demo itself has a missing contact (finger hovers without touching) |\n\n![TopoRetarget pipeline: input, bone-direction warm-up, interaction-mesh optimisation, output](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/main/docs/images/pipeline.png)\n\n![TopoRetarget demos: pen-spin capture and GRAB, TACO, OakInk2, HOT3D clips retargeted to Wuji Hand 2](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/main/docs/images/demos.jpg)\n\n**Citable WUJI software records (no paper behind them)** — these carry a `@software` citation block in the README and are the closest thing to technical reports:\n\n| Record | Cited authors | Year | What it documents | Link | Tracks |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Wuji-MJLab: RL Training for Wuji Hand Dexterous Manipulation | Wuji Technology (9 named contributors) | 2026 | PPO in-hand **cube reorientation** (Hand 1 and Hand 2) and reference-tracking **pen spinning** (Hand 2, 20 joints at 50 Hz), with camera-in-the-loop sim-to-real deployment and ONNX export | [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) | — |\n| Wuji-IsaacLab: RL Training for Wuji Hand Dexterous Manipulation in Isaac Lab | Wuji Technology | 2026 | Same reorientation task for Hand 2 on Isaac Lab 2.3.2 / Isaac Sim 5.1 with rsl_rl PPO; exported policies run on the wuji-mjlab deployment stack | [wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) | — |\n| WujiHand Retargeting | Guanqi He, Wentao Zhang | 2026 | Hand-pose retargeting (adaptive analytical + key-vector optimisers) from Wuji Glove, Vision Pro, video, RealSense, ZED; now folded into Wuji SDK (repo archived in docs) | [wuji-retargeting](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-retargeting) | T02 T04 |\n| Wuji Hand Teleop: ROS2 Teleoperation for Dexterous Hands and Robot Arms | Guanqi He, Wentao Zhang, Liang Zhu, Duo Han, Shiquan Qiu | 2026 (BibTeX key says 2025) | Glove-driven dual-hand teleop plus arm teleop (HTC Vive Tracker or PICO 4, Tianji arms), head stereo + wrist D405 cameras, MCAP recording. Marked **not actively maintained** | [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) | T02 T04 |\n| wuji-openpi | Wuji Technology (fork of Physical Intelligence openpi) | 2026 | Fine-tuning and ROS 2 deployment of **pi0 / pi0.5** for any dual-arm + Wuji Hand layout; reference config `pi05_wuji_multi_54d` (7+7 arm, 20+20 hand = **54-dim** action) | [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | T01 T03 T04 |\n\n## Datasets, models and benchmarks released\n\n| Name | Type | Licence | Link | Useful for |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ✅ TopoRetarget solver | Code (CPU-only QP retargeting; importers for GRAB, TACO, OakInk2, HOT3D and keypoint-capture bundles) | MIT | [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) | Turning a human demo (glove or public dataset) into Wuji Hand 2 joint references in about half a minute per clip |\n| ✅ `data/pen_spin` example clip | Data: one right-hand pen-spin keypoint capture (`pen_spin_029`, 231 frames, 250 mm pen) | ships in the MIT repo | [data/README](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/blob/main/data/README.md) | Testing the retargeting pipeline with no downloads |\n| ✅ `toporetarget-assets.zip` (release v2026.10.23) | Data: raw pen-spin capture package (mocap + Wuji Glove keypoints, pen asset metadata) | not stated separately — ⚠️ unverified | [release asset](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/releases/latest/download/toporetarget-assets.zip) | Reproducing the paper's pen-spin references; template for your own capture format |\n| ✅ wuji-mjlab | Code: RL training + sim-to-real (mjlab, PPO), tasks Cube Reorient and PenSpin | Apache-2.0 | [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) | Training or replaying in-hand skills; needs NVIDIA GPU (CUDA 12.8) and pixi |\n| ✅ wuji-mjlab asset bundle v2026.10.22 | **Trained policies + data + CAD**: reorient checkpoints per hand and **five pen-spin checkpoint sets** (`model.pt`, `policy.onnx`, `config.json`), **40 pen-spin motion clips**, five recipes, cube / pen / jig CAD (STEP, 3MF) | not stated separately (repo is Apache-2.0) — ⚠️ unverified | [asset bundle](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab/releases/download/v2026.10.22/wuji-mjlab-v2026.10.22-assets.zip) | A ready-made in-hand manipulation demo without training; note it needs the camera + tag rig described in the repo |\n| ✅ wuji-isaaclab | Code: Isaac Lab task `Wuji-Hand2-Reorient-v0` | Apache-2.0 (Isaac Sim itself is proprietary) | [wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) | Teams already on Isaac Lab; no pretrained checkpoint mentioned in the README |\n| ✅ wuji-openpi | Code: pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning configs and ROS 2 deployment client; MCAP → LeRobot v2.1 data path | Apache-2.0 | [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | VLA fine-tuning on arm + Wuji Hand data. **No WUJI fine-tuned weights or demonstration dataset are published** — you start from the upstream `pi05_base` checkpoint and your own teleop data |\n| ✅ wuji-description | Robot models: URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD, STEP for Hand 1, Hand 2.1, Hand 2.2 (left / right; bare, cover, glove variants) | MIT | [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) | Simulation and planning without hardware; mechanical integration |\n| ✅ wuji-retargeting | Code + sample recordings (e.g. Vision Pro replay file) | MIT | [wuji-retargeting](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-retargeting) | Webcam / Vision Pro / glove to hand joint angles; superseded by SDK retargeting |\n| ✅ wuji-hand-teleop | Code: ROS 2 teleop + data capture (Docker only, ROS 2 Humble) | MIT (vendored XRoboToolkit parts keep their own licences) | [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) | Collecting arm + hand demonstrations as ROS 2 MCAP |\n| ✅ wuji-mujoco / mujoco-sim / isaaclab-sim | Minimal sim demos (load, control, replay a recorded trajectory) | Apache-2.0 (wuji-mujoco) | [wuji-mujoco](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mujoco) | First smoke test in simulation |\n| MoCap Pen-Spin Dataset (paper) | Dataset described in the paper: 32 demonstrations | see the two bundles above | [paper appendix A.4](https://arxiv.org/html/2606.16272v2) | Reference only; the downloadable form is the bundles above |\n| Benchmarks | none released | — | — | — |\n\nCorrection to the first-pass profile: trained RL checkpoints **are** published (inside the wuji-mjlab release bundle); what is still missing is any WUJI VLA / foundation-model checkpoint.\n\n## Third-party papers using their hardware or software\n\n**No third-party paper that uses a Wuji Hand, Wuji Glove or the WUJI software stack could be confirmed in this pass.** The search budget ran out before the hunt, and the pages that were opened (TopoRetarget reference list, upstream mjlab research page, SPIDER and dex-retargeting READMEs) name no such paper. The mjlab project lists `wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab` among community projects, which is a code listing, not a paper. Ask WUJI staff on site for customer publications.\n\nThe table below is therefore the **verified research the WUJI stack is built on or interoperates with** (opened on arXiv; none of these used Wuji hardware):\n\n| Paper | Authors / organisation | Venue, year | Hardware / software used | What it shows | Tracks |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [mjlab: A Lightweight Framework for GPU-Accelerated Robot Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22074) | Zakka, Liao, Yi, Le Lay, Sreenath, Abbeel | arXiv, 2026 | Base framework of `wuji-mjlab` (MuJoCo Warp + Isaac-Lab-style API) | How the manager-based RL environments WUJI extends are structured | — |\n| [Isaac Lab: A GPU-Accelerated Simulation Framework for Multi-Modal Robot Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.04831) | NVIDIA (Mittal et al.) | arXiv, 2025 | Base framework of `wuji-isaaclab` | Reference for the Isaac Lab task and sensor model | — |\n| [pi0: A Vision-Language-Action Flow Model for General Robot Control](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.24164) | Black et al., Physical Intelligence | RSS 2025 | Model fine-tuned by `wuji-openpi` | Flow-matching VLA with action chunks; base of the WUJI fine-tuning path | T01 T03 T04 |\n| [pi0.5: a Vision-Language-Action Model with Open-World Generalization](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054) | Physical Intelligence | arXiv, 2025 | Default model of `pi05_wuji_multi_54d` | Household tasks in unseen homes; the checkpoint WUJI's reference config starts from | T01 T04 |\n| [DexPilot: Vision Based Teleoperation of Dexterous Robotic Hand-Arm System](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.03135) | Handa et al., NVIDIA | ICRA 2020 | Credited by `wuji-retargeting`; baseline in TopoRetarget | Key-vector retargeting cost that most hand teleop still uses | T02 T04 |\n| [AnyTeleop: A General Vision-Based Dexterous Robot Arm-Hand Teleoperation System](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04577) | Qin et al., UCSD / NVIDIA | RSS 2023 | Source of `dex-retargeting`, credited by `wuji-retargeting` | Camera-only arm + hand teleop across hand models | T02 T04 |\n| [OmniRetarget: Interaction-Preserving Data Generation for Humanoid Whole-Body Loco-Manipulation and Scene Interaction](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.26633) | Yang et al. | arXiv, 2025 | Interaction-mesh idea TopoRetarget adapts to hands; baseline | Interaction-preserving retargeting at whole-body scale | — |\n| [Geometric Retargeting: A Principled, Ultrafast Neural Hand Retargeting Algorithm](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.07541) | Yin et al. | IROS 2025 | Baseline in TopoRetarget | 1 kHz learned retargeting for teleop | T02 |\n| [SPIDER: Scalable Physics-Informed Dexterous Retargeting](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09484) | Pan et al. | arXiv, 2025 | Related work cited by TopoRetarget (its repo covers Allegro, XHand, Inspire, Schunk, Sharpa — not Wuji) | Physics-based sampling to make human demos dynamically feasible | — |\n| [Lessons from Learning to Spin \"Pens\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18902) | Wang et al., UCSD / UC Berkeley | CoRL 2024 | Prior work for the pen-spin task | What makes pen spinning transfer from sim to real | — |\n| [HO-Cap: A Capture System and Dataset for 3D Reconstruction and Pose Tracking of Hand-Object Interaction](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06843) | Wang et al. | arXiv, 2024 | Evaluation data in TopoRetarget | Grasp-centric hand-object clips usable as references | T04 |\n| [ContactPose: A Dataset of Grasps with Object Contact and Hand Pose](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09545) | Brahmbhatt et al. | ECCV 2020 | Contact benchmark in TopoRetarget | Measured contact maps for functional grasps of household objects | T04 |\n| [GRAB](https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.11200) · [TACO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.08399) · [OAKINK2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19417) · [HOT3D](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09598) | Taheri et al. · Liu et al. · Zhan et al. · Banerjee et al. | ECCV 2020 · arXiv 2024 · CVPR 2024 · arXiv 2024 | Public motion sources with importers in `toporetarget` | Thousands of human hand-object clips (tools, kitchen, daily objects) you can retarget to Wuji Hand 2; each keeps its own licence (HOT3D is non-commercial) | T01 T03 T04 |\n| [DexCap: Scalable and Portable Mocap Data Collection System for Dexterous Manipulation](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07788) | Wang et al., Stanford | arXiv, 2024 | Related work cited by TopoRetarget | Glove-based in-the-wild data collection, the same idea as the Wuji Glove data loop | T02 T04 |\n\n## Reading list by track\n\nNo paper applies WUJI devices to a track task directly; the lists below are the shortest route from the confirmed research to a 48-hour build.\n\n### T01 Autonomous Urban Services\n- [pi0.5](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054) — the model `wuji-openpi` fine-tunes; read with the [wuji-openpi README](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) to judge whether a few dozen teleop demos of a service task (hand over, press, open) are feasible in the time.\n- [pi0](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.24164) — explains action chunking and why the fork adds chunk-boundary smoothing.\n- [AnyTeleop](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04577) — camera-only teleop; the fallback if no glove is free.\n- [TopoRetarget](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) — only if you plan to script a contact-rich hand skill from a recorded human demo.\n\n### T02 Resilient & Safe City\n- [DexPilot](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.03135) — the retargeting cost behind glove-to-hand teleoperation; helps when tuning pinch and thumb behaviour for valves and switches.\n- [AnyTeleop](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04577) — system design for remote arm + hand operation, including latency handling.\n- [Geometric Retargeting](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.07541) — fast learned alternative if the built-in retargeting feels wrong for a tool grasp.\n- [DexCap](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07788) — portable glove data collection, useful for logging operator demonstrations in the field.\n- [TopoRetarget](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) — contact-preserving mapping when the operator handles an object rather than free space.\n\n### T03 Sustainable City\nNo directly relevant paper found (nothing on sorting, disassembly or environmental tasks with WUJI devices). Closest useful reading:\n- [pi0](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.24164) / [pi0.5](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054) with [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) — learn a pick-and-sort skill from teleop demos instead of hand-coding grasps.\n- [TACO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.08399) and [OAKINK2](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19417) — tool-use and multi-step human clips that `toporetarget` can import, for unscrewing or dismantling motions.\n\n### T04 Elderly Care & Rehabilitation\nNo directly relevant paper found (no rehabilitation, assistive or clinical study using the Wuji Glove or Hand was confirmed). Closest useful reading:\n- [ContactPose](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09545) — reference contact maps of functional grasps; a comparison target for glove tactile maps in a grip-assessment demo.\n- [HO-Cap](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06843) and [GRAB](https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.11200) — everyday-object grasp motions (cups, bottles, utensils) to retarget for assistive fetch or feeding.\n- [TopoRetarget](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) — shows the Wuji Glove used as a capture device and the pipeline from caregiver demo to robot hand motion.\n- [pi0.5](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054) — home-task generalisation, relevant to assistive manipulation in a living space.\n- [AnyTeleop](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04577) — basis for a telepresence / remote-caregiver hand.\n\n## White papers, patents and technical reports\n\n- **Lecture notes:** [robotics-rigid-body-mechanics](https://github.com/wuji-technology/robotics-rigid-body-mechanics) — WUJI-published LaTeX notes on rotation, screw theory, dynamics and multibody systems (MIT; build the PDF yourself with XeLaTeX; includes Chinese-language packages).\n- **Algorithm notes in docs:** the archived Wuji Retargeting docs have an appendix on algorithm principles and a tuning guide; the wuji-mjlab docs have an architecture page on the reorientation MDP and contact-parameter domain randomisation ([docs index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)).\n- **White papers and patents:** none found or checked in this pass (patent databases were not searched) — not public / ⚠️ unverified.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [arXiv 2606.16272 — TopoRetarget (abstract)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) · [HTML v2 (affiliations, appendix, references)](https://arxiv.org/html/2606.16272v2)\n- [TopoRetarget project page](https://toporetarget2026.github.io/TopoRetarget/)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) · [releases](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/releases) · [data README](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/blob/main/data/README.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) · [release v2026.10.22](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab/releases/tag/v2026.10.22)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-retargeting](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-retargeting)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/wuji-mujoco](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mujoco)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology/robotics-rigid-body-mechanics](https://github.com/wuji-technology/robotics-rigid-body-mechanics)\n- [GitHub organisation: wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) (repository list and organisation profile)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt) · [Videos](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md)\n- [Wuji Technology official site](https://www.wuji.tech/en)\n- [mjlab repository](https://github.com/mujocolab/mjlab) · [mjlab research page](https://mujocolab.github.io/mjlab/main/source/research.html)\n- [SPIDER repository](https://github.com/facebookresearch/spider) · [dex-retargeting repository](https://github.com/dexsuite/dex-retargeting) (checked for Wuji support; none listed)\n- arXiv abstract pages opened for verification: [2601.22074](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22074) · [2511.04831](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.04831) · [2410.24164](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.24164) · [2504.16054](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.16054) · [1910.03135](https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.03135) · [2307.04577](https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04577) · [2509.26633](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.26633) · [2503.07541](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.07541) · [2511.09484](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09484) · [2407.18902](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18902) · [2406.06843](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.06843) · [2007.09545](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09545) · [2008.11200](https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.11200) · [2401.08399](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.08399) · [2403.19417](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19417) · [2406.09598](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09598) · [2403.07788](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07788)\n","WUJI-Products":"---\ntype: products\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, products]\n---\n# WUJI — Product Portfolio\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [Developer guide](WUJI-Developer-Guide.md) · [Roadmap and strategy](WUJI-Roadmap-and-Strategy.md)\n\n> **In 20 seconds:** WUJI sells **two 20-DoF direct-drive dexterous hands**, **one tactile + pose data glove**, and a **free unified SDK / CLI**. No arm, no wrist, no mobile base, no on-board compute: you always pair it with another vendor's arm or humanoid (or use the glove alone as a sensor).\n> **Pick quickly:** need force / compliant contact → **Wuji Hand 2** (back-drivable, MIT mode, Ethernet). Need the simplest plug-in (USB, position control, holds load unpowered-style via self-locking joints) → **Wuji Hand** gen 1. Need teleop, demonstrations or a grip-pressure sensor on a human → **Wuji Glove**.\n\n## Lineup map\n\nTrack relevance: ● strong · ◐ partial · ○ none. Status: ✅ shipping/available · 🧪 announced/preview · 🔭 roadmap/concept.\n\n| Product | Category | Status | Launched | Price (if public) | Positioning (one line) | T01 | T02 | T03 | T04 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Wuji Hand** (gen 1) | 5-finger dexterous hand | ✅ | 2025 ⚠️ unverified (docs figures dated 2025-11) | not public (reseller \"from US$5,500\" ⚠️ unverified) | 20-DoF self-locking direct-drive hand, USB, position control, strongest published load figures | ◐ | ◐ | ◐ | ◐ |\n| **Wuji Hand 2** (2.1 / 2.2 Beta) | 5-finger dexterous hand, gen 2 | 🧪 beta hardware | teased 2026-06; 2.2 Beta docs current in 2026-11 | not public (third-party US$14,600–19,500 ⚠️ unverified) | 20-DoF back-drivable hand with soft pads and MIT force-position control over Ethernet | ◐ | ● | ◐ | ● |\n| **Wuji Glove** | Tactile + pose data glove | ✅ | not public | not public | 526-point palm pressure map + 5 fingertip 6-DoF trackers for teleop and data capture | ◐ | ● | ◐ | ● |\n| **Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI** | Software (Python / C SDK, command-line tool) | ✅ free | unified SDK consolidated in 2026 | free | One API for both hands and the glove; discovery, streaming, MCAP recording, retargeting | ◐ | ◐ | ◐ | ◐ |\n| Hand 2 tactile / final version | Dexterous hand | 🔭 | no date published | not public | Implied by the docs calling 2.2 a \"non-tactile prototype\" | ○ | ○ | ○ | ○ |\n\n## Products\n\n### Wuji Hand\n\n![Wuji Hand](assets/wuji-hand.jpg)\n\nFirst-generation 20-DoF five-finger hand. Every joint has its own motor (serial direct drive, no tendon or linkage coupling) and the joints are **self-locking**, so it holds a grasp without continuous torque. Position control only.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Active DoF / joints | **20** (4 per finger), fully opposable thumb, lateral finger swing |\n| Kinematics | Serial direct-drive rotary joints, no nonlinear coupling |\n| Weight | **580 ± 10 g** (without cables) |\n| Size | 201 × 75 × 50 mm; finger length about 157 mm, thumb about 130 mm |\n| Max grasp diameter | 100 mm |\n| Fingertip force | **15 N** |\n| Static loads | single-finger hook **3 kg** · whole-hand grasp **10 kg** · whole-hand hook 10 kg · vertical grasp 5 kg · max hanging weight 5 kg |\n| Speed | open/close ≈ **0.3 s** · ≥ 2 open-close cycles per second · four-finger bend ≈ 0.25 s |\n| Precision / life | repeatability ± 1 mm · backlash ≤ ± 7 mm · idle grip life ≥ 300,000 cycles |\n| Control | Position control, FOC drives, **1000 Hz × 20 axes** |\n| Connectivity | **USB 2.0** (USB-C on the hand), proprietary protocol |\n| Power | 12–20 V DC via XT30, static 12 W; supplied adapter 12 V 20 A (420 W transient peak) |\n| Sensors | Joint state feedback; no tactile sensing documented |\n| Compute | None on board for applications — driven from your PC / robot controller |\n| Housing / protection | Aluminium alloy, **IP40** (indoor, dry) |\n\n- **Variants:** left and right hands. No EDU / developer tiers published; SDK access is the same for every unit.\n- **Typical applications:** research on dexterous manipulation, in-hand reorientation (RL), teleoperated grasping, end effector on a partner arm.\n- **Hackathon notes:** simplest wiring (one USB + one power cable). No force control and no back-drivability: be careful around people and rigid fixtures. Best when you need to **hold** heavier objects.\n- Official page: https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand · docs: [product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n\n### Wuji Hand 2\n\n![Wuji Hand 2](assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg)\n\nSecond-generation 20-DoF hand with **back-drivable** direct-drive joints, a skeleton / soft-pad / skin build, and **MIT force-position hybrid control**. Units in the field are **2.1 or 2.2 Beta**; the docs state that 2.2 is a non-tactile prototype whose parameters are not final.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs, 2.2 Beta) |\n|---|---|\n| Active DoF / joints | **20** (4 per finger), full thumb opposition, lateral abduction |\n| Kinematics | Serial direct-drive rotary joints, no nonlinear coupling |\n| Weight | **650 g** bare hand · 800 g with soft pads and cables · base 70 g extra |\n| Size | 180 × 80 × 40 mm (pose-dependent reference); fingers about 137 mm, little finger 134 mm, thumb 140 mm |\n| Min grasp diameter | 0 mm (fingertips close fully) |\n| Joint ranges (four fingers) | MCP flex −60° to 90° · MCP abd −40° to 40° · PIP −60° to 120° · DIP −60° to 90° |\n| Joint ranges (thumb) | CMC flex −68° to 74° · CMC abd −85° to 40° · MCP −60° to 90° · IP −60° to 90° |\n| Control | **MIT mode** (default: position, velocity, feed-forward effort, kp / kd per joint) or position mode (Beta); FOC; **1000 Hz × 20 axes** |\n| Connectivity | **RJ45 Ethernet, 100BASE-TX** |\n| Power | 11–13 V DC (12 V nominal) via XT30; 12 V 20 A adapter included (≥ 200 W) |\n| Sensors | Joint state and effort feedback, on-board IMU stream; **no tactile sensing** in 2.2; skin is passive |\n| Compute | None on board for applications |\n| Payload / fingertip force / IP rating | not public for Hand 2 |\n| Firmware | 2.2: v2.0.0 and later (currently **v2.5.1**) · 2.1: frozen at v1.2.4 |\n\n- **Variants:**\n  - **2.2 Beta** (serial positions 5–7 = `A01`): 11–13 V input, current firmware line, fingertip soft-pad link in the models, level-based status light.\n  - **2.1 Beta** (serial `A00`): **12 V only**, firmware frozen, some newer SDK capabilities unavailable. Check which revision you are handed before you plan features.\n  - Left and right hands. No EDU / developer tiers published.\n- **Serviceable parts:** a whole finger can be swapped with power off; soft pads and skin are replaceable. Do not run the hand without its skin.\n- **Mounting:** factory wrist flange with mounting drawings in the docs. Docs warn that the XT30 + RJ45 two-cable connector layout will change in later 2.2 releases.\n- **Typical applications:** compliant grasping and contact-rich manipulation, glove-driven teleoperation, RL sim-to-real, VLA fine-tuning on dual-arm rigs.\n- **Hackathon notes:** the right choice when contact with people or delicate objects matters (T04) or when you teleoperate tools and switches (T02). Needs a wired Ethernet port on your host and a bench supply or the 12 V adapter. Beta hardware: budget time for quirks.\n- Official page: https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2 · docs: [product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) · [version differences](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md)\n\n### Wuji Glove\n\n![Wuji Glove](assets/wuji-glove.jpg)\n\nWearable data glove that streams a palm-side pressure map, fingertip poses and wrist-back IMU data. Built for teleoperating a dexterous hand and for recording human demonstrations; also usable on its own as a hand-function sensor.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Tactile sensing | 24 × 31 matrix, **526 active points**, full palmar side, **120 FPS** |\n| Pressure range / resolution | 0–20 N, 0.1 N; spatial pitch 4 mm; repeatability ± 6 % |\n| Pose tracking | **5 EMF modules** (one per fingertip), 6 DoF each, **120 Hz**, ≤ 2 mm RMS position, < 5° RMS orientation, ≤ 10 ms latency |\n| Hand kinematics | Real-time full-hand inverse kinematics with joint angles; 6-step calibration |\n| IMU | 1 × 6-axis on the back of the hand, **800 Hz**, ± 16 g, ± 2000 °/s |\n| Weight | glove **67.5 g** · 192.6 g with cable |\n| Size | 215 × 195 mm; total length with cable 340 mm |\n| Power / data | USB Type-C 5 V / 1 A; data over **RJ45 (via adapter), 100BASE-TX** |\n| Durability | press life and flex life 100,000+ cycles each |\n| Environment | operating −5 to 40 °C, < 55 % RH |\n| Wrist / arm tracking | Not built in; mechanical mounts for an external tracker or optical markers |\n| Limits | EMF tracking is disturbed by metal / ferromagnetic objects: keep **≥ 3 cm** clearance |\n\n- **Variants:** not public (sizes and left / right availability are not listed in the pages used).\n- **Typical applications:** dexterous-hand teleoperation, tactile data collection, HCI experiments, VR / AR gesture input.\n- **Hackathon notes:** fastest path to a working demo (glove → SDK retargeting → hand). Glove-only projects are viable for T04 (grip-pressure and finger-range assessment); it is **not a medical device**. For arm teleop you must add your own wrist tracking.\n- Official page: https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove · docs: [product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n\n### Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI\n\n![Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI](assets/wuji-sdk.jpg)\n\nOne free development kit for Wuji Hand 2, Wuji Hand and Wuji Glove, plus a terminal tool for device care. Joint-level access only: there is no grasp planner or skill library.\n\n| Item | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Languages | Python and C |\n| Install | `python -m pip install wuji-sdk` (wheels for CPython 3.8–3.14); C packages from GitHub Releases |\n| Platforms | Linux x86_64 / arm64 · macOS 11+ on Apple silicon only · Windows 10 21H2+ / 11 x86_64 · C package also for Android aarch64 · Docker guide |\n| Device management | Auto-discovery on the local network, several devices in parallel |\n| Streams | Joint state / commands, effort and MIT parameters, IMU, tactile matrix, EMF poses, hand tracking; callback or async; merged cross-device subscriptions |\n| Recording | Multi-channel **MCAP** with pause / resume, episode switching, quality monitoring |\n| Retargeting | Built in (hand keypoints in, 20 joint angles out) |\n| Wuji CLI | Device scan, parameter get / set, live visualisation, stream capture, glove hand-model and tactile calibration, `wuji doctor` health check, log export, firmware upgrade |\n| Hand gen 1 | Supported by the unified SDK over USB; older `wujihandpy` package still available |\n\n- **Typical use:** every WUJI project starts here; pair with `wuji-ros2` if your arm stack is ROS 2.\n- Official page: https://docs.wuji.tech · [SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) · [install](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/quick-start.md)\n\n## Accessories and ecosystem\n\n| Item | Type | Status | What it gives you |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wrist flange + mounting drawings (Hand 2) | Mechanical | ✅ | Bolt the hand to a partner arm; adapter plates for specific arms are not listed publicly — ask WUJI staff |\n| Hand 2 base (70 g) | Mechanical | ✅ | Desk / stand mounting |\n| 12 V 20 A power adapter, original cables | Power | ✅ included | Use the supplied cables; Hand 2.1 accepts 12 V only |\n| Replaceable fingers, soft pads, skin (Hand 2) | Spares | ✅ | Field service of worn or damaged parts |\n| Glove RJ45 adapter + data acquisition board | Electronics | ✅ | Ethernet data link for the glove |\n| `wuji-ros2` | ROS 2 drivers | ✅ | Hand 2 and Glove drivers, messages, bringup (official target: Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical) |\n| `wuji-description` | Sim models | ✅ | URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD for both hand generations (rigid-body only) |\n| `wuji-mjlab` / `wuji-isaaclab` | RL | ✅ | In-hand cube reorientation training with sim-to-real path |\n| `toporetarget` | Retargeting research code | ✅ | Human hand-object motion to Wuji Hand |\n| `wuji-openpi` | VLA tooling | ✅ | pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning and ROS 2 deployment on dual-arm + Wuji Hand rigs |\n| `wuji-hand-teleop` | Teleop | ✅ (not actively maintained) | ROS 2 hand + arm teleop via HTC Vive Tracker or PICO 4 |\n\nNot offered by WUJI: arms, wrists, grippers, cameras, compute modules, batteries, WUJI-trained foundation models (none found).\n\n## Legacy and discontinued\n\n| Item | State | Replacement |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wuji Studio (desktop tool) | Archived | Wuji CLI (migration guide in the docs) |\n| `wujihandpy` (Hand gen 1 Python package) | Still available, superseded | Wuji SDK |\n| `wujihandros2` (Hand gen 1 ROS 2 driver) | Archived, usable | `wuji-ros2` covers Hand 2 and Glove |\n| Wuji Hand 2.1 Beta firmware | Frozen at v1.2.4 | Hand 2.2 Beta |\n\n## Image credits\n\n| File | Shows | Source URL |\n|---|---|---|\n| assets/wuji-hand.jpg | Wuji Hand (gen 1) product video cover | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/posters/hand_video_cover.webp |\n| assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg | Wuji Hand 2 hero image | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/p1-hero.webp |\n| assets/wuji-glove.jpg | Wuji Glove hero image | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/glove/glove-hero.webp |\n| assets/wuji-sdk.jpg | Software ecosystem illustration (Hand 2 simulation model in MuJoCo) from the Hand 2 page; stands in for the SDK, which has no product photo | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/p5-mujoco.webp |\n\nAll images © Wuji Technology, taken from the official site wuji.tech and converted to JPEG.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Wuji Hand product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2)\n- [Wuji Glove product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove)\n- [Wuji Docs](https://docs.wuji.tech) · [English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 version identification and compatibility](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK installation and environment](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/quick-start.md)\n- [WUJI profile in this pack](WUJI.md) (GitHub repo list, launch timing and unverified third-party price listings are carried over from its sources)\n","WUJI-Roadmap-and-Strategy":"---\ntype: roadmap\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, roadmap]\n---\n# WUJI — Roadmap and Strategy\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [Product portfolio](WUJI-Products.md) · [Developer guide](WUJI-Developer-Guide.md) · [Solutions and projects](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md)\n\n> **Read this first:** WUJI (舞肌科技, Wuji Tech) publishes **no dated product roadmap**. What follows is assembled from its release notes, docs warnings, GitHub READMEs and its own videos, plus Chinese trade press for funding. Funding data comes from third-party databases and press, **not** from a WUJI announcement, and the sources label the rounds differently — treat round names as ⚠️ unverified and investor names as reported.\n> **One-line strategy:** be the open, research-grade **dexterous hand + human-data** supplier for embodied-AI model builders — sell the hand, the glove and a free software stack, and let partner models (Dyna-2, RynnBrain, Natura-1, GENE-26.5, pi0.5) prove the hardware.\n\n## Company trajectory\n\n| Date | Milestone | Source type |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2018 | Founder **Pan Yunzhe (潘韫哲)** graduates from UIUC (computer science and chemistry), per IT Juzi | trade press |\n| 2019-03 | Company founded; starts with **high-torque-density micro motors**. Press and databases name the founding entity 上海舞肌科技有限公司 (Shanghai); the current site lists Shenzhen and Beijing offices and carries a Shanghai ICP filing | official (year) + press (month, entity) |\n| 2019 – about 2022 | \"F-series\" motor developed over roughly three years; press quotes **8 N·m peak torque at 200 g** | trade press ⚠️ unverified |\n| 2023-08 | Angel round (IT Juzi) | trade press ⚠️ unverified |\n| 2023-11-24 | Pre-A round — ZhenFund (真格基金), Sequoia China Seed Fund (TheRoboRadar) | database |\n| late 2023 | Full pivot from motors to dexterous hands (Chinese press summary; article itself could not be opened) | ⚠️ unverified |\n| 2025-09-17 | **Wuji Hand (gen 1) released**: 20 DoF, direct drive, USB | official video |\n| 2025-11-07 to 12-05 | Gen-1 firmware reaches full closed-loop control, then v1.0.0 with 1 kHz real-time control | official changelog |\n| 2025-11-13 | Round reported as \"Pre-A+\" (TheRoboRadar) or \"A\" (IT Juzi) — 5Y Capital (五源资本), Huafang, ZhenFund, Sequoia China | database / press |\n| 2026-02-06 | Round reported as \"A\" (TheRoboRadar) or \"A+\" (IT Juzi) — Alphaist Partners, 中移和创, Huafang Capital, 碧鸿投资 | database / press |\n| 2026-02-09 / 02-14 | Wuji Studio + Python SDK, then **Wuji Glove 1.0** | official |\n| 2026-03 to 2026-07 | \"Several A+ rounds in quick succession\" (IT Juzi); listed round on **2026-07-15**: Monolith, 尚势资本, Meituan Longzhu (美团龙珠), **Ant Group**, 德石投资 | database / press |\n| 2026-04 to 2026-05 | Partner model demos on Wuji Hand: LiberAI breakfast preparation, Genesis AI GENE-26.5 | official videos |\n| 2026-06-01 / 06-05 | **Wuji Hand 2** release film, then global debut at **ICRA 2026** (Vienna) | official videos |\n| 2026-06-10 / 06-15 | `wuji-openpi` released; TopoRetarget paper (CoRL 2026) | GitHub / arXiv |\n| 2026-07 | Software generation change: unified resource-style SDK, Hand 2 in the C SDK, retargeting moved into the SDK, firmware v2.0.0 for Hand 2.2 | release notes |\n| 2026-08 | Dyna-2 (Dyna Robotics) and RynnBrain 1.1 (Alibaba DAMO) real-robot work on Wuji hands | official videos + partner pages |\n| 2026-08-26 | Beijing News reports valuation \"risen to **RMB 5 billion**\" after several rounds in the year | single press source ⚠️ unverified |\n| 2026-09 | VLA post-training paper and report (20 / 20 on five skills); MINT open-sourced; X Square Robot's WALL-B reported as adapted to the Wuji Hand (database news item ⚠️ unverified) | arXiv / official / database |\n| 2026-10 | Natura-1 (Nature Will, ROKAE AR5 arms + Wuji hands); EgoExplorer dataset uses Wuji Glove; **IROS 2026** booth and salon (Pittsburgh); ROS 2 drivers, macOS SDK, RL checkpoint bundle | official |\n| 2026-11-10 | Hand 2 firmware **v3.0.0** with position mode (Beta); SDK and CLI on Windows; glove calibration solver 15× faster | release notes |\n| 2026-11-14 to 11-16 | On site at the Leukerbad Robotics Hackathon | event context |\n\nCadence worth noting: **26 dated software releases between 2026-02-09 and 2026-11-10** — roughly one every two weeks.\n\n## Current focus projects\n\n| Focus | What is happening now | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Wuji Hand 2 from prototype to product** | Two beta revisions in the field (2.1 frozen, 2.2 active). Docs list what is still open: thermal design, durability, joint zero accuracy, back-drive consistency, soft-pad hardness, skin design, load curves | [Hand 2 user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md) |\n| **Control maturity** | MIT mode default; whole-hand position mode added as Beta; feed-forward compensation from October 2026 units; thermal derating and current-sensing fault tolerance added in firmware | [release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| **One software stack** | Unified SDK + CLI replaces Studio, HMI, Upgrader, `wujihandpy`; now on Linux, macOS (Apple silicon), Windows, Android (C); ROS 2 Lyrical drivers; Docker recipe; AI-agent skills for the CLI | [SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) |\n| **Human-data loop** | Glove → retargeting → hand → MCAP → RL / VLA. Recent work is on data quality: EMF confidence warnings, IMU timestamp stability, guided tactile calibration, offline re-solving | [glove docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md) |\n| **Dexterous learning showcases** | Pen spinning under disturbance (RL), VLA post-training on dual Tianji arms + dual Wuji hands, TopoRetarget, MINT | [papers](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md) |\n| **Model-company partnerships** | Hands supplied to or used by Dyna Robotics, Alibaba DAMO, Nature Will, Genesis AI, LiberAI, Gento; open call for teams to co-develop real-world dexterous applications | [solutions register](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md) |\n| **Gen-1 hand in maintenance** | Docs mark gen 1 as \"kept for existing devices\"; still supported by the unified SDK | [docs home](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/index.md) |\n\n## Announced and upcoming products\n\nNo item below has a published date. \"Official\" = WUJI wrote it; \"inferred\" = follows from WUJI's wording.\n\n| Status | Item | When | Basis |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🧪 | **Wuji Hand 2.2 Beta** — current hardware, firmware v3.0.0 (2026-11-10) | shipping as beta now | official |\n| 🧪 | **Position control mode** for Hand 2 leaving Beta | no date | inferred from the \"(Beta)\" label |\n| 🔭 | **Wuji Hand 2 final / production version** — both revisions are called prototypes whose parameters \"don't represent the final product\" | no date | inferred |\n| 🔭 | **Tactile sensing on Hand 2** — 2.2 is described as a \"non-tactile prototype\" | no date | inferred |\n| 🔭 | **New external interface and supply-voltage range** for Hand 2 (no longer XT30 + RJ45 as two separate cables) | \"later versions\" | official (docs warning) |\n| 🔭 | **Product version of the hand + arm teleoperation stack**, replacing the unmaintained `wuji-hand-teleop` | \"coming soon\" | official (README) |\n| 🔭 | **VLA post-training code** (hand-action codec, DAgger takeover, residual RL) | \"when it is released\" | official (report) |\n| 🔭 | Deformable soft-pad simulation; SDK-label-to-model-actuator axis mapping; IMU-to-hand frame definition; wrist load, bending and screw specifications; electrical pin-out and power figures | \"will be added later\" | official (docs notes) |\n| 🔭 | Hand 2 unboxing and setup video | \"in production\" | official (videos page) |\n| 🔭 | More device types — the SDK is described as covering gloves, hands \"and more\" / \"other peripherals\" | no date | inferred |\n| — | Arm, wrist, humanoid, wireless glove, own foundation model | nothing announced | — |\n\nPrices are not published by WUJI. Third-party figures: gen-1 list price **¥39,800** (TheRoboRadar), reseller \"from US$5,500\" and Hand 2 listings of US$14,600–19,500 — all ⚠️ unverified.\n\n## Strategic direction and markets\n\n**Positioning**\n\n- Stated mission: give robots human-level dexterous manipulation and speed up general physical intelligence.\n- Technical bet: **fully direct-drive, 20 independent joints**, built on in-house motors, instead of tendon or linkage hands. Chinese press places WUJI among the mid-stream whole-hand makers (with Linkerbot and Sharpa) and as a representative of the direct-drive / quasi-direct-drive route; one outlet files it under core drive components because of the motor origin.\n- Hand 2's headline change is **back-drivability and compliance** (\"yield over strength\"). Press also quotes an industry practitioner saying gen 1 had heat and return-rate problems that gen 2 improved (temperatures under 50 °C) — third-party claim ⚠️ unverified.\n- Business model: hardware sales on inquiry (sales@wuji.tech) plus a free, permissively licensed software stack. No subscription, no vertical solutions, no certified products.\n\n**Customers and partners (all research / demo use, none a field deployment)**\n\n| Type | Names |\n|---|---|\n| Embodied-AI model companies | Dyna Robotics (USA), Genesis AI, LiberAI, Nature Will, X Square Robot (⚠️ unverified), Gento |\n| Corporate / institutional labs | Alibaba DAMO Academy (RynnBrain 1.1), Shanghai AI Laboratory (EgoExplorer) |\n| Universities (co-authors) | IIIS Tsinghua, ShanghaiTech, HKU, Zhejiang University |\n| Arm pairings seen in public work | Tianji 7-DoF (WUJI's own reference), ROKAE AR5 (Nature Will), YAM 6-DoF (Dyna) |\n| Distribution | Direct from Shenzhen / Beijing; US reseller Robotics Center linked from the site footer |\n\n**Funding**\n\n| Reported date | Round label (source A / source B) | Reported investors | Amount |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2023-08 | Angel (IT Juzi only) | not named | undisclosed |\n| 2023-11-24 | Pre-A | ZhenFund, Sequoia China Seed Fund | undisclosed |\n| 2025-11-13 | Pre-A+ / A | 5Y Capital, Huafang, ZhenFund, Sequoia China | undisclosed |\n| 2026-02-06 | A / A+ | Alphaist Partners, 中移和创, Huafang Capital, 碧鸿投资 | undisclosed |\n| 2026-07-15 (and others Mar–Jul) | A+ | Monolith, 尚势资本, Meituan Longzhu, Ant Group, 德石投资 | undisclosed |\n\n- Valuation: \"risen to RMB 5 billion\" in one Beijing News article (2026-08-26). No second source found.\n- Context: Chinese press describes a 2026 funding surge across the dexterous-hand sector, with WUJI named among companies closing several rounds in the first seven months.\n- No amounts, revenue, headcount or shipment figures are public. An industry list (Aibang, 2026-07-31) includes WUJI among 29 hand suppliers without a volume.\n\n**Europe and Switzerland**\n\n- **No European office, subsidiary or distributor found.** Offices listed: Shenzhen (Bao'an) and Beijing (Haidian).\n- European touchpoints on record: Hand 2's public debut at **ICRA 2026 in Vienna** (June 2026) and this hackathon in Leukerbad (November 2026). The official X handle is `@wuji_global`, and the GitHub profile advertises international hiring.\n- Docs, SDK and site are fully bilingual (English / Chinese); the US is the only market with a named reseller.\n- No CE, medical or safety certification is mentioned for any product — relevant for any European pilot.\n\n## Research and open-source activity\n\n| Area | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Papers | TopoRetarget (CoRL 2026, arXiv 2606.16272) with IIIS Tsinghua; VLA post-training (arXiv 2609.19666) with ShanghaiTech; MINT (arXiv 2609.04958) with ShanghaiTech, Tsinghua, HKU, Zhejiang | ✅ published |\n| Third-party research on WUJI hardware | EgoExplorer dataset (glove), Dyna-2, RynnBrain 1.1, Natura-1, GENE-26.5 | ✅ public |\n| Core tooling (MIT) | `wuji-sdk`, `wuji-cli`, `wuji-ros2`, `wuji-description`, `toporetarget`, `wuji-hand-teleop` | ✅ active except teleop (unmaintained) |\n| Learning stacks (Apache-2.0) | `wuji-mjlab` (with checkpoints, 40 pen-spin clips, jig CAD), `wuji-isaaclab`, `wuji-openpi` | ✅ active |\n| Data / models released | RL checkpoints; pen-spin capture bundle; MINT weights and annotations for 560,649 episodes / 1,021 h of egocentric video | ✅ |\n| Not released | WUJI VLA or foundation-model weights, teleoperation demonstration datasets, post-training code | 🔭 / not public |\n| Community | Docs with `llms.txt` and agent skills, open lecture notes on rigid-body mechanics, \"Wuji's Talk\" podcast / salon series, IROS 2026 salon | ✅ |\n\nPattern: WUJI opens the full path from **human motion to robot hand** (capture, retarget, simulate, train, deploy) and keeps the hardware and firmware closed. About 24 public repos; details and author lists are in [papers and research](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md).\n\n## What would impress this company at the hackathon\n\n**Inference, not a WUJI statement.** Derived from where WUJI spends its engineering time and what its partner videos show.\n\nGeneral signals:\n\n- **Use the 20 DoF.** A task a parallel gripper could do will not stand out. Pinch, in-hand adjustment, tool use, lids, zips, cutlery, switches do.\n- **Use compliance on Hand 2.** Tune kp / kd per finger and show safe, yielding contact — the feature gen 2 was built around.\n- **Close the data loop.** Glove teleop → MCAP recording → a learned or replayed skill is exactly WUJI's published pipeline; even a small imitation result from on-site demonstrations fits their story.\n- **Integrate with another vendor's arm cleanly.** WUJI has no arm; a reusable mount + TF + driver bridge for an arm at the venue (ROKAE, Flexiv, Dobot, Unitree, AGIBOT and others) is directly useful to them. ROKAE + Wuji already has a public precedent (Natura-1).\n- **Give feedback on the beta.** Documented bugs, a ROS 2 Humble / Jazzy bridge, a LeRobot adapter, or the missing SDK-to-model axis mapping would be contributions they can ship.\n- **Stay inside the limits.** Indoor, dry, supervised; no medical or safety claims.\n\n| Track | Idea that plays to WUJI's strengths | Why it fits |\n|---|---|---|\n| **T01 Autonomous Urban Services** (T01.3, T01.5, T01.7) | Mobile manipulator with a Wuji Hand 2 that operates human interfaces: lift buttons, door handles, card readers, handing over small items | Shows fingers doing what grippers cannot; mirrors partner demos (meal delivery, tidying) |\n| **T02 Resilient & Safe City** (T02.2, T02.7) | Glove-driven dexterous teleoperation of valves, breakers, connectors and tools from a safe distance, with recorded sessions that later seed autonomy | WUJI's own IROS booth demo was hands-on teleoperation; strongest natural fit |\n| **T03 Sustainable City** (T03.1, T03.6) | Fine disassembly or sorting step that needs dexterity (unscrewing caps, separating mixed-material items, pulling batteries), taught by demonstration | Weakest fit — only convincing if the task truly needs fingers |\n| **T04 Elderly Care & Rehabilitation** (T04.1, T04.3, T04.7) | Glove-only hand-function assessment (grip-pressure map, finger range, contact events over time), or a compliant assistive hand that opens containers and holds a cup or spoon | Uses the 526-point tactile glove without any robot, or Hand 2's back-drivability near people |\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Wuji Technology official site](https://www.wuji.tech/en) · [Purchase and Partnership](https://www.wuji.tech/en/cooperation) · [Careers (office addresses)](https://www.wuji.tech/en/careers) · [VLA post-training report](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0)\n- [Wuji Docs release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) · [docs index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt) · [docs home](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/index.md) · [videos page](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 user notice (capability boundaries)](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md) · [electrical and network integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/electrical-network-integration.md) · [control guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/control-guide.md) · [Hand 2 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) · [Wuji Glove introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- GitHub: [wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) · [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) · [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) · [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab)\n- [YouTube channel @WUJI_TECH](https://www.youtube.com/@WUJI_TECH/videos) (release, ICRA, IROS and partner videos; individual links in the [solutions register](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md))\n- arXiv: [2606.16272 TopoRetarget](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) · [2609.19666 VLA post-training](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.19666) · [2609.04958 MINT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04958) · [2610.18872 EgoExplorer](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18872)\n- Funding and company background (third party): [TheRoboRadar — WUJI TECH company profile](https://theroboradar.com/companies/wuji-tech) · [IT Juzi via Sina Tech — 2026 dexterous-hand funding review (2026-08-12)](https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-08-13/doc-inimzytm3603256.shtml) · [Beijing News — dexterous-hand funding feature (2026-08-26)](https://m.bjnews.com.cn/detail/1787753981129466.html) · [GGII via Tencent News — funding in the first seven months of 2026 (2026-08-05)](https://news.qq.com/rain/a/20260805A0ERC600)\n- Industry context (third party): [Dingjiao One via Sina Finance — \"no standard hand yet\" (2026-08-11)](https://finance.sina.com.cn/roll/2026-08-11/doc-inimwyqv4421934.shtml) · [same article on Huxiu](https://m.huxiu.com/article/4882124.html) · [Aibang Robotics — 29 dexterous-hand suppliers (2026-07-31)](https://www.aibangbots.com/a/11893)\n- Not opened (HTTP 403), cited only as the origin of the \"late-2023 pivot\" claim: [Zhihu — Ant Group and Meituan invest in Wuji Tech](https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2062483738613883285)\n- In this pack: [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [solutions and projects](WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects.md) · [papers and research](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md) (partner projects, dates of videos and unverified third-party prices are carried over from their sources)\n","WUJI-Solutions-and-Projects":"---\ntype: solutions\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, solutions]\n---\n# WUJI — Solutions and Projects Register\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](WUJI.md) · [Product portfolio](WUJI-Products.md) · [Papers and research](WUJI-Papers-and-Research.md) · [Roadmap and strategy](WUJI-Roadmap-and-Strategy.md)\n\n> **Coverage note:** Walked on 2026-11-14: the full `wuji.tech` sitemap (25 URLs: home, Hand, Hand 2, Glove, Purchase and Partnership, Careers, Contact, Terms, in English and Chinese, plus the one blog report `/blog/post-training-0`); the docs portal `docs.wuji.tech` (167-page English index, all release notes from 2026-02-09 to 2026-11-10, gen-1 changelog from 2025-11-07, videos page, archive page); all 24 public repos of the GitHub org `wuji-technology`; all 19 videos on the official YouTube channel `@WUJI_TECH` (2025-09-17 to 2026-10-29) with their descriptions; the arXiv records and partner pages those videos cite.\n> **Not accessible / not done:** the web-search tool was unavailable for this pass (session search budget exhausted), so **no news-engine sweep was run** in English or Chinese — funding rounds, Chinese trade-press coverage, China-side exhibitions, tenders and any deployment not mentioned on WUJI's own channels may be missing. LinkedIn, X (`@wuji_global`), Bilibili and Xiaohongshu were not read. The Chinese site has the same pages as the English one (no extra solution or case-study section).\n> **Key finding:** WUJI has **no Solutions / Industries / Case-studies section**. It sells three hardware products plus an open software stack, and describes them as a \"universal manipulation solution\" for research, robot integration and human-machine interaction. Nothing is marketed for delivery, inspection, rescue, waste, energy, elderly care or rehabilitation. Track tags below mark **where a building block can be applied**, not a WUJI vertical offering.\n\n## Solutions catalogue — everything they offer\n\n| # | Solution / application | What it does | Products used | Maturity | Tracks | Source link |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Wuji Hand 2** — dexterous end effector | 20-DoF back-drivable direct-drive five-finger hand with force-position (MIT) control, for mounting on a partner arm or humanoid | Hand 2 (2.1 / 2.2 Beta) | 🧪 beta hardware, sold on inquiry | T01 T02 T03 T04 | [Hand 2 page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) |\n| 2 | **Wuji Hand** (gen 1) — dexterous end effector | 20-DoF self-locking direct-drive hand, position control, USB | Hand gen 1 | ✅ shipping (docs now flagged \"kept for existing devices\") | T01 T02 T03 T04 | [Hand page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand) |\n| 3 | Tactile glove accessory for Wuji Hand gen 1 | Pressure skin worn by the gen-1 robot hand; SDK exposes attach status and tactile pressure stream | Hand gen 1 + SDK | ✅ SDK support · ⚠️ unverified as a catalogue item (no product page, no specs) | — | [Gen-1 changelog](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/release-notes.md) |\n| 4 | **Wuji Glove** — human hand capture | Wearable glove streaming palm-side pressure map, fingertip 6-DoF poses and IMU; official uses: hand teleoperation, tactile data collection, HCI experiments, VR/AR gesture input | Glove | ✅ shipping (1.0 released 2026-02-14) | T02 T04 | [Glove page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove) |\n| 5 | Precision pinch and nail action (Hand 2 capability showcase) | Thumb-to-finger pinch down to **0 mm** grasp diameter, fingernail-style prying of thin objects | Hand 2 | 🧪 | T01 T03 T04 | [Hand 2 page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) |\n| 6 | Compliant motion (Hand 2 capability showcase) | Back-drivable joints + per-joint kp / kd give soft, yielding contact instead of rigid position tracking | Hand 2 | 🧪 | T01 T04 | [Hand 2 page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) |\n| 7 | **Glove-to-hand teleoperation closed loop** (Capture → Mapping → Execution → Training) | Operator wears the glove, the hand mirrors it live; the same stream is recorded as training data | Glove + Hand / Hand 2 + SDK | ✅ official quick start (about 45 min) | T02 T04 | [Hand 2 quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/quick-start.md) |\n| 8 | **Hand + arm teleoperation stack** (`wuji-hand-teleop`) | ROS 2 package: glove drives the hands, HTC Vive Tracker or PICO 4 drives the arms, stereo video back to the headset; one-click Monitor GUI | Glove + Hand + Tianji arms (reference) | ✅ open source, **not maintained**; 🔭 \"product version coming soon\" | T01 T02 T04 | [Repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) |\n| 9 | **Hand retargeting** (built into SDK) | Converts 21 MediaPipe-format hand keypoints to 20 joint commands, so any hand tracker can drive the hand | SDK + Hand / Hand 2 | ✅ (Python and C) | T02 T04 | [Retargeting docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md) |\n| 10 | Data recording and offline processing | Multi-stream MCAP recording with separate source / receive timestamps, pause / resume, offline re-solving of glove poses | SDK + Glove / Hand 2 | ✅ | T04 | [Data recording docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md) |\n| 11 | Tactile contact detection and calibration | Guided per-glove calibration trains a contact model; outputs binary contact, per-zone pressure and a 3D tactile point cloud | Glove + SDK / CLI | ✅ | T04 | [Tactile calibration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/tactile-calibration.md) |\n| 12 | **Wuji SDK** (Python + C) | One SDK for Hand, Hand 2 and Glove: discovery, streaming, control, recording, retargeting; multi-app device sharing via SDK Bridge; usage telemetry can be switched off with `WUJI_TELEMETRY_DISABLE=1` | all | ✅ free, MIT | — (plumbing for every track) | [SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) |\n| 13 | **Wuji CLI + agent skills** | Terminal tool: scan, ping, get / set, subscribe, live Rerun viewer (`wuji viz`), health check, logs, calibration, firmware upgrade; ships installable \"skills\" so an AI coding agent can drive it | all | ✅ free | — | [CLI overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/introduction.md) |\n| 14 | ROS 2 integration (`wuji-ros2`) | Drivers, messages, launch files for Hand 2 and Glove (joint, pose, IMU, tactile, point cloud) via the ROS build farm | Hand 2, Glove | ✅ (since 2026-10-26) | — | [ROS 2 docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/ros2-integration.md) |\n| 15 | **Simulation model assets** (`wuji-description`) + sim demos | URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD and STEP for both hand generations; minimal MuJoCo and Isaac Sim loaders | none needed | ✅ | T01 T02 T03 T04 (prototype without hardware) | [Model docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/model-integration.md) |\n| 16 | Mechanical integration kit | Factory wrist flange, adapter mount (69 g), palm mounting-interface CAD and A3 drawings for fitting the hand to a partner arm | Hand 2 | ✅ | — | [Mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md) |\n| 17 | RL training and sim-to-real (`wuji-mjlab`, `wuji-isaaclab`) | PPO for in-hand cube reorientation (both generations) and reference-tracking pen spinning (Hand 2); release bundle includes jigs, 40 motion clips and **trained checkpoints** (ONNX) | Hand, Hand 2 | ✅ open source | — | [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) |\n| 18 | TopoRetarget | Turns human hand-object demonstrations into robot-hand reference motions that keep the contact pattern; CPU-only, no training | Hand, Hand 2 | ✅ open source (CoRL 2026 paper) | — | [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) |\n| 19 | **VLA fine-tuning and deployment** (`wuji-openpi`) | Fork of Physical Intelligence openpi: fine-tune pi0 / pi0.5 on any single- or dual-arm + Wuji Hand layout (reference: 54-D), with a ROS 2 deployment stack | Hand + partner arms | ✅ open source | T01 T03 T04 | [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) |\n| 20 | VLA post-training recipe (research report) | Four stages on one hand-action codec: fine-tune, human-correction (DAgger) with smooth takeover, residual RL on the real robot | 2 Tianji arms + 2 Wuji hands | 🧪 paper + report public; code \"not public yet\" | — | [Report](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0) |\n| 21 | MINT + EgoPipeline | Model that reconstructs camera and two-hand motion from first-person RGB video; output can be retargeted to the Wuji Hand; released with weights and annotations for **1,021 h** of video | none (data side) | ✅ open source (repo now under the first author's account) | — | [MINT video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JIHCCwSayGo) |\n| 22 | Purchase, partnership and distribution | Direct sales and integration partnerships (sales@wuji.tech); site footer links to US reseller Robotics Center, which lists itself as authorized distributor | all | ✅ | — | [Purchase and Partnership](https://www.wuji.tech/en/cooperation) |\n| 23 | Education and community | Open LaTeX lecture notes on rigid-body mechanics; \"Wuji's Talk\" podcast / salon series | — | ✅ | — | [Lecture notes repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/robotics-rigid-body-mechanics) |\n| 24 | Archived legacy tools | Wuji Studio (desktop app), Wuji Hand HMI, Upgrader, `wujihandpy`, `wujihandros2`, standalone `wuji-retargeting` and `mujoco-sim` / `isaaclab-sim` — all superseded by SDK + CLI | Hand gen 1, Glove | ✅ usable, no updates | — | [Archived docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/archived.md) |\n| 25 | High-torque-density motors (origin business, 2019) | The company started with motors before hands | — | not marketed on the current site | — | [Podcast description](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r86fXB8kEgw) |\n\n### Wuji Hand 2\n\n![Wuji Hand 2](assets/wuji-sol-hand2.jpg)\n\n- **20 active DoF** (4 per finger), thumb opposition, **back-drivable** direct-drive joints, **1000 Hz × 20 axes**, Ethernet (RJ45) + XT30 power, 12 V. Site lists fingertip peak force **≥ 12 N**, open / close **≥ 4 cycles/s**, joint backlash **< 1°** (Beta 1 figures, \"will continue to iterate\").\n- Default control is MIT mode (position, velocity, feed-forward effort, kp / kd per joint); whole-hand **position mode (Beta)** arrived 2026-11-10 and needs firmware v3.0.0 or later.\n- Both field revisions (2.1 and 2.2) are **non-tactile prototypes**; 2.1 is frozen on firmware v1.2.4. Built-in feed-forward compensation applies only to units shipped from October 2026 — ask WUJI staff which batch is on site.\n- Used for: any track task that needs fingers rather than a gripper (handles, switches, tools, cutlery, small parts). Indoor and dry only.\n- Official: [product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) · [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) · [version differences](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md)\n\n### Wuji Hand (gen 1)\n\n![Wuji Hand (gen 1)](assets/wuji-sol-hand1.jpg)\n\n- **20 DoF**, self-locking direct-drive joints, **580 g**, fingertip force **15 N**, static grasp load **10 kg**, single-finger hook **3 kg**, max grasp diameter **100 mm**, USB 2.0, position control, **IP40**.\n- Reliability claims on the site: survives an internal **80 cm** drop test, twist-lock finger structure releases under overload, **≥ 300,000** no-load cycles.\n- Now driven by the unified Wuji SDK (Linux only; on Windows the gen-1 functions return \"unsupported\"). Released 2025-09-17; this is the hand in most partner demos up to mid-2026.\n- Official: [product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand) · [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n\n### Wuji Glove\n\n![Wuji Glove](assets/wuji-sol-glove.jpg)\n\n- **526 pressure points** over the palm side at **120 FPS** (0–20 N, 0.1 N steps, 4 mm pitch), **5 fingertip EMF trackers** (≤ 2 mm RMS, ≤ 10 ms latency), wrist IMU at **800 Hz**; glove weighs **67.5 g**, tethered (USB-C power, RJ45 data).\n- Works **without any robot**: grip-pressure maps, finger joint angles, 21-keypoint skeleton and contact events are available live or recorded. This is the fastest WUJI route into T04 hand-function assessment or exercise feedback (it is not a medical device).\n- Limits: EMF tracking degrades within 3 cm of metal; operating humidity < 55 % RH; one glove size listed (215 × 195 mm).\n- Used outside WUJI by the EgoExplorer dataset team (Shanghai AI Laboratory and others) for finger motion and regional touch.\n- Official: [product page](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove) · [docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n\n### Precision pinch and nail action (Hand 2 capability showcase)\n\n![Precision pinch and nail action](assets/wuji-sol-pinch.jpg)\n\n- Marketed capability: thumb pad against any fingertip with a minimum grasp diameter of **0 mm**, plus rigid \"nails\" for getting under thin edges.\n- Relevance: holding cutlery, pills, cards, zips, small waste fractions. SDK retargeting was tuned in 2026-08 for better thumb-to-fingertip contact, and a firmware fix removed false over-current stops during pinching.\n- Official: [Hand 2 page, Capabilities Showcase](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2)\n\n### Compliant motion (Hand 2 capability showcase)\n\n![Compliant motion](assets/wuji-sol-compliant.jpg)\n\n- Back-drivable joints with soft finger pads; stiffness and damping set per joint (defaults kp = 5.0, kd = 0.1 on new units).\n- Relevance: contact with people or fragile objects is yielding rather than rigid. There is **no certified safety function** — thermal derating, over-current stop and software limits are device protection only.\n- Official: [control guide](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/control-guide.md)\n\n### Glove-to-hand teleoperation closed loop\n\n![Glove-to-hand teleoperation closed loop](assets/wuji-sol-teleop-loop.jpg)\n\n- Four steps as WUJI presents them: **Capture** (glove) → **Mapping** (retargeting) → **Execution** (hand) → **Training** (recorded data feeds RL / VLA).\n- The SDK ships a live example (`examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py`); official estimate is about **45 minutes** from unboxing to a mirrored hand.\n- Who uses it: every dexterous-data pipeline WUJI publishes starts here (wuji-openpi, the VLA post-training report). For the hackathon it is the base of any \"human stays outside the hazard\" or remote-caregiver demo.\n- Official: [cross-product teleoperation](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/quick-start.md)\n\n### Hand + arm teleoperation stack (wuji-hand-teleop)\n\n![Hand + arm teleoperation stack](assets/wuji-sol-teleop-arm.jpg)\n\n- Docker-based ROS 2 workspace: Wuji Glove → retarget + IK → left / right hand (about 120 Hz joint targets); arm pose from **HTC Vive Trackers** or a **PICO 4** headset; stereo camera stream to the headset; MANUS gloves supported by the community only.\n- Reference arms are **Tianji 7-DoF**; other arms plug in through the documented wrist-pose topics, which is the integration path for the arms at Leukerbad.\n- Status: README says **not actively maintained, no support**, \"product version coming soon\". Records ROS 2 MCAP that `wuji-openpi` converts to LeRobot format.\n- Official: [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop)\n\n### Hand retargeting\n\n![Hand retargeting](assets/wuji-sol-retarget.jpg)\n\n- Input: 21 hand keypoints in MediaPipe order. Output: 20 joint angles in firmware order, ready to send. One line builds a session for Hand or Hand 2, left or right.\n- Input sources documented across SDK and the archived repo: Wuji Glove (recommended), webcam + MediaPipe, Apple Vision Pro, video files, Intel RealSense, ZED, MANUS-style pipelines.\n- No glove on your team? A laptop camera is enough to drive the hand.\n- Official: [retargeting docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md) · [session example](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/sdk-practice/retarget-session.md)\n\n### Data recording and offline processing\n\n- MCAP recording from Python and C, episode pause / resume that waits for the state change, separate source-event and host-receive timestamps for cross-device alignment.\n- Offline pipeline recomputes joint angles, fingertip poses, skeleton and fused IMU from recorded raw glove data without a device attached.\n- Relevance: session logs for rehab or assessment prototypes, and demonstration datasets for any learned skill.\n- Official: [SDK data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md) · [glove offline solving](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/offline-pipeline.md)\n\n### Tactile contact detection and calibration\n\n- `wuji calib tactile` (or `glove.calibrate_tactile()`): prompted hand motions train a per-glove contact model, then the `tactile_binary` stream reports contact in real time; sensitivity adjustable 0.5–3.0.\n- Also available: per-zone pressure (palm and each finger) and a 3D tactile point cloud for visualisation.\n- Relevance: \"is the person actually gripping / touching\" events without writing signal processing.\n- Official: [tactile calibration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-cli/latest/tactile-calibration.md) · [tactile data reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/tactile.md)\n\n### Simulation model assets\n\n![Simulation model assets](assets/wuji-sol-sim.jpg)\n\n- `wuji-description` carries URDF, MJCF, MJX, USD and STEP for Hand gen 1, Hand 2.1 and Hand 2.2 (2.2 adds a soft-pad link per fingertip; rigid-body only, no deformable simulation yet). Models are rooted at the arm-flange mount.\n- A model loads in MuJoCo with one command and no hardware, so a team can develop while the real hand is shared.\n- Official: [model assets and loading](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/model-integration.md) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description)\n\n### VLA fine-tuning and deployment (wuji-openpi)\n\n- Pipeline: teleoperation capture (ROS 2 MCAP) → LeRobot v2.1 conversion → supervised fine-tuning of pi0 / pi0.5 → policy server → closed-loop ROS 2 deployment. Arm count and DoF are config values, not hard-coded.\n- Needs an NVIDIA GPU (CUDA 12) and a few hundred demonstrations; WUJI's own report used **200 demonstrations** per skill. Not a 48-hour path unless you start from an existing dataset.\n- Official: [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n\n### TopoRetarget (no track tag, picture for reference)\n\n![TopoRetarget](assets/wuji-sol-toporetarget.jpg)\n\n- Retargets recorded human hand-object motion (own pen-spin capture, GRAB, TACO, OakInk2, HOT3D clips) to the Wuji Hand while preserving which keypoints touch the object; reported **+40.6 percentage points** pen-spin training success and zero-shot transfer to hardware.\n- Official: [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) · [project page](https://toporetarget2026.github.io/TopoRetarget/)\n\n## Projects register — past and current\n\n| Date | Project / deployment / pilot / partnership | Partner or customer | Location | What happened (one line) | Tracks | Source link |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-11-10 | Docs / SDK release | — | — | CLI and SDK on Windows and Apple silicon; Hand 2 position mode (Beta); glove calibration solver 15× faster | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-10-29 | Pen spinning under disturbances (demo) | — | — | Video of an RL policy spinning a pen on Hand 2 while being pushed | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W8yfvxsaZRs) |\n| 2026-10-26 | ROS 2 drivers + fault logs release | — | — | `wuji-ros2` drivers for Hand 2 and Glove; SDK on macOS; C-side MCAP recording | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-10-22 | `wuji-mjlab` v2026.10.22 | — | — | Asset bundle with jigs, 40 pen-spin clips, five recipes and matched checkpoints | — | [Repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) |\n| 2026-10-19 | **IROS 2026 booth + salon \"Toward an Embodied Future\"** | — | Pittsburgh, USA | Hand 2 and Glove manipulation demos, hands-on teleoperation for visitors, a talk session for researchers | T02 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3uO7-6idn8o) |\n| 2026-10-15 | **EgoExplorer dataset** uses Wuji Glove | Shanghai AI Laboratory and collaborating institutions | China | 100-hour wearable vision-motion-touch dataset; glove records finger motion and regional touch | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fc9syM7nwq8) · [arXiv 2610.18872](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18872) |\n| 2026-10-14 | **Natura-1** foundation model on Wuji hands | Nature Will | not stated | WUJI supplied hands for training and task deployment; Nature Will's dual-arm rig is **ROKAE AR5 arms + Wuji hands** | T01 T04 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xadNfiDMOs4) · [Natura-1 post](https://www.naturewill.com/blog/natura-1) |\n| 2026-10-12 | Description packages reorganised | — | — | Separate Hand 2.1 and Hand 2.2 ROS 2 model packages; SDK supports Ubuntu 20.04+ and Python 3.8+ | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-09-26 | **WUJI × Gento** | Gento (robot maker; details not verified) | not stated | \"Gento Luna\" robot uses WUJI hands to handle bottles, stack blocks and put toys away | T01 T04 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K6txrShpl_A) |\n| 2026-09-22 | SDK / firmware release | — | — | Feed-forward compensation (units shipped from Oct 2026), multi-app device sharing, glove live view in CLI | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-09-17 | **VLA post-training paper and report** | ShanghaiTech University (co-authors) | China | Five marker skills (pick up, hand-to-hand transfer, in-hand rotation, uncap, write \"WUJI\") each reach **20 / 20** trials on 2 Tianji arms + 2 Wuji hands | — | [arXiv 2609.19666](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.19666) · [Report](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0) |\n| 2026-09-08 | Documentary \"From Motor to Dexterous Hand — WUJI's Seven-Year Journey\" | Alphaist Partners (production) | — | Company history film: single motor in 2019 to direct-drive hands on the ICRA floor | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PFOwvftdg4A) |\n| 2026-09-07 | **MINT open-sourced** | ShanghaiTech, Tsinghua, HKU, Zhejiang University (co-authors) | — | Model, code, EgoPipeline reference and annotations for **560,649 episodes / 1,021 h** of egocentric video; hand motion retargets to Wuji Hand | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JIHCCwSayGo) · [arXiv 2609.04958](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04958) |\n| 2026-08-12 | **Dyna-2** real-robot tasks on Wuji hands | Dyna Robotics | USA | Two of Dyna-2's evaluation tasks run on 6-DoF YAM arms fitted with a pair of \"WUJI-2\" 20-DoF hands | T01 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Cu95eXorU0) · [Dyna-2 page](https://www.dyna.co/dyna-2) |\n| 2026-08-03 to 08-31 | SDK / CLI releases | — | — | Guided tactile calibration, `wuji logs`, `wuji viz` for Hand 2, Beta 2 sim models with soft pads, palm-mount CAD | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-08-02 | **RynnBrain 1.1** real-robot evaluation | Alibaba DAMO Academy | China | \"Tianji-Wuji\" dexterous system used for long tasks: steak cooking, plating, meal delivery, pouring | T01 T04 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WoyZ662JQSc) · [RynnBrain page](https://alibaba-damo-academy.github.io/RynnBrain/) |\n| 2026-07-01 to 07-23 | Hand 2 software generation change | — | — | Resource-style API, Hand 2 in the C SDK, retargeting moved into the SDK, firmware v2.0.0 for Beta 2 hardware, Hand 2 (Beta 1) sim models | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-06-30 | Glove calibration tutorial | — | — | Official video for hand-model calibration with the CLI | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LdbhNvbI9Ig) |\n| 2026-06-15 | **TopoRetarget** paper + code (CoRL 2026) | IIIS, Tsinghua University (co-authors) | China | Interaction-preserving retargeting; policies transfer zero-shot to Wuji Hand for cube reorientation and pen spinning | — | [arXiv 2606.16272](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) |\n| 2026-06-10 | `wuji-openpi` released | builds on Physical Intelligence openpi | — | pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning and ROS 2 deployment for dual-arm + Wuji Hand rigs | T01 T03 T04 | [Repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) |\n| 2026-06-05 | **Wuji Hand 2 global debut at ICRA 2026** | — | Vienna, Austria (ICRA 2026 venue; city not named in WUJI's video) | First public showing: 20 DoF, back-drivable actuation, improved thermal design | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OiG3kM18tls) |\n| 2026-06-01 | Wuji Hand 2 release film | — | — | \"Yield over Strength, Stand over Time\"; teaser had run on 2026-05-10 (\"after 8 months, fully upgraded\") | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7QYedp3ozjw) |\n| 2026-05-06 | **GENE-26.5** manipulation model on Wuji Hand | Genesis AI (WUJI calls it a partner) | not stated | Partner's manipulation model announced as running on the Wuji Hand | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=44yS6YRrA4I) |\n| 2026-04-16 | **Breakfast-preparation demo** on Wuji Hand | LiberAI (WUJI calls it a partner) | not stated | Partner's first dexterous manipulation model shown preparing breakfast | T01 T04 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RoApCJ25BGY) |\n| 2026-02-15 | Podcast \"The Dexterous Hand Solution\" | Alphaist Partners (hard-tech venture fund; investor status not stated) | — | **Founder and CEO Yunzhe Pan** on the direct-drive choice and sim-to-real; confirms 2019 start with motors | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r86fXB8kEgw) |\n| 2026-02-14 | **Wuji Glove 1.0 release** | — | — | First data-capture glove; Wuji Studio and the Python SDK had shipped on 2026-02-09 | T02 T04 | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NE5FytzRz_E) |\n| 2025-11-07 to 2026-02-02 | Gen-1 hand firmware / SDK line | — | — | Full closed-loop control (2025-11-07), firmware v1.0.0 with 1 kHz real-time control (2025-12-05), six further updates | — | [Gen-1 changelog](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/release-notes.md) |\n| 2025-09-17 | **Wuji Hand official release** | — | — | First-generation 20-DoF hand launched (most-viewed video on the channel) | — | [Video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LXVV-oErD8s) |\n| undated | US distribution | Robotics Center (San Francisco; East Coast site in Allston, MA) | USA | Linked from the WUJI site footer; reseller states it is an authorized distributor. Its spec text partly conflicts with WUJI's docs — use WUJI's numbers | — | [Reseller page](https://www.roboticscenter.ai/store/product/wuji-hand) |\n| 2019 | Company founded | — | Shenzhen, China | Started with high-torque-density motors, then hands and data-capture devices | — | [Podcast description](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r86fXB8kEgw) |\n\nNot found on any WUJI channel: named paying customers, shipment numbers, government programmes, joint labs, competitions, or any deployment in Europe or Switzerland. All partner entries above are **research or demo use of WUJI hardware by AI-model companies and labs**, not field deployments.\n\n## Future projects and announced plans\n\n| Announced | Planned for | What | Confidence | Tracks | Source link |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06 (README) | \"coming soon\", no date | **Product version of the hand + arm teleoperation stack**, replacing the unmaintained `wuji-hand-teleop` | official | T02 T04 | [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) |\n| 2026-10 (docs) | no date | **Final Wuji Hand 2 with tactile sensing** — both current revisions are labelled \"non-tactile prototype\", parameters \"don't represent the final product\" | inferred | T01 T02 T03 T04 | [Hand 2 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) |\n| 2026-09 (report) | \"when it is released\" | **Code for the VLA post-training pipeline** (codec, DAgger takeover, residual RL); link placeholder says not public yet | official | — | [Report](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0) |\n| 2026-11 (docs) | \"in production\" | Wuji Hand 2 unboxing and setup video guide | official | — | [Videos page](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md) |\n| 2026-11-10 | no date | Hand 2 **position control mode** leaves Beta | inferred | — | [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) |\n| 2026-10 (docs) | no date | **Deformable soft-pad simulation** for Hand 2 (\"isn't supported yet\") | inferred | — | [Hand 2 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) |\n| 2026-09 (report) | open research | Long-horizon skill composition, new objects and scenes for dexterous VLA policies (current results are about 30-second atomic skills) | official (stated as open work) | T01 T04 | [Report](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0) |\n| 2026 (docs index) | ongoing | Gen-1 Wuji Hand phased into maintenance: docs marked \"kept for existing devices\"; Hand 2 is the lead product | inferred | — | [Docs home](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/index.md) |\n| 2026 (GitHub) | no date | More device types: the SDK is described as covering \"Wuji Glove, Wuji Hand, Wuji Hand 2, and others\" | inferred | — | [GitHub org](https://github.com/wuji-technology) |\n| 2026 (GitHub profile, videos) | ongoing | International hiring and an open call for robotics teams to co-develop real-world dexterous applications | official | — | [WUJI × Gento video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K6txrShpl_A) |\n\nNo dated roadmap, price list, funding plan or new-product announcement (arm, wrist, humanoid, wireless glove) was found. ⚠️ unverified beyond WUJI's own channels because the news search could not be run.\n\n## Solutions by track — quick index\n\n### T01 Autonomous Urban Services\n- **Wuji Hand 2 / Wuji Hand as the end effector** of another vendor's mobile manipulator: door handles, lift buttons, bottles, cutlery, table service (solutions 1, 2, 5, 6).\n- **Partner precedents for service tasks:** RynnBrain 1.1 meal delivery and steak cooking (Tianji arms + Wuji hands), LiberAI breakfast preparation, Gento Luna tidying bottles and toys, Dyna-2 tasks, Natura-1 on **ROKAE AR5 + Wuji hands**.\n- **wuji-openpi** for a learned skill if you can collect demonstrations (solution 19); **hand + arm teleop stack** as the demonstration source or as a remote-operated concierge fallback (solution 8).\n- **Simulation assets** to build before hardware access (solution 15).\n\n### T02 Resilient & Safe City\n- **Glove-to-hand teleoperation closed loop** — operator outside the hazard, dexterous hand inside (solution 7). This is the strongest WUJI fit for the track.\n- **Hand + arm teleoperation stack** with headset video (solution 8); **retargeting** from a webcam or VR headset when no glove is free (solution 9).\n- **Wuji Glove** as the operator input device (solution 4); **Hand 2 / Hand** for valves, switches, connectors and tools (solutions 1, 2).\n- Precedent: hands-on teleoperation was WUJI's own IROS 2026 booth demo. Nothing found for search and rescue, inspection, patrol or mapping.\n\n### T03 Sustainable City\n- Nothing specific found. WUJI markets no sorting, recycling, energy, charging, environmental or agriculture application.\n- Closest reusable pieces: **Hand 2 precision pinch** for small or awkward items and disassembly steps (solutions 1, 5), **wuji-openpi** for a learned sort-by-demonstration skill (solution 19), **simulation assets** (solution 15).\n\n### T04 Elderly Care & Rehabilitation\n- **Wuji Glove alone** for hand-function measurement: 526-point grip-pressure map, finger angles, contact events, recorded sessions (solutions 4, 10, 11). No robot needed; not a medical device.\n- **Compliant, back-drivable Hand 2** for assistive manipulation near a person: fetching, holding a spoon or cup, opening containers (solutions 1, 5, 6).\n- **Glove-to-hand teleoperation and retargeting** for remote caregiver help or mirror-style therapy concepts (solutions 7, 9); **hand + arm teleop stack** for telepresence (solution 8).\n- Partner precedents in household tasks: breakfast preparation (LiberAI), meal delivery and pouring (RynnBrain 1.1), putting toys and bottles away (Gento Luna).\n- Nothing found for fall detection, massage, exoskeleton, prosthetic or EMG products.\n\n## What they do NOT offer\n\n- **No complete robot:** no arm, wrist actuator, mobile base or humanoid. Every manipulation demo needs another vendor's arm plus your own mounting and integration time.\n- **No vertical solutions or case studies** for any of the four tracks; no field deployments, only research and demo use.\n- **No high-level skills:** no grasp planner, no perception, no task library. Control is joint-level; you write the grasps or teleoperate.\n- **No general foundation model.** Published weights are narrow: RL checkpoints for cube reorientation and pen spinning (`wuji-mjlab` bundle) and the MINT video-to-hand-motion model.\n- **No tactile sensing on Hand 2** today (beta prototypes are non-tactile); touch data comes only from the human-worn glove, or the gen-1 tactile accessory (availability unverified).\n- **No outdoor or wet use:** gen-1 hand is IP40; glove needs < 55 % RH and no metal within 3 cm; glove and hands are tethered.\n- **No certified safety or medical function:** no safety-rated stop, no medical-device status for the glove.\n- **No EMG, exoskeleton, prosthetic, haptic-feedback or wireless product.** The glove senses only; it does not push back on the wearer.\n- **No Europe-based office or distributor found;** sales are direct from Shenzhen / Beijing or through a US reseller.\n\n## Image credits\n\n| File | Shows | Source URL |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assets/wuji-sol-hand2.jpg` | Wuji Hand 2 release-film poster | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/hand2-trailer-poster-en.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-hand1.jpg` | Wuji Hand (gen 1) on its stand, video cover | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/posters/hand_video_cover.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-glove.jpg` | Wuji Glove hero image | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/glove/glove-hero.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-pinch.jpg` | Hand 2 pinching a spoon handle (\"Precision Pinch\") | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/p3-pinch.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-compliant.jpg` | Hand 2 with soft cover lifting a thin sheet (\"Compliant Motion\") | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/p3-compliant.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-teleop-loop.jpg` | Wuji Glove with forearm acquisition board, from the \"Glove closed-loop flow\" section | https://www.wuji.tech/assets/images/hand2/p5-glove.webp |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-teleop-arm.jpg` | Dataflow diagram of the hand + arm teleoperation stack | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop/main/docs/images/dataflow.png |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-retarget.jpg` | \"Retargeting & Teleoperation\" demo cover (hand and glove drawing) | https://docs.wuji.tech/shared/assets/videos/cover-vid-retarget-live.png |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-sim.jpg` | MuJoCo simulation demo cover | https://docs.wuji.tech/shared/assets/videos/cover-vid-mujoco-live.png |\n| `assets/wuji-sol-toporetarget.jpg` | TopoRetarget results on six clips (pen spin, GRAB, TACO, OakInk2, HOT3D) | https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget/main/docs/images/demos.jpg |\n\nAll images © Wuji Technology (official site, docs CDN or the company's GitHub repos). The TopoRetarget panel renders third-party dataset clips that stay under their own licences.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Wuji Technology site map](https://www.wuji.tech/sitemap.xml) · [home](https://www.wuji.tech/en) · [Hand](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand) · [Hand 2](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) · [Glove](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove) · [Purchase and Partnership](https://www.wuji.tech/en/cooperation) · [Careers](https://www.wuji.tech/en/careers) · [Chinese home](https://www.wuji.tech/zh)\n- [WUJI research report: Towards High-DoF Dexterous Manipulation through VLA Post-Training](https://www.wuji.tech/blog/post-training-0)\n- [Wuji Docs English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt) · [docs home](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/index.md) · [release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) · [videos](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md) · [archived](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/archived.md)\n- [Hand 2 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) · [Hand 2 version compatibility](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md) · [Hand 2 quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/quick-start.md) · [Hand 2.1 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/beta1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand gen-1 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md) · [gen-1 changelog](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/release-notes.md)\n- [Wuji Glove introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [GitHub org wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) · [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [wuji-cli](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-cli) · [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) · [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) · [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) · [wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) · [wuji-mujoco](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mujoco) · [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) · [wuji-retargeting](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-retargeting) · [robotics-rigid-body-mechanics](https://github.com/wuji-technology/robotics-rigid-body-mechanics)\n- [MINT repository (redirects from the WUJI org to the first author's account)](https://github.com/ZZJ-Asher/wuji-ego-mint)\n- [YouTube channel @WUJI_TECH](https://www.youtube.com/@WUJI_TECH/videos) — individual videos linked in the tables above\n- [arXiv 2609.19666 — VLA post-training](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.19666) · [arXiv 2606.16272 — TopoRetarget](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.16272) · [arXiv 2609.04958 — MINT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04958) · [arXiv 2610.18872 — EgoExplorer](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18872)\n- [TopoRetarget project page](https://toporetarget2026.github.io/TopoRetarget/)\n- Partner pages: [Dyna-2 (Dyna Robotics)](https://www.dyna.co/dyna-2) · [RynnBrain 1.1 (Alibaba DAMO Academy)](https://alibaba-damo-academy.github.io/RynnBrain/) · [Natura-1 (Nature Will)](https://www.naturewill.com/blog/natura-1)\n- Third party, not official: [Robotics Center — Wuji Hand listing](https://www.roboticscenter.ai/store/product/wuji-hand) · [humanoid.guide — Wuji Hand 2](https://humanoid.guide/welcome-wuji-hand-2/) · [RuntimeWire — Hand 2 teaser (2026-06-05)](https://runtimewire.com/article/wuji-tech-hand-2-robotic-hand-teaser)\n","WUJI":"---\ntype: company\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nhq: \"Shenzhen, China\"\nfounded: 2019\nwebsite: https://www.wuji.tech\ncategories: [dexterous-hand, data, components]\non_site_guess: \"Wuji Hand / Wuji Hand 2 (20-DoF direct-drive hands) on a demo stand or partner arm, plus Wuji Glove for teleoperation\"\nfit_t01: 2\nfit_t02: 3\nfit_t03: 2\nfit_t04: 3\nidentity_confidence: high\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, company]\n---\n# WUJI\n\n> **One-liner:** Wuji Technology (舞肌科技, Shenzhen) builds 20-DoF fully direct-drive dexterous robot hands and a tactile data glove, with an unusually open SDK / sim / RL / VLA software stack.\n> **Why it matters at Leukerbad:** It is the only pure dexterous-hand vendor on site: an end effector you bolt onto someone else's arm or humanoid, and a glove that gives you teleoperation and demonstration data in hours. It is not a complete robot, so every WUJI project is a multi-vendor project (or a glove-only sensing project).\n\n## Snapshot\n\n| Item | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| HQ | Shenzhen, Guangdong, China (COFCO Chuangxin R&D Center, Bao'an District); second office in Haidian, Beijing |\n| Legal name | 深圳舞肌科技有限公司 (Shenzhen Wuji Technology Co., Ltd.) |\n| Founded | **2019** (company statement: started with high-torque-density motors, then hands and data-capture devices) |\n| Founders / CEO | not public on the official site. One third-party page says the company grew out of motor maker Pan Motor — ⚠️ unverified |\n| Size and funding | not public (no funding round found in this research) |\n| Core business | Dexterous hands (Wuji Hand, Wuji Hand 2), data glove (Wuji Glove), SDK / CLI, open-source sim, RL and VLA tooling |\n| Website | https://www.wuji.tech (wuji.tech) · sales@wuji.tech · support@wuji.tech |\n| Docs / developer portal | https://docs.wuji.tech (English + Chinese, about 167 English pages, has `llms.txt`) |\n| GitHub | https://github.com/wuji-technology (24 public repos, mostly MIT / Apache-2.0, pushed as recently as 2026-11-10) |\n\n## Portfolio at a glance\n\n| Product | Type | Status | Key specs (verified from official docs) | Price | Img key |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Wuji Hand** (gen 1) | 5-finger dexterous hand | ✅ shipping | **20 active DoF** (4 per finger), serial direct-drive joints, self-locking · **580 ± 10 g** · 201 × 75 × 50 mm · fingertip force **15 N** · whole-hand static grasp load **10 kg** · open/close ≈ 0.3 s · **1000 Hz × 20 axes**, position control · **USB 2.0** · 12–20 V DC · IP40 · idle grip life ≥ 300,000 cycles | Official price not public. Reseller listing \"from US$5,500\" — ⚠️ unverified | wuji-hand |\n| **Wuji Hand 2** (2.1 / 2.2 Beta) | 5-finger dexterous hand, 2nd gen | 🧪 beta hardware in the field (docs call 2.2 a \"non-tactile prototype\", specs not final) | **20 active DoF**, **back-drivable** direct-drive joints, thumb opposition · **650 g** bare (800 g with pads and cables) · 180 × 80 × 40 mm · **MIT force-position hybrid control** (default) + position mode (Beta) · **1000 Hz × 20 axes** · **RJ45 Ethernet 100BASE-TX** + XT30 power · 11–13 V DC, 12 V 20 A adapter · on-board IMU stream · firmware v2.5.1 | Official price not public. Third-party listings US$14,600–19,500 — ⚠️ unverified | wuji-hand-2 |\n| **Wuji Glove** | Tactile + pose data glove | ✅ shipping | **526 tactile points** (24 × 31 matrix, full palmar side) at **120 FPS**, 0–20 N, 0.1 N resolution, 4 mm pitch · **5 EMF 6-DoF fingertip trackers** at 120 Hz, ≤ 2 mm RMS, ≤ 10 ms latency · 6-axis IMU at 800 Hz · glove **67.5 g** · USB-C power, RJ45 data via adapter · −5 to 40 °C | not public | wuji-glove |\n| **Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI** | Software (Python / C SDK, command-line tool) | ✅ available, free | One SDK for Hand, Hand 2 and Glove · `pip install wuji-sdk` (CPython 3.8–3.14) · Linux x86_64 / arm64, macOS Apple silicon, Windows · MCAP recording · built-in retargeting · C packages incl. Android aarch64 | free (MIT repo) | wuji-sdk |\n\nNot found: any WUJI arm, wrist or humanoid product. Hand 2 tactile version is implied by the \"non-tactile prototype\" wording but no date is published (🔭).\n\n## What they will most likely bring to the hackathon\n\n**Best guess (not confirmed by the organisers or WUJI):**\n\n- **Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) and/or Wuji Hand gen 1**, left and right, on a desk stand or with wrist flange adapters. Reasoning: these are the only two hardware hand lines; the docs, firmware and ROS 2 packages were all updated in Oct–Nov 2026, so Hand 2 is the product they want developers on.\n- **Wuji Glove pairs** for live teleoperation. Reasoning: the official \"cross-product teleoperation\" quick start is glove to hand, and it is the fastest demo to get working.\n- **No arm of their own.** Expect to mount the hand on another vendor's arm or humanoid (Flexiv, ROKAE, Dobot, Unitree, AGIBOT and others on site). Ask WUJI staff on day 1 which flange adapters they brought; the Hand 2 docs include wrist flange drawings.\n- Quantity is unknown; hands are costly and fragile (IP40), so plan for **shared or supervised access**.\n\n## Developer platform (summary)\n\n- **Wuji SDK** (unified, Python + C): auto-discovery on the local network, multi-device connect, callback and async subscriptions, device parameters. Docs: https://docs.wuji.tech · repo: https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk\n- **Control level:** joint-level only. Hand 2 = MIT mode (position, velocity, feed-forward effort, kp / kd per joint) or position mode (Beta); Hand gen 1 = position control. **No built-in grasp planner or high-level skills** — you write those.\n- **Platforms:** Linux x86_64 / arm64, macOS (Apple silicon), Windows 10 / 11; Docker deployment guide; Hand 2 and Glove connect over Ethernet (RJ45), Hand gen 1 over USB.\n- **ROS 2:** `wuji-ros2` (drivers for Hand 2 and Glove, messages, bringup; distributed via the ROS build farm). Official install targets **Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical** — check your laptop / use Docker. Older `wujihandros2` (Hand gen 1, 1000 Hz joint states, RViz) is archived but usable; repo lists Humble and Kilted.\n- **Simulation assets:** `wuji-description` with **URDF, MJCF, MJX and USD** for both hand generations; load in MuJoCo and Isaac Sim without hardware. Rigid-body only (no soft-pad deformation).\n- **Teleoperation and retargeting:** retargeting is built into the SDK (21 MediaPipe-format keypoints in, 20 joint angles out) — so a webcam + MediaPipe, Vision Pro, VR headset or the Wuji Glove can all drive the hand. `wuji-hand-teleop` adds ROS 2 hand + arm teleop (HTC Vive Tracker and PICO 4 paths; not actively maintained).\n- **Data collection:** SDK records multi-channel streams to **MCAP** with episode switching and quality monitoring; glove gives tactile + pose + IMU.\n- **Learning stacks (open source):** `wuji-mjlab` (PPO in-hand cube reorientation with sim-to-real bridge, ONNX export), `wuji-isaaclab` (same task for Hand 2), `toporetarget` (human hand-object motion to Wuji Hand, arXiv 2606.16272), `wuji-openpi` (fork of Physical Intelligence openpi for fine-tuning and ROS 2 deployment of **pi0 / pi0.5** on dual-arm + Wuji Hand setups).\n- **Pretrained models / on-board compute:** no WUJI foundation model or published checkpoints found (not public). No on-board application compute; the hand is driven from your PC or a Jetson-class host (WUJI benchmarks glove calibration on Jetson AGX Orin).\n- **Practical limits:** hand is **IP40** (indoor, dry, no dust); glove EMF tracking degrades near metal (keep at least 3 cm clearance); Hand 2 is beta hardware with non-final parameters.\n\n## Current projects, deployments and customers\n\nPublic information on customers and field deployments is **thin**; nothing found for Europe or Switzerland.\n\n- **2026-11-10** — Docs release: SDK and CLI on Windows and Apple silicon, Hand 2 position mode (Beta), glove calibration solver 15× faster. [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n- **2026-10** — `wuji-ros2` and `wuji-description` released through the ROS build farm; `wuji-isaaclab` and `wuji-mjlab` updated. [GitHub org](https://github.com/wuji-technology)\n- **2026-06** — TopoRetarget paper and code (retargeting human hand-object motion to the Wuji Hand, used for pen-spin RL). [Repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget)\n- **2026-06** — `wuji-openpi`: pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning and deployment on dual-arm + Wuji Hand rigs (teleop repo references Tianji arms). [Repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- **2026-06-05** — Trade press reports WUJI teasing Wuji Hand 2 with a claimed 20% transmission-efficiency gain; no price or ship date disclosed at the time. [RuntimeWire](https://runtimewire.com/article/wuji-tech-hand-2-robotic-hand-teaser)\n- Named customers, shipment volumes and commercial deployments in any of the four tracks: **not public**. Positioning in the docs is research, robot integration and human-machine interaction.\n\n## Roadmap and future direction\n\n- 🧪 **Wuji Hand 2 to final product:** docs label 2.2 as a non-tactile beta prototype, which implies a tactile / final version later; no date or spec published (🔭).\n- ✅ **Software consolidation (2026):** one Wuji SDK + CLI replaces the older per-product tools (wujihandpy, Wuji Studio, HMI, Upgrader are archived); Hand gen 1 is now also supported by the unified SDK.\n- ✅ **Data-loop strategy:** glove → retargeting → hand → MCAP recording → RL / VLA fine-tuning. The company's stated mission is human-level dexterous manipulation for humanoids.\n- Funding, valuation, production volumes, overseas offices: **not public**.\n\n## Challenge fit\n\n| Track | Fit 0–5 | Why (one line) | Best products | Go deeper |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| T01 Autonomous Urban Services | 2 | End effector only: adds fine manipulation (buttons, handles, parcels) to another vendor's mobile robot; indoor IP40 limits street use | Wuji Hand 2, Wuji Hand | [T01 brief](T01-Autonomous-Urban-Services/WUJI-T01-1-Brief.md) |\n| T02 Resilient & Safe City | 3 | Glove-driven teleoperated dexterous handling (valves, switches, tools) keeps the human out of the hazard; needs a partner arm | Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand 2 | [T02 brief](T02-Resilient-and-Safe-City/WUJI-T02-1-Brief.md) |\n| T03 Sustainable City | 2 | Possible sorting / disassembly manipulation, but a 20-DoF hand is overkill versus a gripper for most waste tasks | Wuji Hand, Wuji Glove | [T03 brief](T03-Sustainable-City/WUJI-T03-1-Brief.md) |\n| T04 Elderly Care & Rehabilitation | 3 | Glove alone measures grip pressure (526 points) and finger pose for hand-rehab assessment; hand + arm enables assistive fetch / feeding demos. Not a medical device | Wuji Glove, Wuji Hand 2 | [T04 brief](T04-Elderly-Care-and-Rehabilitation/WUJI-T04-1-Brief.md) |\n\n## Related docs\n- [Product portfolio](WUJI-Products.md) · [Developer guide](WUJI-Developer-Guide.md) · [Roadmap and strategy](WUJI-Roadmap-and-Strategy.md)\n- [Start here — all companies and tracks](../../00-START-HERE.md)\n\n## Sources\n\n- [Wuji Technology official site](https://www.wuji.tech) (company description, addresses, product pages [Hand](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand), [Hand 2](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2), [Glove](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove))\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 version identification and compatibility](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/version-compatibility.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 ROS 2 integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/ros2-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/introduction.md) · [installation](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/quick-start.md) · [hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji Docs release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) ([wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk), [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2), [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description), [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab), [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi), [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget), [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop))\n- [RuntimeWire: Wuji Tech teases Wuji Hand 2 (2026-06-05)](https://runtimewire.com/article/wuji-tech-hand-2-robotic-hand-teaser)\n- Third-party price listings (unverified, not official): [roboticscenter.ai Wuji Hand](https://www.roboticscenter.ai/store/product/wuji-hand) · [humanoid.guide Wuji Hand 2](https://humanoid.guide/welcome-wuji-hand-2/)\n- [LinkedIn: Wuji Tech](https://www.linkedin.com/company/wuji-tech/) (identity reference given in the task; not fetched)\n","WUJI-T01-1-Brief":"---\ntype: challenge-brief\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T01\nchallenge_title: \"Autonomous Urban Services\"\nfit: 2\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t01, brief]\n---\n# WUJI × T01 Autonomous Urban Services — Brief\n\n**Fit: 2/5** — Supporting role only: WUJI makes a 20-DoF hand and a data glove, not a robot that moves; it adds human-hand interaction (buttons, handles, key cards, handovers) to another vendor's platform.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Best hardware / platform for this track | **Wuji Hand 2** (🧪 2.2 Beta): 20 DoF, back-drivable, force-position control at **1000 Hz**, **650 g**, Ethernet. Fallback **Wuji Hand** gen 1 (✅ 15 N fingertip, 10 kg static grasp, USB). **Wuji Glove** for teleop |\n| Strongest proof point (real deployment or demo + date) | **None in urban services** (no public delivery, cleaning or concierge deployment). Closest: open-source glove → hand teleop and a pi0.5 fine-tuning pipeline for dual 7-DoF arms + two Wuji Hands (`wuji-openpi`, 2026-06) |\n| Fastest credible 48-hour demo | Hand on a partner arm operates infrastructure built for humans: press a lift button, tap a key card, hand over an item. Canned hand poses, glove teleop as remote-assist fallback |\n| Biggest risk | Arm + hand integration eats the weekend. **Indoor only** (gen 1 is IP40; Hand 2 rating and load limits not public). Shared beta hardware |\n| Pairs well with (other vendors on site) | Galaxea R1 / Galbot G1 / AGIBOT G1 (mobile base + arms) · Flexiv Rizon / ROKAE xMate (force-controlled arm) · XREAL (operator view) |\n\n## Why\n- Hotels, clinics and lifts are built for hands; a five-finger hand needs no building retrofit.\n- Joint-level Python / C SDK (`pip install wuji-sdk`) with built-in retargeting: glove or webcam drives the hand within hours.\n- URDF / MJCF / USD models allow sim work while hardware is shared.\n- Glove teleop gives a credible \"operator takes over when autonomy is stuck\" story for service fleets.\n\n## Not a fit for\n- Projects whose core is navigation, delivery routing or outdoor mobility — WUJI adds nothing there.\n- Outdoor, wet or dirty tasks (street cleaning, waste, snow).\n- Teams wanting a single-vendor robot or ready-made skills (no grasp planner, no pretrained model).\n\n## Sources\n- [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Hand 2 docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) · [Hand gen 1 docs](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) · [SDK retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T01-2-Products-and-Solutions.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T01-3-Playbook.md) · [Track overview](../../../Challenges/T01-Autonomous-Urban-Services/T01-0-Track-Overview.md)\n","WUJI-T01-2-Products-and-Solutions":"---\ntype: challenge-products\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T01\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t01, products]\n---\n# WUJI × T01 — Products and Solutions\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T01-1-Brief.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T01-3-Playbook.md)\n\n**Bottom line:** WUJI makes hands and gloves, not mobile robots. For T01 it is the **end effector and teleop input** on someone else's platform. Nothing below moves, navigates or delivers by itself.\n\n## Relevant products (ranked for this track)\n\n### Wuji Hand 2\n\n![Wuji Hand 2](../assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg)\n\n**Role in T01:** the \"human hand\" on a service robot — pressing lift and door buttons, turning handles, picking key cards, handing over small items. Back-drivable joints and force-position control make contact with fixed infrastructure (walls, panels, handles) more forgiving than a stiff position-controlled hand.\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs, 2.2 Beta) |\n|---|---|\n| Degrees of freedom | **20 active**, direct-drive, back-drivable, thumb opposition |\n| Mass | **650 g** bare · 800 g with soft pads and cables · base 70 g extra |\n| Size | 180 × 80 × 40 mm |\n| Control | **MIT force-position hybrid** (default) · position mode (Beta) · **1000 Hz × 20 axes** |\n| Comms / power | RJ45 Ethernet (100BASE-TX) · XT30, **11–13 V DC**, 12 V 20 A adapter (≥ 200 W) |\n| Mounting | Standard palm-bottom interface (1 × M3 + 2 × M4 threaded holes), adapter mount + adapter flange in the box, STEP file in `wuji-description`. ISO flange size: not public |\n| Payload, fingertip force, wrist load limits | **not public** (docs: wrist load / shock limits pending — avoid high loads) |\n| IP rating / temperature | **not public** for Hand 2 — treat as indoor, dry |\n| Tactile sensing | **None** in this beta (\"non-tactile prototype\") |\n\n- **Status:** 🧪 beta hardware; docs warn parameters, skin and external interface will change.\n- **Price:** official price not public. Third-party listings US$14,600–19,500 — ⚠️ unverified.\n- **Availability on site:** not confirmed; expect shared, supervised units.\n- **What you control:** per-joint position, velocity, feed-forward effort and kp / kd (MIT mode) or position targets; enable / disable; IMU and joint state streams. Python and C SDK, ROS 2 driver (`wuji_hand2_driver`). **No grasp planner, no skill library.**\n\n### Wuji Hand\n\n![Wuji Hand](../assets/wuji-hand.jpg)\n\n**Role in T01:** the lower-risk hand if Hand 2 units are scarce or unstable. Published force numbers, simple USB hookup, self-locking joints (holds an object without continuous effort commands).\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Degrees of freedom | **20 active** (4 per finger), self-locking direct-drive joints |\n| Mass / size | **580 ± 10 g** · 201 × 75 × 50 mm |\n| Fingertip force | **15 N** |\n| Whole-hand static grasp load | **10 kg** |\n| Open / close time | ≈ 0.3 s |\n| Control | Position control, **1000 Hz × 20 axes** |\n| Comms / power | **USB 2.0** · 12–20 V DC |\n| Protection | **IP40** — indoor, no water, no dust |\n| Idle grip life | ≥ 300,000 cycles |\n\n- **Status:** ✅ shipping.\n- **Price:** official price not public. Reseller listing \"from US$5,500\" — ⚠️ unverified.\n- **What you control:** joint position targets and joint state via the unified Wuji SDK; older ROS 2 package `wujihandros2` (archived; docs still online).\n\n### Wuji Glove\n\n![Wuji Glove](../assets/wuji-glove.jpg)\n\n**Role in T01:** remote-operator input (\"human takes over when the robot is stuck\") and demonstration capture for imitation learning. Not a robot component by itself.\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Finger tracking | **5 EMF 6-DoF fingertip trackers**, 120 Hz, ≤ 2 mm RMS, ≤ 10 ms latency |\n| Tactile | **526 points**, 120 FPS, 0–20 N, 0.1 N resolution |\n| IMU | 6-axis, 800 Hz |\n| Mass | **67.5 g** |\n| Comms / power | USB-C power, RJ45 data via adapter |\n| Operating temperature | −5 to 40 °C |\n| Limit | EMF tracking degrades near metal — keep ≥ 3 cm clearance |\n\n- **Status:** ✅ shipping. **Price:** not public.\n- **What you get:** hand skeleton (feeds SDK retargeting directly), tactile frames, IMU; MCAP recording; ROS 2 driver (`wuji_glove_driver`, 10 topics).\n- The glove tracks **fingers, not the arm** — arm teleop needs another tracker (the archived teleop repo used HTC Vive Trackers or PICO 4).\n\n### Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI\n\n![Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI](../assets/wuji-sdk.jpg)\n\n**Role in T01:** the fastest route from laptop to moving fingers.\n\n| Item | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Install | `pip install wuji-sdk` (Python) · C packages |\n| Platforms | Linux x86_64 / arm64, macOS Apple silicon, Windows (SDK + CLI); the **retargeting** page lists Linux and macOS arm64 only |\n| Retargeting | 21 MediaPipe-format keypoints (metres) in → 20 joint angles out, for Hand and Hand 2, left / right |\n| Recording | Multi-stream **MCAP** |\n| Status / price | ✅ available, free (MIT repo) |\n\n## What WUJI already does in this domain\n\n**Nothing public.** No delivery, cleaning, facility-maintenance, hospitality, retail or municipal deployment, pilot or customer was found. The official docs position the hands for research, robot integration and human-machine interaction.\n\nClosest adjacent evidence:\n\n| Date | What | Relevance to T01 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06 | `wuji-openpi`: pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning + ROS 2 deployment for a dual 7-DoF-arm + two-Wuji-Hand rig (54-D action, head + two wrist cameras). No tasks named, no checkpoints or datasets published | Shows the hands running in a bimanual learned-policy setup — the kind of stack a service manipulator would use |\n| undated | `wuji-hand-teleop`: glove-driven dual-hand teleop, optional Tianji arm control via Vive Tracker or PICO 4. Archived, \"not actively maintained\" | Reference for remote-operator service robots |\n| undated | Official video list: release films, glove → hand retargeting / teleop, in-hand reorientation in sim and on hardware | Manipulation research demos only; no service scenario |\n\nNote: the web-search quota for this research run was exhausted, so trade-press coverage of exhibitions or integrator partnerships could not be checked. Treat \"nothing public\" as \"nothing in official docs, GitHub or the company profile\".\n\n## What they are building next in this domain\n\n- 🧪 **Hand 2 final version** — the \"non-tactile prototype\" wording implies a tactile version later; no date (🔭). Tactile fingertips would matter for buttons and handles.\n- ✅ **Software consolidation** — one SDK + CLI + ROS 2 driver for all devices (2026-10 / 2026-11 releases).\n- **Inference:** WUJI's direction is a data loop (glove → retargeting → hand → MCAP → RL / VLA) for general humanoid dexterity, not urban-service products. Any T01 relevance arrives through robot makers that integrate the hand. No service-robot roadmap is published.\n\n## Software, models and data that help for this track\n\n| Asset | Use in a 48-hour T01 build | Caveat |\n|---|---|---|\n| [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) `examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py` | Glove or webcam keypoints drive the hand — remote-assist in hours | Example switches Hand 2 to position mode (Beta) |\n| SDK replay example (thumb opposition) | Pattern for **recording and replaying canned hand poses** (button-press finger, key-card pinch, handle wrap) | No interpolation; do not jump to `pos=0`, use the homing routine |\n| [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) | Hand 2 + Glove in the ROS graph next to a partner arm / Nav2 stack | **ROS 2 Lyrical only**, source build; most partner robots run Humble — bridge via the Python SDK or a container. No command watchdog in the Hand 2 driver |\n| [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) | URDF / MJCF / USD + STEP of the mount: design an adapter plate and test poses in sim | Rigid-body only |\n| [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | Fine-tune pi0.5 on your own teleop episodes | Needs NVIDIA GPU (CUDA 12), ROS 2 Humble, your own data and base checkpoint — **too heavy for 48 h** unless a team member already knows openpi |\n| [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) / wuji-isaaclab | RL in-hand reorientation | Not relevant to T01 |\n\nPretrained models or datasets from WUJI: **none published**.\n\n## Gaps and limits for this track\n\n- **No mobility, no arm, no navigation, no perception.** Everything T01 is about (\"move, deliver, maintain\") comes from a partner vendor.\n- **Indoor only.** Gen 1 is IP40; Hand 2 has no published rating. Leukerbad streets in November (snow, slush, sub-zero) are out.\n- **Hand 2 load limits unpublished** — do not lean on door handles or carry heavy parcels with it. Gen 1 has numbers (15 N fingertip, 10 kg static).\n- **No tactile sensing on the hand** — contact must be inferred from joint effort / tracking error or the arm's force sensing.\n- **Integration cost:** you must machine or 3D-print an adapter plate, route Ethernet + 12 V along the arm, and fuse arm and hand control yourself.\n- **ROS distro mismatch** (Lyrical vs. the Humble most robots use).\n- **Overkill risk:** for most delivery or cleaning tasks a parallel gripper or a tray is simpler and more robust. Use the hand only where five fingers change the outcome.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI company profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 SDK practice — replaying a thumb opposition](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-practice/opposition-replay.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK — hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — videos](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/videos.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2)\n- [GitHub: wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- [GitHub: wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop)\n- [GitHub: wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description)\n- Product pages: [Hand](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand) · [Hand 2](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) · [Glove](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove)\n","WUJI-T01-3-Playbook":"---\ntype: challenge-playbook\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T01\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t01, playbook]\n---\n# WUJI × T01 — Hackathon Playbook\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T01-1-Brief.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T01-2-Products-and-Solutions.md)\n\n**Read first:** WUJI is a **supporting vendor** for T01 (fit 2/5). Every concept below needs a partner arm or robot, and all are **indoor** (hotel, clinic, spa, lift lobby). The winning angle is narrow but real: service robots get stuck wherever the building expects a human hand.\n\n## Solution approaches\n\n### Concept 1 — \"Remote hands\" tele-assist station (safest)\n\n- **Problem → value:** Delivery and service robots stall at human interfaces (keypads, lift panels, key-card readers). One remote operator wearing a glove takes over the hand for 20 seconds, then autonomy resumes. One operator can back up many robots.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Hand 2 or Wuji Hand on its desk mount or a fixed partner arm · Wuji Glove · webcam at the hand. Optional: XREAL glasses as the operator's view.\n- **Architecture / stack:** Glove `hand_skeleton` → SDK `RetargetSession` (21 keypoints → 20 joint angles) → hand joint commands. Camera stream to the operator. A small state machine: AUTONOMOUS → HELP REQUESTED → TELEOP → RESUME. Everything on one Linux or Apple-silicon laptop. No-glove fallback: webcam + MediaPipe world landmarks into the same retargeter.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: get hand + glove running with the SDK teleop example; build a mock panel (lift buttons, keypad, card reader).\n  - H6–24: operator video view, help-request trigger, MCAP logging of each intervention.\n  - H24–40: record interventions and **replay** the most common one (e.g. floor-2 button) autonomously — \"the fleet learns from each assist\".\n  - H40–48: rehearse; measure time-to-resolve per intervention.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (1) Robot stand-in reaches the panel and raises \"need a hand\". (2) Operator across the room puts on the glove, presses the code, taps the key card. (3) Second attempt: the logged intervention replays without the operator. (4) One slide: interventions per robot per day × operator seconds.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** Glove EMF tracking near metal panels (keep ≥ 3 cm; glove stays with the operator, away from the rig) · Hand 2 position mode is Beta → fall back to Hand gen 1 · if no arm, the panel is brought to the hand on a slider.\n- **Judging angles:** Innovation — medium · Technical depth — medium · Impact — a practical human-in-the-loop model for service fleets · Leukerbad — older hotels and clinics cannot retrofit every lift and door for robots.\n\n### Concept 2 — \"Button and handle\" skill module on a force-controlled arm\n\n- **Problem → value:** Give any indoor delivery robot an autonomous skill for lift buttons, door openers and lever handles — the last gap in door-to-door indoor delivery.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Hand (gen 1 preferred: published **15 N** fingertip force) or Hand 2 · Flexiv Rizon or ROKAE xMate arm (force / torque sensing) · RGB-D or wrist camera.\n- **Architecture / stack:** Perception: fiducial tag or small detector locates the panel and target button → arm planner moves to a pre-contact pose → hand takes a canned pose (index extended, others curled) → arm pushes along the finger axis until its force sensing reports contact → verify (button light / door opens). Hand poses are recorded once via glove teleop and replayed. Arm vendor SDK + Wuji Python SDK in one process; laptop compute.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: adapter plate (STEP in `wuji-description`; 1 × M3 + 2 × M4 pattern) — 3D-print or ask WUJI for a flange; cable routing; e-stop check.\n  - H6–24: pose library (press, pinch card, wrap handle); panel localisation; force-guarded press.\n  - H24–40: second skill (lever handle or key-card tap); success-rate test over 20 trials.\n  - H40–48: polish, record backup video.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (1) Operator names a floor. (2) Arm + hand find and press the correct button on a mock panel moved to a new position. (3) Hand picks a key card and taps the reader. (4) Show the trial log and success rate.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** Hand 2 wrist-load limits are unpublished → press with low force, let the arm's force control do the work · adapter plate not ready → clamp the factory base to a bracket · perception flaky → fiducial tags.\n- **Judging angles:** Innovation — medium · Technical depth — high (force-guarded contact, hand + arm coordination) · Impact — reusable module · Leukerbad — spa hotels, rehab clinics, multi-storey buildings on steep terrain.\n\n### Concept 3 — Hotel / clinic runner: mobile manipulator with a WUJI hand\n\n- **Problem → value:** A robot delivers towels, parcels or pharmacy bags from reception to a room **through a lift and a door**, with no building retrofit. Frees staff in a seasonal resort.\n- **Hardware:** Wheeled dual-arm platform (Galaxea R1 family, Galbot G1 or AGIBOT G1 / G2) with **one** Wuji Hand on one arm, stock gripper on the other · Wuji Glove for tele-assist. Power note: Hand 2 needs 11–13 V DC, up to 20 A adapter rating — confirm the robot can supply it or carry a battery.\n- **Architecture / stack:** Partner robot's navigation stack for corridor travel → Concept 2 skill at the lift → handover at the door (hand opens when the recipient pulls; with Hand 2 use back-drivability / joint tracking error as the release cue) → Concept 1 tele-assist when a step fails. Wuji SDK on the robot's onboard Linux PC or a strapped-on laptop; if the robot runs ROS 2 Humble, bridge through a thin Python node instead of `wuji-ros2` (Lyrical only).\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: secure a platform and WUJI's agreement to mount; power + mount; navigation between two waypoints.\n  - H6–24: button press from the mobile base (base positioning error is the hard part); handover behaviour.\n  - H24–40: full run reception → lift panel → door; add tele-assist.\n  - H40–48: three clean runs filmed; live demo on the shortest reliable route.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (1) \"Room 12 needs towels.\" (2) Robot drives, presses the lift button with a finger. (3) Arrives, knocks or rings, hands over. (4) One forced failure → operator glove assist → continues.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** Two vendors' time and hardware needed — highest scheduling risk · base misalignment → fiducials at the panel · if mobile integration slips by H24, drop to Concept 2 on a static arm and show navigation separately.\n- **Judging angles:** Innovation — medium-high · Technical depth — high · Impact — high and easy to explain · Leukerbad — strong (hotels, thermal baths, clinics).\n\n### Concept 4 — Learned dexterous service skill (most ambitious)\n\n- **Problem → value:** Replace hand-coded poses with a policy learned from glove demonstrations, so new service tasks (sorting key cards, opening a parcel-locker latch) are taught, not programmed.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Hand(s) on partner arm(s) · Wuji Glove · arm teleop device · head + wrist cameras · **NVIDIA GPU** (CUDA 12).\n- **Architecture / stack:** Glove + arm teleop → MCAP / LeRobot episodes → fine-tune with `wuji-openpi` (pi0.5; reference config is dual 7-DoF arms + two hands, 54-D, configurable) or a lighter behaviour-cloning policy → ROS 2 Humble deployment.\n- **48-hour plan:** H0–6 teleop rig working · H6–24 collect 50–100 episodes of one task · H24–40 fine-tune and evaluate · H40–48 demo, with teleop as fallback.\n- **3-minute demo script:** Show a demonstration, the training curve, then the policy doing the task; compare against scripted replay when the object is moved.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** No published checkpoints or datasets; teleop repo is archived and tied to Tianji arms; training time may exceed the weekend. Fallback: present the data pipeline + scripted replay (Concept 2).\n- **Judging angles:** Innovation — high · Technical depth — very high · Impact — long-term · Leukerbad — weak unless the task is local.\n\n## Cross-vendor combos worth considering\n\n| Combo | What it enables | Integration effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| WUJI Hand + Flexiv Rizon or ROKAE xMate | Force-guarded button / handle / card skills (Concept 2) | Medium — adapter plate, two SDKs |\n| WUJI Hand + Galaxea R1 / Galbot G1 / AGIBOT G1 | Mobile indoor delivery through lifts and doors (Concept 3) | High — mount, power, base alignment, two teams |\n| WUJI Hand + Unitree G1 humanoid | Humanoid concierge with a five-finger hand | High — wrist interface and payload unknown, ⚠️ unverified fit |\n| WUJI Glove + Hand + XREAL glasses | Remote operator sees the scene and drives the hand (Concept 1) | Low–medium |\n| WUJI Hand + Dobot CR / Nova cobot | Fixed concierge counter: key-card and small-item handover | Medium — no arm-side force sensing assumed; rely on hand compliance |\n| WUJI SDK on D-Robotics RDK | Small edge host on the robot instead of a laptop | Low–medium — SDK ships Linux arm64 builds; not tested on RDK, ⚠️ unverified |\n| WUJI Glove + OriginFlow EMG | Richer operator-intent data for demonstrations | High, research-grade — skip for T01 |\n\n## Questions to ask the WUJI engineers on site\n\n1. How many hands (gen 1 vs. Hand 2, left / right) and gloves are here, and how is access shared?\n2. Which arm flanges did you bring adapters for? Any already mounted on a partner robot on site?\n3. Hand 2: what are safe **wrist load, fingertip force and payload** limits for pressing buttons and turning handles? IP rating?\n4. Can we read per-joint effort / current for contact detection, and at what rate?\n5. Is Hand 2 **position mode** stable on the firmware installed here, or should we stay in MIT mode? Recommended kp / kd for contact tasks?\n6. ROS 2: is there a Humble build or Docker image, or should we bridge through the Python SDK?\n7. Can Hand 2 run from a mobile robot's battery (11–13 V)? Peak current in practice?\n8. Spare soft pads / skins on site, and what happens if we damage a finger?\n\n## Decision rule\n\n- **Pick WUJI for T01 if** your idea hinges on a robot using infrastructure made for human hands (buttons, handles, key cards, handovers) indoors, you have a committed partner arm or mobile platform by H6, and someone on the team can build an adapter plate and merge two SDKs.\n- **Avoid if** your core is navigation, outdoor delivery, cleaning or waste logistics, you want a single-vendor robot, or a simple gripper would do the job.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI company profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 SDK practice — replaying a thumb opposition](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-practice/opposition-replay.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK — hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [GitHub: wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2)\n- [GitHub: wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- [GitHub: wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop)\n- [GitHub: wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description)\n","WUJI-T02-1-Brief":"---\ntype: challenge-brief\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T02\nchallenge_title: \"Resilient & Safe City\"\nfit: 3\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t02, brief]\n---\n# WUJI × T02 Resilient & Safe City — Brief\n\n**Fit: 3/5** — Good \"remote hands\" for a multi-vendor hazard-response robot (glove-driven dexterous teleoperation), but no arm, no mobility, no outdoor rating and no public safety-domain deployment.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Best hardware / platform for this track | **Wuji Glove → Wuji Hand 2** (20 DoF, back-drivable, MIT mode, 1000 Hz) on a partner arm. Fallback: Wuji Hand gen 1 (USB, **15 N** fingertip, **10 kg** static grasp) |\n| Strongest proof point (real deployment or demo + date) | None in safety / rescue / inspection. Closest: official glove-to-hand teleoperation workflow, SDK release **2026-11-10** |\n| Fastest credible 48-hour demo | Operator behind a partition closes a valve, trips a breaker and pulls a plug on a mock hazard panel; arm uses pre-taught poses, fingers follow the glove |\n| Biggest risk | **No WUJI arm**: you need another vendor's arm plus a flange adapter. Hands are dry-lab devices (gen 1 **IP40**; Hand 2 beta: **15–30 °C**, no shock guarantee) |\n| Pairs well with (other vendors on site) | Flexiv, ROKAE, Dobot (arm) · Unitree, AGIBOT, Galaxea (mobile carrier) · XREAL (operator view) · SKYLANDX (3D context) |\n\n## Why\n- Hazardous-environment teleoperation is a core T02 theme; glove → retargeting → hand is WUJI's best-documented workflow (about **45 min** to first teleop per docs).\n- 20 independent DoF operate **human controls and tools** (valves, switches, plugs, handles) without a custom gripper per task.\n- Hand 2 offers per-joint stiffness and effort limits for gentle contact. Caveat: no robot-side touch sensing; docs say not to treat joint current as force.\n- Open stack: `pip install wuji-sdk`, webcam keypoints can replace a glove, MCAP session logs, ROS 2 drivers, URDF / MJCF / USD.\n\n## Not a fit for\n- Outdoor, wet, dusty or cold field work (avalanche, flood, fire scene).\n- Patrol, mapping, monitoring or autonomy-first projects: no sensing platform, mobility or high-level skills.\n- Heavy-force rescue tasks (debris, jammed doors).\n\n## Sources\n[WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Hand 2 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) · [Hand 2 user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md) · [Hand gen 1 overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md) · [Glove quick start](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/getting-started.md) · [Release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T02-2-Products-and-Solutions.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T02-3-Playbook.md) · [Track overview](../../../Challenges/T02-Resilient-and-Safe-City/T02-0-Track-Overview.md)\n","WUJI-T02-2-Products-and-Solutions":"---\ntype: challenge-products\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T02\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t02, products]\n---\n# WUJI × T02 — Products and Solutions\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T02-1-Brief.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T02-3-Playbook.md)\n\n**Bottom line for T02:** WUJI supplies the *hand* and the *operator glove* of a teleoperated hazard-response robot. Arm, mobility, cameras, mapping and autonomy must come from other vendors on site. WUJI has **no public safety, rescue or inspection deployment**.\n\n## Relevant products (ranked for this track)\n\n### Wuji Glove\n\n![Wuji Glove](../assets/wuji-glove.jpg)\n\n**Role in T02:** the operator interface. It turns a human hand into a 20-joint command for the robot hand, and its tactile map shows how the operator is gripping. It also works alone as a gesture / grip sensor when no hand or arm is free.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs) | Why it matters for T02 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Finger tracking | 5 EMF 6-DoF fingertip modules, **120 Hz**, ≤ 2 mm RMS, < 5° RMS, latency **≤ 10 ms** | Low-lag teleoperation, no camera line of sight needed |\n| Tactile | **526 points** (24 × 31 matrix), 120 FPS, 0–20 N, 0.1 N resolution, palm side | Measures the operator's grip, not the robot's contact |\n| IMU | 6-axis, **800 Hz**, on the back of the hand | Orientation only; no wrist position |\n| Connection | Wired: USB-C power (5 V / 1 A), RJ45 100BASE-TX via data-acquisition board on the forearm | Operator is tethered to a PC |\n| Environment | −5 to 40 °C, **< 55 % RH** | Control-room device, not for wet field use |\n| Metal sensitivity | Keep **≥ 3 cm** from metallic / ferromagnetic objects | Do not rest the glove on a steel bench |\n| Weight | 67.5 g glove, 192.6 g with cable | Wearable for long sessions |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ shipping · price not public · on-site quantity unknown.\n- **Developer access:** `tactile`, `emf_poses`, `imu_data/palm` streams and joint angles from built-in inverse kinematics; per-user hand-model calibration (`wuji calib hand-model`); live viewer (`wuji viz`). One client can hold the glove at a time.\n- **Setup time per docs:** about **30 min** to first data, about **45 min** to glove-to-Hand-2 teleoperation.\n\n### Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta)\n\n![Wuji Hand 2](../assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg)\n\n**Role in T02:** the remote hand that operates human controls (valves, breakers, plugs, handles) in a place a person should not enter. Back-drivable joints make contact with unknown objects more forgiving.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs) | Why it matters for T02 |\n|---|---|---|\n| DoF | **20 active** (4 per finger), full thumb opposition, no coupled joints | Uses tools and controls built for human hands |\n| Drive | Back-drivable direct drive, FOC, **1000 Hz × 20 axes** | Compliant contact, fast response |\n| Control | **MIT mode** (position, velocity, current feed-forward, per-joint kp / kd) · position mode (Beta; docs require firmware v3.0.0+ and SDK v2026.11.9+) | Tune stiffness per task; cap effort per joint |\n| Feedback | Position (rad), velocity (rad/s), effort (current in A in MIT mode; torque estimate in N·m in position mode), diagnostics, IMU | Docs warn: **do not use joint current as a contact-force measurement** on 2.2 |\n| Weight | 650 g bare, **800 g** with pads and cables (base 70 g extra) | Fits small cobots and humanoid wrists |\n| Interface | RJ45 Ethernet 100BASE-TX + XT30 power, 11–13 V DC, 12 V 20 A adapter (≥ 200 W) | Needs a 12 V rail and an Ethernet run on the carrier robot |\n| Environment | **15–30 °C**, dry and clean, no liquids, oil mist or dust; no IP rating published | Indoor mock-ups only |\n| Robustness | No guarantee for drop, vibration, shock or durability; \"do not grasp fragile or high-value objects\"; avoid long high-load runs (thermal design unfinished) | Treat as a prototype; plan gentle tasks |\n| Force / payload | **not public** for Hand 2 (docs say prototype values are not a design basis) | Test your task on day 1 |\n\n- **Status / price:** 🧪 beta prototype (\"non-tactile\") · official price not public (third-party listings US$14.6k–19.5k ⚠️ unverified).\n- **Mounting:** palm interface with M3 / M4 threaded holes, identical on left / right; an adapter mount and adapter flange ship in the box; integrators are expected to machine an arm-side plate. STEP files and drawings are in `wuji-description`. Wrist load limits are not yet published.\n- **Developer access:** joint level only (Python / C). No grasp planner, no skills, no camera.\n\n### Wuji Hand (gen 1)\n\n![Wuji Hand](../assets/wuji-hand.jpg)\n\n**Role in T02:** the lower-risk hand if Hand 2 units are scarce or unstable. Published force numbers, simpler USB wiring, self-locking joints that hold a grip.\n\n| Spec | Value (official docs) | Why it matters for T02 |\n|---|---|---|\n| DoF | **20 active**, serial direct drive, **self-locking** joints | Holds a grasp without continuous effort |\n| Fingertip force | **15 N** | Enough for switches, small valves, connectors; not for forcing |\n| Load | Whole-hand static grasp **10 kg**, vertical grasp **5 kg**, single-finger hook **3 kg**, max grasp diameter **100 mm** | Can hold and carry a hand tool; test your object before relying on it |\n| Control | Position control, **1000 Hz × 20 axes**; effort limit per joint 0–3.5 A (default 1.5 A) | Simple and stable; less compliant than Hand 2 |\n| Feedback | Joint position, effort (A), per-joint temperature, bus voltage, error codes | Health monitoring during long teleop sessions |\n| Interface | **USB 2.0** (USB-C) + XT30 power, 12–20 V DC, static power 12 W | One USB cable to the host PC |\n| Protection | **IP40** | Dry indoor use only |\n| Weight | 580 ± 10 g | Light payload cost on the arm |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ shipping · official price not public (reseller \"from US$5,500\" ⚠️ unverified).\n- **Mounting:** direct-mount adapter with a grooved flange for M5 and M6 screws; M4 screws to the hand's latch.\n\n### Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI\n\n![Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI](../assets/wuji-sdk.jpg)\n\n**Role in T02:** the glue. One package discovers gloves and hands, retargets human pose to joint commands, and records sessions.\n\n| Capability | Detail | T02 use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Install | `pip install wuji-sdk`; CLI via the official install script | Running in minutes on Linux, macOS (Apple silicon), Windows |\n| Teleop example | `wuji-sdk/examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py` (glove → Hand 2, right hand by default) | The core of every remote-hands demo |\n| Retargeting | 21 MediaPipe-format hand keypoints in → 20 joint angles out | Webcam hand tracking as a glove substitute |\n| Recording | `TopicRecorder` → **MCAP** (LZ4 / Zstd), episodes, pause / resume, drop-rate / jitter / sync metrics and alerts | Incident log and demonstration data. Camera streams are not covered by the SDK recorder |\n| Diagnostics | `wuji devices`, `wuji ping`, `wuji doctor`, fault logs, status LEDs (warning / fault / fatal) | Fast triage when a hand stops mid-demo |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ available, free.\n\n## What WUJI already does in this domain\n\n**Nothing public.** No deployment, pilot, customer case or demo in emergency response, hazardous-environment teleoperation, infrastructure inspection or security was found in WUJI's official site, docs, GitHub organisation or in the company-profile research. The docs position the products for \"research, robot integration and human-machine interaction\".\n\nClosest adjacent, dated evidence:\n\n| Date | What | Relevance to T02 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-11-10 | Unified SDK / CLI release (Windows, Apple silicon, Hand 2 position mode Beta) — [release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) | Teleop stack is current and maintained |\n| 2026-08-31 | `wuji-hand-teleop` archived (dual Tianji arms + dual Wuji Hands, Vive Tracker / PICO 4, stereo head camera streamed to the headset) — [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) | A full arm + hand remote-operation reference exists, but is unsupported; README says a product version is \"coming soon\" |\n| 2026-06 | `wuji-openpi`: pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning for two 7-DoF arms + two hands — [repo](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | Path from teleop demonstrations to autonomous skills; no checkpoints published |\n\nNote: a dedicated news search could not be run in this research pass (search quota exhausted), so trade-press coverage of safety-domain demos was not re-checked beyond the profile research. Ask the WUJI staff on site.\n\n## What they are building next in this domain\n\n- 🧪 **Hand 2 final version with tactile sensing** — inference from the docs calling 2.2 a \"non-tactile prototype\"; no date or spec. Tactile fingertips would matter for blind manipulation in smoke or clutter.\n- 🔭 **Productised teleoperation system** — the archived teleop README mentions a product version \"coming soon\"; no details.\n- 🔭 **Connector change on Hand 2** — docs warn the external interface form will change in later 2.2 releases; adapters built this weekend may not fit future units.\n- **No safety- or rescue-specific roadmap is public.** Ruggedised or sealed hands: not announced.\n\n## Software, models and data that help for this track\n\n| Asset | What you get | 48-hour use |\n|---|---|---|\n| [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) (MIT) | Device API, retargeting, MCAP recording, Python examples | Glove → hand teleop on day 1 |\n| [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) | ROS 2 drivers for Hand 2 and Glove (official target: Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical) | Bridge to a partner arm's ROS 2 stack; use Docker if your laptop differs |\n| [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) | URDF / MJCF / MJX / USD, STEP and flange drawings | Simulate the task; design or print the arm adapter |\n| [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) (MIT, archived) | ROS 2 Humble Docker stack for arm + hand teleop, camera streaming to PICO | Read for architecture; do not expect it to run on other arms unmodified |\n| [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) (Apache-2.0) | Fine-tuning and deployment of pi0 / pi0.5; needs NVIDIA GPU (CUDA 12), LeRobot v2.1 data | Stretch goal only |\n| Pretrained models / datasets | **none published** | — |\n\n## Gaps and limits for this track\n\n- **Not a robot.** No arm, base, camera, mapping, navigation or autonomy. Glove gives finger pose but **no wrist position**; arm teleoperation needs an external tracker or another input.\n- **Not field-rated.** IP40 (gen 1); Hand 2 limited to 15–30 °C, dry and clean, no shock guarantee. Any \"avalanche / flood / fire\" story must be staged indoors and described honestly as a lab prototype.\n- **No touch on the robot side.** Current Hand 2 beta has no tactile sensors and its joint current must not be used as a force measurement. Operator feedback is visual only; the glove has no haptic actuators in the published specs.\n- **Light forces.** 15 N fingertip class (gen 1); Hand 2 force data not public. Stiff industrial valves or emergency door releases may be out of reach.\n- **Tethered and local.** Glove and Hand 2 are wired Ethernet on one subnet. Remote operation over a wide-area link is not documented; watchdog behaviour on communication loss is not documented.\n- **Beta hardware.** Thermal behaviour under long load is unverified; interface and parameters may change.\n- **Access.** Units are expensive and fragile; expect shared, supervised use.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI company profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 user notice / usage constraints](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 joint states and control](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/joint-control.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji Glove quick start (incl. glove-to-hand teleoperation)](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/getting-started.md)\n- [Wuji SDK data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [Wuji Docs release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) · [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- Canonical product pages (JavaScript-rendered; specs above come from the docs, not these pages): [Wuji Hand](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand) · [Wuji Hand 2](https://www.wuji.tech/en/hand2) · [Wuji Glove](https://www.wuji.tech/en/glove)\n","WUJI-T02-3-Playbook":"---\ntype: challenge-playbook\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T02\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t02, playbook]\n---\n# WUJI × T02 — Hackathon Playbook\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T02-1-Brief.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T02-2-Products-and-Solutions.md)\n\n**Read first:** WUJI = hand + glove + SDK. No arm, no base, no cameras, no autonomy. Hands are dry-lab devices (IP40 / 15–30 °C). Every concept below is an **indoor mock-up** of a hazard task and needs a partner vendor, except Concept 2.\n\n## Solution approaches\n\n### Concept 1 — Remote Hands: hazard-panel teleoperation cell\n\n- **Problem → value:** After a gas alarm, fire or flooding in a technical room (thermal-water plant, cable-car drive room, tunnel substation), someone still has to close a valve, trip a breaker or pull a plug. A glove-driven robot hand does it while the technician stays outside.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand 2 (or Hand gen 1) · one partner arm (Flexiv Rizon or ROKAE xMate preferred for compliant contact; Dobot CR as alternative) · 1–2 USB cameras · a plywood \"hazard panel\" with a quarter-turn valve, a rocker / breaker switch, a connector, a door handle.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Perception: operator's eyes via camera feed on a monitor (no machine perception needed).\n  - Planning: arm moves between **pre-taught poses** (\"valve\", \"breaker\", \"plug\") selected by keyboard or foot pedal, plus small jog offsets. The glove has no wrist position, so do not plan on free-hand arm teleop on day 1.\n  - Control: `1.teleop_real.py` from `wuji-sdk` (glove → retargeting → 20 joint commands at 1000 Hz). Set `effort_limit` and soft kp / kd on Hand 2 for gentle contact. Arm through its vendor SDK.\n  - Compute: one laptop on the 192.168.1.x subnet for glove + hand; arm controller on a second interface.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: secure a hand, a glove and an arm slot; confirm flange adapter; run glove-to-hand teleop on the desk stand; build the panel.\n  - H6–24: mount hand on arm; teach arm poses; tune stiffness and effort limits per task; add camera view.\n  - H24–40: record every run to MCAP; add a simple operator UI (task buttons, hand temperature / fault status); measure task times.\n  - H40–48: rehearse, film a backup video, freeze the code.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (0:00) alarm scenario on screen, operator sits behind a partition. (0:30) arm goes to \"valve\", operator closes it with the glove. (1:15) \"breaker\" tripped, connector pulled. (2:15) show the recorded session replay and task times versus sending a person in protective gear. (2:45) limits and next steps.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** no adapter plate → hand stays on the desk stand and the panel is brought to the hand. Glove tracking jitter near metal → keep 3 cm clearance, or use webcam + MediaPipe keypoints into the SDK retargeter. Hand 2 fault or overheating → switch to Hand gen 1. Valve too stiff for the 15 N class → use a lever-handle valve.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation — human tools operated without a custom gripper; technical depth — compliance tuning, retargeting, logging; impact — keeps staff out of hazard zones; Leukerbad — thermal plant rooms and lift machinery in a valley that road closures can isolate.\n\n### Concept 2 — Gesture and grip command glove for a patrol robot (glove-only)\n\n- **Problem → value:** In noise, darkness or with a radio in the other hand, responders command robots badly by voice or tablet. A glove turns hand signals into robot commands and logs what the responder's hand did.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove only · any mobile robot with an open motion API (Unitree Go2, Genisom M1, Magiclab MagicDog) · laptop. No Wuji Hand and no arm needed — the choice if hands are fully booked.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Perception: glove joint angles (EMF inverse kinematics) + palm IMU + tactile map.\n  - Planning: small classifier (k-NN or a tiny MLP on 20 joint angles) for 6–8 static signals (stop, come, search left / right, sit, return); tactile squeeze as a dead-man confirm.\n  - Control: map classes to the robot's high-level velocity / mode API.\n  - Compute: laptop; glove is tethered by Ethernet, so the operator carries the laptop or stays at a console.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: glove streaming, per-user calibration; robot API hello-world.\n  - H6–24: collect gesture data (MCAP), train classifier, add confirm logic.\n  - H24–40: run a short \"search the corridor\" course; add event log.\n  - H40–48: rehearse; measure recognition accuracy and false triggers.\n- **3-minute demo script:** responder signals the quadruped through a mock search course without speaking; squeeze-to-confirm prevents accidental commands; show the log and accuracy numbers.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** tether limits walking range → present as a console or vehicle-mounted operator. Humidity limit (< 55 % RH) and metal sensitivity → keep it indoors. Weak WUJI differentiation (a camera could do gestures) → emphasise tactile confirm and no line of sight.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation — moderate; technical depth — modest; impact — practical operator interface; Leukerbad — mountain-rescue style hand signals in poor visibility. Lowest risk, lowest ceiling.\n\n### Concept 3 — Mobile Remote Hands with AR operator view\n\n- **Problem → value:** The hazard is not next to the robot. A mobile platform carries the hand to the cabinet or valve; the operator sees the scene in AR and works through the glove.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand 2 · mobile manipulator or humanoid with a free wrist (Galaxea R1 family, AGIBOT G1 / G2, Unitree G1 / H1, Spirit AI Moz1, UniX Wanda — whichever team will allow an end-effector swap) · XREAL glasses for the camera view · optional SKYLANDX MetaCam scan of the room as a 3D context map.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Perception: robot head / wrist camera stream to XREAL; pre-scanned 3D model for orientation.\n  - Planning: base driven by the vendor's teleop or navigation; arm by vendor teleop or pre-taught poses; fingers by glove.\n  - Control: Wuji SDK or `wuji-ros2` node on the robot's onboard computer or a tethered laptop; hand needs a 12 V rail and Ethernet on the robot.\n  - Compute: robot onboard PC + operator laptop on one network.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: agree with the partner vendor on mounting, power and network; bench teleop.\n  - H6–24: mechanical and electrical integration; camera to glasses; drive-and-reach test.\n  - H24–40: full mission run (drive in → open cabinet → flip switch → drive out); log everything.\n  - H40–48: rehearse; backup video.\n- **3-minute demo script:** operator in glasses and glove at a desk; robot drives into the \"sealed\" area, opens a cabinet door and isolates a circuit; split screen shows operator hand and robot hand.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** end-effector swap refused or adapter missing → fall back to Concept 1 on a fixed arm placed on a cart. Network latency over Wi-Fi → keep hand control on the robot's onboard PC and send only glove data. Weight and power budget on the wrist (800 g + cabling) → check with the vendor first.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation — multi-vendor remote-presence system; technical depth — high integration; impact — closest to a real response robot; Leukerbad — remote expert operates local equipment when the access road is closed.\n\n### Concept 4 — Teach once by teleop, repeat when the link drops\n\n- **Problem → value:** Teleoperation fails when communication fails. Record the operator's valve-closing or breaker-trip demonstration and let the robot repeat it autonomously on link loss.\n- **Hardware:** as Concept 1 (fixed arm + hand + glove) plus a wrist or scene camera; NVIDIA GPU machine only for the stretch goal.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Perception: fiducial marker (AprilTag) on the panel to re-locate the target; camera on the arm.\n  - Planning: baseline = **trajectory replay** of recorded arm poses and hand joint trajectories, re-anchored to the marker, with compliant kp / kd. Stretch = fine-tune pi0.5 with `wuji-openpi` (needs LeRobot v2.1 data, CUDA 12 GPU, no checkpoints provided — unlikely to converge in 48 h).\n  - Control: heartbeat between operator PC and robot PC; on timeout switch from teleop to stored skill, then to a safe open-hand pose.\n  - Compute: laptop for baseline; GPU workstation for the stretch.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: Concept 1 basics.\n  - H6–24: reliable teleop; record 20–50 demonstrations per skill to MCAP together with arm states.\n  - H24–40: replay with marker re-anchoring; heartbeat and mode switch; success-rate test with the panel moved a few centimetres.\n  - H40–48: rehearse the cable-pull moment; backup video.\n- **3-minute demo script:** operator starts closing the valve, a team member unplugs the network cable, the robot finishes the job alone and reports status when the link returns.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** replay is brittle to panel pose → keep the marker and limit offsets; no robot-side touch sensing → rely on compliance, not force thresholds (docs advise against using joint current as force). If autonomy fails, demo Concept 1 and show replay in simulation with the MJCF model.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation — shared autonomy for degraded communication; technical depth — highest; impact — resilience is literally the track title; Leukerbad — alpine valleys lose connectivity in storms.\n\n## Cross-vendor combos worth considering\n\n| Combo | What it enables | Integration effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| WUJI hand + **Flexiv Rizon** | Force-controlled arm for compliant valve turning and door opening | Medium: adapter plate, two SDKs on one PC |\n| WUJI hand + **ROKAE xMate** (7-DoF, joint torque sensing) | Same role; hand-guided teaching of arm poses | Medium |\n| WUJI hand + **Dobot CR / Nova** | Simple position-controlled carrier with easy pose teaching | Low–medium |\n| WUJI hand + **Unitree G1 / H1** or **AGIBOT** humanoid | Humanoid with a 20-DoF hand for a mobile response story | High: wrist mount, power, vendor approval |\n| WUJI hand + **Galaxea R1** / **Galbot G1** / **Spirit AI Moz1** | Wheeled dual-arm base that drives the hand to the task | High: end-effector swap |\n| WUJI glove + **Unitree Go2** / **Genisom M1** / **MagicDog** | Gesture-commanded patrol or search robot (Concept 2) | Low: software only |\n| WUJI teleop + **XREAL** glasses | Head-up camera view for the operator | Low–medium: video streaming app |\n| WUJI teleop + **SKYLANDX MetaCam** | 3D scan of the room as operator context / digital twin | Low if used as a pre-scan |\n| WUJI glove + **OriginFlow** EMG | Two-channel operator input (pose + muscle effort) for grip-strength commands | Medium, research-style ⚠️ unverified compatibility |\n| WUJI hand + **D-Robotics RDK** | Onboard host for the hand SDK on a mobile robot (SDK supports Linux arm64) | Medium ⚠️ not tested by WUJI as far as public docs show |\n\n## Questions to ask the WUJI engineers on site\n\n1. How many Hand 2, Hand gen 1 and glove units are available per team, and for how many hours?\n2. Which arm flange adapters did you bring, and for which vendors' arms on site? Can we get the STEP file for a printed plate?\n3. Which firmware is on the Hand 2 units — is position mode (firmware v3.0.0+) available, or MIT mode only?\n4. What kp / kd and `effort_limit` values do you recommend for turning a valve and flipping a switch? What fingertip force can Hand 2 safely deliver?\n5. What happens to the hand if the Ethernet link or the host process dies — hold, relax or fault? Is there a command watchdog?\n6. How do you recommend getting wrist pose for arm teleoperation with the glove (which tracker and mount)? Did you bring any?\n7. How long can Hand 2 hold a loaded grasp before thermal derating, and how do we read temperature?\n8. Is a tactile Hand 2 or any ruggedised / sealed version planned, and has any customer used the hands for remote operation in hazardous areas?\n\n## Decision rule\n\n**Pick WUJI for T02 if** your idea is teleoperated or taught manipulation of human-scale controls in a staged indoor hazard scene, and you have secured a partner arm (or mobile manipulator) plus a mounting adapter in the first six hours.\n\n**Avoid if** your idea is patrol, mapping, monitoring, outdoor or wet operation, heavy-force rescue, or anything that must run autonomously out of the box — WUJI adds cost and integration risk without solving those.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI company profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Glove quick start (incl. glove-to-hand teleoperation)](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/getting-started.md)\n- [Wuji Glove introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 user notice / usage constraints](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 joint states and control](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/joint-control.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) overview](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji SDK data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [Wuji SDK hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) · [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) · [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) · [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) · [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n","WUJI-T03-1-Brief":"---\ntype: challenge-brief\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T03\nchallenge_title: \"Sustainable City\"\nfit: 2\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t03, brief]\n---\n# WUJI × T03 Sustainable City — Brief\n\n**Fit: 2/5** — Supporting role only: a 20-DoF hand and a tactile glove add value for *circular-economy* tasks made for human hands (disassembly, repair, cap / lid separation), but for ordinary waste sorting a simple gripper is cheaper, tougher and faster.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Best hardware / platform for this track | **Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand** (gen 1 if you need published force numbers: **15 N** fingertip, **10 kg** static grasp; Hand 2 if you need compliant, back-drivable MIT control) — always on a partner arm |\n| Strongest proof point (real deployment or demo + date) | **None in this domain.** No public WUJI sustainability, recycling or energy deployment found. Closest: glove-to-hand teleoperation quick start and `wuji-openpi` pi0 / pi0.5 pipeline (2026-06), both generic manipulation |\n| Fastest credible 48-hour demo | Glove-teleoperated **disassembly / repair station**: operator wearing the glove drives the hand on a fixed arm to open a small device and separate parts into reuse bins, while every episode is logged to MCAP |\n| Biggest risk | **IP40**, soft pads and exposed flex cables: no wet, dirty, sharp or dusty waste. Plus Hand 2 is beta with unpublished payload and wrist-load limits |\n| Pairs well with (other vendors on site) | Flexiv (Rizon force-controlled arm) · ROKAE (xMate) · Dobot (CR cobots) · Galaxea / Galbot (mobile dual-arm) · D-Robotics (edge vision) · XREAL (operator view) |\n\n## Why\n- Only pure dexterous-hand vendor on site: useful where objects are **built for human fingers** (clips, caps, connectors, knobs, valve heads) and a parallel gripper fails.\n- **Glove → hand teleoperation works in hours** (retargeting is inside the SDK), so a human-in-the-loop disassembly cell is realistic.\n- Built-in **MCAP recording** turns every teleoperated episode into training data: a credible \"today teleop, tomorrow autonomy\" story.\n- Gen 1 reports **per-joint current and bus voltage**, so you can show a measured energy-per-grasp figure (T03.3 \"energy-efficient robotic systems\").\n\n## Not a fit for\n- Bulk waste sorting, litter picking, anything outdoors, wet or abrasive: use a gripper or suction instead.\n- Environmental monitoring, water / energy management, mobile inspection: WUJI has no mobile base, no perception stack and no on-board compute.\n- Teams that want a single-vendor build: every WUJI idea needs someone else's arm.\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T03-2-Products-and-Solutions.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T03-3-Playbook.md) · [Track overview](../../../Challenges/T03-Sustainable-City/T03-0-Track-Overview.md)\n","WUJI-T03-2-Products-and-Solutions":"---\ntype: challenge-products\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T03\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t03, products]\n---\n# WUJI × T03 — Products and Solutions\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T03-1-Brief.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T03-3-Playbook.md)\n\n**Bottom line:** WUJI sells an end effector and a data glove, not a sustainability solution. Its sensible T03 role is **dexterous handling in circular-economy tasks** (disassembly, repair, separating multi-material items) and **capturing human demonstrations** of those tasks. What WUJI actually brings on site is not confirmed; check at the booth first.\n\n## Relevant products (ranked for this track)\n\n### Wuji Glove\n![Wuji Glove](../assets/wuji-glove.jpg)\n\n**Role in T03:** lowest-risk entry point. Worn by a human, it (a) teleoperates the Wuji Hand for disassembly / sorting steps, and (b) records how a skilled person grips and takes apart an item (pressure map + finger pose), which is the raw material for later automation. Works even if no arm is available.\n\n| Spec (official docs) | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Tactile | **526 points** (24 × 31 matrix, full palm side), **120 FPS**, 0–20 N, 0.1 N resolution, 4 mm pitch, ±6 % repeatability |\n| Finger tracking | 5 EMF 6-DoF fingertip modules, 120 Hz, ≤ 2 mm RMS, < 5° RMS, ≤ 10 ms latency |\n| IMU | 6-axis on back of hand, 800 Hz |\n| Weight | **67.5 g** glove (192.6 g with cable) |\n| Interfaces | USB-C power (5 V / 1 A), RJ45 Ethernet data via adapter |\n| Environment | −5 to 40 °C, **< 55 % RH** operating; water resistance not stated |\n| Known limit | EMF tracking is disturbed by metal / ferromagnetic objects: keep **≥ 3 cm** clearance |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ shipping · price not public.\n- **Developer access:** SDK subscriptions for tactile frames, fingertip poses, solved hand skeleton and IMU; MCAP recording; ROS 2 driver in `wuji-ros2`.\n- **T03 caveat:** e-waste and cans are metal. Expect degraded finger tracking when fingers are close to metal parts; the tactile matrix still works. Test on your actual objects in hour 1.\n\n### Wuji Hand (gen 1)\n![Wuji Hand](../assets/wuji-hand.jpg)\n\n**Role in T03:** the hand with **published load numbers**, simple USB hookup and per-joint current feedback. Best choice when the task is gripping, twisting or pulling recyclables and you need to argue payload and energy with real figures.\n\n| Spec (official docs) | Value |\n|---|---|\n| DoF | **20 active** (4 per finger), self-locking direct-drive joints |\n| Weight / size | **580 ± 10 g** · 201 × 75 × 50 mm |\n| Forces | fingertip **15 N** · whole-hand static grasp **10 kg** · vertical grasp 5 kg · single-finger hook 3 kg |\n| Object size | max grasp diameter **100 mm** |\n| Speed | open / close ≈ **0.3 s**, ≥ 2 cycles per second |\n| Precision | ±1 mm repeatability |\n| Power | 12–20 V DC · **12 W static** · adapter 12 V 20 A |\n| Control | position control, 1000 Hz × 20 axes, **USB 2.0** (USB-C) + XT30 power |\n| Feedback | joint position, **joint effort in amps**, per-joint bus voltage, temperature, error code |\n| Protection | **IP40**, aluminium shell, idle grip life ≥ 300,000 cycles |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ shipping · official price not public (reseller listing \"from US$5,500\" — ⚠️ unverified).\n- **Developer access:** joint-level position targets, per-joint effort limit (default 1.5 A, range 0–3.5 A, derated by firmware when hot), full state readback. No grasp planner.\n- **Extras:** docs mention an optional tactile glove worn on the hand and an impact-release wrist adapter with safety chain; whether either is on site is unknown.\n\n### Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta)\n![Wuji Hand 2](../assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg)\n\n**Role in T03:** compliant handling. Back-drivable joints with MIT (stiffness / damping) control let fingers give way on fragile or irregular items (glass jars, thin plastic, connectors) instead of crushing them. Probably the unit WUJI most wants developers on, but it is beta.\n\n| Spec (official docs) | Value |\n|---|---|\n| DoF | **20 active**, back-drivable direct-drive, full thumb opposition |\n| Weight / size | **650 g** bare · 800 g with pads and cables · 70 g base · 180 × 80 × 40 mm |\n| Object size | min grasp diameter 0 mm (pinch) |\n| Fingertip force / payload / joint torque | **not published** in the beta docs |\n| Control | **MIT force-position mode** (default) + position mode (Beta), 1000 Hz × 20 axes |\n| Power | 11–13 V DC, adapter 12 V 20 A (≥ 200 W rated); typical draw not stated |\n| Interfaces | RJ45 Ethernet 100BASE-TX + XT30 (docs warn the connector form will change) |\n| Sensing | no tactile skin (\"non-tactile prototype\"); joint states and diagnostics via SDK |\n| Mounting | standard flange + adapter mount + adapter flange in the box; palm pattern 1 × M3 + 2 × M4; STEP files in `wuji-description`. **Wrist load and shock limits not yet published** |\n| IP rating | not stated — treat as indoor, clean, dry |\n\n- **Status / price:** 🧪 beta hardware · official price not public (third-party listings US$14,600–19,500 — ⚠️ unverified).\n- **Developer access:** per-joint `kp` / `kd`, effort limit (amps in MIT mode, N·m in position mode), position targets, joint states and diagnostics. Official teleop examples switch the hand to position mode first.\n\n### Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI\n![Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI](../assets/wuji-sdk.jpg)\n\n**Role in T03:** the glue. One Python / C SDK for hand, Hand 2 and glove, with the two features a 48-hour team needs most: retargeting and recording.\n\n| Capability | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Install | `pip install wuji-sdk` · Linux x86_64 / arm64, macOS Apple silicon, Windows |\n| Retargeting | `RetargetSession`: **21 MediaPipe-format keypoints (metres) in → 20 joint angles out**, same call for both hand generations. Sources: Wuji Glove skeleton, webcam + MediaPipe, VR hand tracking. Retargeting wheels cover Linux and macOS arm64 only (**not Windows**) |\n| Recording | `TopicRecorder` writes selected channels to one **MCAP** file per episode, with drop-rate / jitter / sync metrics and alerts |\n| ROS 2 | `wuji-ros2` drivers; official install targets Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical |\n\n- **Status / price:** ✅ available · free (MIT).\n\n## What WUJI already does in this domain\n\n**Nothing public.** No WUJI deployment, pilot, demo, partner or application page was found for waste sorting, recycling, disassembly, energy, water or environmental monitoring.\n\n- Official docs position the products for **research, robot integration and human-machine interaction** only.\n- Published demos are generic dexterity: in-hand cube reorientation (`wuji-mjlab`, `wuji-isaaclab`, 2026-10), pen-spin retargeting (`toporetarget`, 2026-06), dual-arm pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning (`wuji-openpi`, 2026-06).\n- Research limits for this file: web search was unavailable during this run, so the check covered the official docs, the official GitHub organisation and the existing company profile. Chinese-language press and trade-show coverage was **not** searched for this track — ⚠️ treat \"nothing found\" as \"nothing found in official channels\".\n\n## What they are building next in this domain\n\nNo sustainability-specific plans are announced. Relevant general direction:\n\n- 🧪 **Hand 2 final version** — the \"non-tactile prototype\" wording implies a tactile version later (inference; no date). Tactile fingertips would matter for material identification by touch.\n- ✅ **Data loop** (glove → retargeting → hand → MCAP → RL / VLA fine-tuning) is the company's stated path to autonomy. *Inference:* that loop fits disassembly and repair, where product variety defeats hard-coded automation, but WUJI has not said so.\n- Interfaces on Hand 2 will change in later 2.2 releases (stated in docs), so anything you build this weekend is a prototype against a moving target.\n\n## Software, models and data that help for this track\n\n| Asset | What it gives you in 48 hours | Caveat |\n|---|---|---|\n| [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) | Hand / glove control, retargeting, MCAP recording from plain Python | Joint-level only |\n| [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) | URDF / MJCF / MJX / USD + STEP files for adapter plates | Rigid bodies only |\n| [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) | ROS 2 drivers and messages for Hand 2 and Glove | Targets Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical; use Docker or skip ROS |\n| [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | Fine-tuning + ROS 2 deployment of pi0 / pi0.5 for dual-arm + two Wuji Hands (54-D actions), LeRobot v2.1 data | **No checkpoints or datasets published**; needs NVIDIA GPU (CUDA 12), ROS 2 Humble client and the archived teleop repo. Not a 48-hour path for most teams |\n| [wuji-mjlab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-mjlab) / [wuji-isaaclab](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-isaaclab) | PPO in-hand cube reorientation with sim-to-real | Task is not sustainability-related; useful only as an RL template |\n| [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop) | ROS 2 hand + arm teleoperation reference | Archived, not maintained |\n\nNo sorting, waste, disassembly or energy datasets or models exist from WUJI. You bring your own vision model (for example an open-vocabulary detector on a laptop GPU or a D-Robotics RDK board).\n\n## Gaps and limits for this track\n\n- **No proof in the domain** and no sustainability story from the vendor: the impact case is entirely yours to build.\n- **Wrong tool for most waste tasks:** real waste is wet, dirty, sharp and abrasive. Gen 1 is IP40; Hand 2 has soft pads, a skin that must stay fitted and fragile flex cables. Use **clean, dry mock items** only.\n- **No arm, no mobility, no perception, no compute.** Budget several hours for flange adaptation, cable routing and payload checks (hand ≈ 0.6–0.9 kg before the object).\n- **Hand 2 unknowns:** payload, fingertip force and wrist-load limits are unpublished; beta firmware; position mode is Beta.\n- **Glove near metal:** EMF finger tracking degrades within 3 cm of metal, which is most e-waste.\n- **Energy optics:** a 20-motor hand with a 12 V 20 A supply is hard to sell as \"energy-efficient\" unless you measure it (gen 1 reports 12 W static and per-joint current).\n- **Access:** unit count unknown; expect shared, supervised time on the hardware.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji SDK data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology repositories](https://github.com/orgs/wuji-technology/repositories)\n- [GitHub: wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n- [T03 track overview (this repo)](../../../Challenges/T03-Sustainable-City/T03-0-Track-Overview.md)\n","WUJI-T03-3-Playbook":"---\ntype: challenge-playbook\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T03\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t03, playbook]\n---\n# WUJI × T03 — Hackathon Playbook\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T03-1-Brief.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T03-2-Products-and-Solutions.md)\n\n**Read first:** WUJI is a **2/5 fit** for T03. It has no sustainability track record and no arm. The concepts below are the credible niches: tasks on objects **made for human fingers**, where a gripper fails, plus human-demonstration capture. All use **clean, dry mock items** (hands are IP40 / beta, pads and cables are fragile). Official T03 directions these map to: T03.1 smart waste sorting, T03.6 smart recycling and resource optimization, T03.3 energy-efficient robotic systems.\n\n## Solution approaches\n\n### Concept 1 — \"Hands that teach\": disassembly demonstration recorder (glove only, hand as mirror)\n\n- **Problem → value:** Repair and disassembly for reuse are manual because every product is different. Recording *how* a skilled person does it (finger poses + **526-point** pressure map) is the missing dataset for automating it. Value: a reusable, labelled demonstration set and a live grip-effort view per step.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove (1–2). Optional: Wuji Hand on a desk stand mirroring the operator live. Optional: webcam for step video. No arm needed.\n- **Architecture / stack:** glove streams (tactile, fingertip poses, skeleton, IMU) → Wuji SDK on a laptop → `TopicRecorder` to one **MCAP per episode** → small Python step-segmenter (pressure peaks + pose change) → dashboard (time per step, peak force per step, parts recovered). Mirror path: glove skeleton → `RetargetSession` → hand joint targets.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: borrow glove, install SDK, verify streams, test tracking next to your actual items (metal check).\n  - H6–24: recording script with episode start / stop, 3 item types (for example remote control, small power adapter, plastic bottle with cap and label), 10 episodes each.\n  - H24–40: step segmentation, dashboard, live hand mirror.\n  - H40–48: rehearse, record backup video, write impact estimate.\n- **3-minute demo script:** 0:00 problem (repair is unscalable without data) → 0:30 operator disassembles one item with glove, hand mirrors it, pressure map live → 1:45 dashboard shows auto-segmented steps and the stored episode → 2:30 how this dataset feeds a robot policy; numbers recorded so far.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** EMF tracking degrades within 3 cm of metal → choose mostly plastic items, or rely on tactile + IMU; no hand available → show the skeleton in a 3-D viewer or MuJoCo with `wuji-description` models.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation medium (data angle is fresh for T03) · technical depth medium · impact indirect (enabler, not a robot doing work — say so) · Leukerbad: repair-café / hotel maintenance framing. **Weakness:** thin \"robot acts on the world\" element.\n\n### Concept 2 — Teleoperated reuse cell: human fingers, robot hand, scripted arm\n\n- **Problem → value:** Small e-waste and multi-material packaging need finger-level work (unclip a cover, pull a battery, peel a connector) before parts can be reused or recycled cleanly. A teleoperated dexterous cell keeps the worker away from the item and logs every action as training data for later autonomy.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand (gen 1 for known force limits, Hand 2 for compliance) + partner arm (Flexiv Rizon, ROKAE xMate or Dobot CR). Fixture or vice to hold the item. Camera over the bench. Optional XREAL glasses as the operator's remote view.\n- **Architecture / stack:** fingers: glove skeleton → `RetargetSession` → hand (Hand 2 in position mode, as in the official teleop examples). Arm: **pre-taught poses** stepped by a foot pedal or key (do not attempt full arm teleop on day 1; the glove tracks fingers, not a global wrist pose — confirm with WUJI). Logging: MCAP for hand + glove, plus arm joint log and video. Compute: one laptop; arm on its own controller.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: secure arm + hand slots, mount hand (adapter flange, cable slack, payload check), glove → hand teleop working on the desk.\n  - H6–24: teach 5–8 arm poses around the fixture; complete one item end-to-end by teleop; add recording.\n  - H24–40: second item type, sorted output bins with a counter, operator view; stretch: replay a recorded finger trajectory autonomously for one step.\n  - H40–48: reliability runs, backup video, impact slide.\n- **3-minute demo script:** 0:00 one-line problem → 0:20 operator (standing apart) opens the item, extracts the battery or board, drops parts into \"reuse\" and \"recycle\" bins → 2:00 show logged episode and the one step that already replays without the human → 2:30 metric: parts recovered per item, minutes per item, path to autonomy.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** mounting eats the first day → fall back to hand on a stand with items handed in by a person; Hand 2 position mode (Beta) unstable → use gen 1; fragile clips need more than fingertip force → pre-loosen and say so; glove near metal → webcam + MediaPipe keypoints as alternative input to the same retargeting call.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation good (dexterous circular-economy cell) · technical depth good (retargeting, multi-device sync, data pipeline) · impact plausible but must be argued per item · Leukerbad: a remote alpine village ships waste down the valley; local repair / pre-sorting of hotel and clinic e-waste is a reasonable framing (your claim to substantiate).\n\n### Concept 3 — Multi-material separator: vision + grasp primitives (autonomous)\n\n- **Problem → value:** Many recyclables are rejected or down-cycled because materials are still joined: metal lid on a glass jar, cap on a bottle, sleeve on a container. Separation is a twist / pinch / peel task, which is where a multi-finger hand beats a gripper.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Hand (gen 1: **15 N** fingertip, max grasp diameter **100 mm**) or Hand 2 on a partner arm; a second arm with a simple gripper or a fixed clamp to hold the container; RGB-D camera; vision on a laptop GPU or D-Robotics RDK board.\n- **Architecture / stack:** camera → detector / classifier (item class + pose) → task selector (which primitive) → arm motion to pre-grasp (vendor SDK or MoveIt) → hand **grasp primitives** written as joint-target sequences (power grasp, tripod pinch, cap-twist with re-grasp) → verify by joint effort / position readback → drop into the correct stream bin.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: mount hand, hand-eye calibration, one power grasp from a fixed pose.\n  - H6–24: tune the cap-twist primitive on one jar size by hand-coded trajectories (use teleop to find good finger poses, then freeze them); detector for 3–4 classes.\n  - H24–40: integrate detect → pick → clamp → twist → sort; success-rate logging.\n  - H40–48: narrow to the items that work, demo polish, energy-per-item measurement.\n- **3-minute demo script:** 0:00 show a jar with lid = contaminated stream → 0:20 robot detects, clamps, unscrews, sorts lid and jar separately; repeat with a bottle → 2:00 success rate over N trials and energy per item → 2:30 what scales (more primitives, learned from glove demos).\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** cap torque exceeds what fingers deliver (Hand 2 forces unpublished) → pre-loosen caps or switch to snap lids; re-grasp twist unreliable → rotate with the arm wrist while the hand only holds; one arm only → fixed clamp; perception late → fixed item positions.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation high · technical depth high · impact clear and countable (items correctly separated) · Leukerbad: glass and packaging volume from hotels and restaurants. Completeness is the risk — scope to **one** item family.\n\n### Concept 4 — Retrofit-free energy round: a robot hand for human interfaces (most ambitious)\n\n- **Problem → value:** Old hotel and clinic buildings waste heat through radiators left on, windows tilted open and lights on in empty rooms. Smart-building retrofits are costly; a mobile robot that operates the **existing** knobs, handles and switches needs no retrofit. Sustainability metric: kWh avoided per round (estimate, state assumptions).\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Hand on a wheeled dual-arm mobile manipulator (Galaxea R1 family, Galbot G1, AGIBOT G1 / G2 or similar on site), its cameras; optional thermal camera. Mock-up wall with a radiator thermostat head, window handle and light switch.\n- **Architecture / stack:** navigation and arm motion from the host robot's stack → detector for fixture type and state → per-fixture hand primitive (wrap-and-twist for thermostat head, hook-and-turn for handle, single-finger press for switch), compliant with Hand 2 MIT gains → log each action and estimated saving. Compute on the host robot or a laptop.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: confirm a host robot will accept a third-party hand (mechanical + power + network); if not, switch to a fixed arm in front of the mock-up.\n  - H6–24: build mock-up wall; three primitives working from fixed poses.\n  - H24–40: perception of fixture state; base repositioning between fixtures (or manual repositioning).\n  - H40–48: run-through, savings model, video.\n- **3-minute demo script:** 0:00 \"empty room, heating on, window tilted\" → 0:20 robot turns the thermostat down, closes the window, switches the light off → 2:00 log and estimated kWh per room per night → 2:30 why a hand (works with any existing fixture) and robot energy cost vs saving.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** integration on a mobile robot not allowed or too slow (likely) → fixed-arm mock-up demo; a gripper could do some of this → emphasise fixture variety and show at least one fixture a gripper cannot handle; net-energy question → measure hand and arm power.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation high · real-world impact strong narrative for an alpine spa town with heated buildings · technical depth depends on how much is autonomous · highest integration risk of the four.\n\n**Stretch for any concept — learned skill:** `wuji-openpi` (pi0 / pi0.5) is a real path but ships **no checkpoints or data**, expects a dual-arm rig, an NVIDIA GPU and a ROS 2 Humble deployment chain. Within 48 hours a replayed trajectory or a small imitation policy on one fixed step is more realistic than VLA fine-tuning.\n\n**Energy figure for the pitch (any concept):** put a DC power meter on the hand's 12 V supply, or on gen 1 integrate per-joint current × bus voltage from the SDK as an approximation. Gen 1 static draw is **12 W** (official); Hand 2 typical draw is not published.\n\n## Cross-vendor combos worth considering\n\n| Combo | What it enables | Integration effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| WUJI Glove + Hand + **Flexiv Rizon** | Force-controlled arm + dexterous hand: compliant disassembly cell (Concepts 2, 3) | Medium — custom adapter plate, payload check, two SDKs |\n| WUJI Glove + Hand + **ROKAE xMate** or **Dobot CR** | Same cell on a more conventional cobot | Medium |\n| WUJI Hand + **Galaxea R1 / Galbot G1 / AGIBOT G1-G2** | Mobile dexterous manipulation for the energy round (Concept 4) | High — third-party end effector on a vendor robot; needs vendor approval |\n| WUJI + **D-Robotics RDK** | Low-power edge vision for item classification (supports the \"low energy\" story); SDK has Linux arm64 builds, hand control from an RDK board ⚠️ unverified | Low–medium |\n| WUJI Glove + **XREAL** glasses | Remote operator view for teleoperated cell | Low–medium |\n| WUJI Glove + **OriginFlow** (EMG capture) | Richer human-demonstration dataset: muscle activity + tactile + pose (Concept 1) | Medium — time sync between two capture systems |\n| WUJI Hand + **Unitree Z1** or other light arm | Compact demo cell | Medium–high — check payload: hand alone is about 0.6–0.9 kg |\n\n## Questions to ask the WUJI engineers on site\n\n1. Which units are here (Hand gen 1, Hand 2, gloves, left / right) and how is access booked?\n2. Which flange adapters did you bring, and which arms on site have you already mounted the hand on?\n3. Hand 2: what fingertip force, payload and wrist load / shock limits should we design for? What must we never do?\n4. Can the hand twist a jar lid or bottle cap? Is there an example of a re-grasp or twist primitive?\n5. Does the glove give a wrist pose usable for arm teleoperation, or fingers only? How does tracking behave next to metal parts in practice?\n6. For glove → Hand 2 teleop, is position mode (Beta) stable enough, or do you recommend MIT mode with specific `kp` / `kd`?\n7. Can the pads / skin be protected (thin over-glove) or cleaned if they touch dusty or sticky items?\n8. Is there a ROS 2 Humble / Jazzy Docker image, and can you share any base checkpoint or demo dataset for `wuji-openpi`?\n\n## Decision rule\n\n- **Pick WUJI for T03 if** your idea hinges on finger-level manipulation of objects made for human hands (disassembly, cap / lid separation, knobs and handles), you have secured a partner arm in the first hours, and you are happy with a teleoperated or semi-autonomous demo on clean mock items.\n- **Avoid if** you want bulk waste sorting, litter picking, outdoor or wet work, environmental monitoring, or a single-vendor autonomous robot — a gripper arm, quadruped or mobile manipulator from another vendor gets you there faster.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [T03 track overview (this repo)](../../../Challenges/T03-Sustainable-City/T03-0-Track-Overview.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 mechanical integration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/hardware-integration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji SDK hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji SDK data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology repositories](https://github.com/orgs/wuji-technology/repositories)\n- [GitHub: wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi)\n","WUJI-T04-1-Brief":"---\ntype: challenge-brief\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T04\nchallenge_title: \"Elderly Care & Rehabilitation\"\nfit: 3\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t04, brief]\n---\n# WUJI × T04 Elderly Care & Rehabilitation — Brief\n\n**Fit: 3/5** — Useful sensing and dexterity building block for hand rehab and assistive manipulation, but no care track record, no robot of its own, nothing medically certified.\n\n| Question | Answer |\n|---|---|\n| Best hardware / platform for this track | **Wuji Glove** ✅ (526 tactile points at 120 FPS, fingertip 6-DoF pose, 67.5 g) — works alone. Second: **Wuji Hand 2** 🧪 (20 DoF, back-drivable) on a stand or partner arm |\n| Strongest proof point (real deployment or demo + date) | **None in care or rehab.** Official docs list only teleoperation, tactile data collection, HCI and VR / AR. Closest asset: official glove → hand teleop example (SDK updated 2026-11-10) |\n| Fastest credible 48-hour demo | Glove-only **hand-function check and exercise game**: live grip-pressure map + finger range of motion, scored against a baseline. Optional: a Wuji Hand mirrors the exercise |\n| Biggest risk | Not a medical device; **one glove size**, no cleaning guidance, EMF tracking disturbed by metal (implant compatibility not stated). Hands scarce; Hand 2 is beta |\n| Pairs well with (other vendors on site) | XREAL (AR-guided therapy) · OriginFlow (EMG) · Flexiv / ROKAE (force-controlled arm for the hand) · D-Robotics (edge host) |\n\n## Why\n- **Glove measures what hand therapy needs**: per-finger pressure zones (4 mm pitch) and a 21-keypoint hand skeleton with joint angles, via a free Python SDK. Caveat: pressure is **normalized 0–1, not newtons** — relative scores only.\n- **Glove-only ideas need no partner robot** — the lowest-risk WUJI path in any track.\n- **Hand 2 can run soft** (per-joint kp / kd, effort limit) for mirror-therapy or object handling at arm's length; the user notice says keep body away while it moves.\n- **Fast tooling**: built-in retargeting (webcam + MediaPipe also works), MCAP recording, simulation models.\n- **Leukerbad angle**: rehab clinics and older spa guests make hand rehab a believable local story.\n\n## Not a fit for\n- Mobility support, fall detection, lifting people, night rounds — no mobile robot, no arm.\n- Force on a patient (massage, physio manipulation) — small fingertip force, no safety certification.\n- Teams wanting ready-made assistive skills — SDK is joint-level, no grasp planner.\n\n## Sources\n[WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Glove introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md) · [Glove tactile reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/tactile.md) · [Hand 2 user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md)\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T04-2-Products-and-Solutions.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T04-3-Playbook.md) · [Track overview](../../../Challenges/T04-Elderly-Care-and-Rehabilitation/T04-0-Track-Overview.md)\n","WUJI-T04-2-Products-and-Solutions":"---\ntype: challenge-products\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T04\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t04, products]\n---\n# WUJI × T04 — Products and Solutions\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T04-1-Brief.md) · [Playbook](WUJI-T04-3-Playbook.md)\n\n**In one line:** WUJI sells a tactile data glove and 20-DoF robot hands. For care and rehab the glove is the stronger card (it works alone); the hands need a stand or a partner arm. WUJI has **no published healthcare activity**.\n\n## Relevant products (ranked for this track)\n\n### Wuji Glove\n\n![Wuji Glove](../assets/wuji-glove.jpg)\n\n**Role in T04:** wearable sensor for hand-function assessment and exercise coaching (grip pressure pattern, finger range of motion, tremor), and the input device for teleoperating a robot hand (tele-care, mirror therapy). The only WUJI product usable without another vendor's robot.\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Tactile sensing | **526 active points** (24 × 31 matrix, full palm side), **120 FPS**, 4 mm pitch, hardware range 0–20 N, 0.1 N resolution, repeatability ±6% |\n| Tactile output in the SDK | **Normalized 0.0–1.0, not newtons**; also grouped by zone (palm 288 points, thumb 41, index 43, middle 58, ring 52, pinky 44), per-point contact yes/no, 3D pressure point cloud |\n| Finger pose | 5 fingertip EMF trackers, 6-DoF, **120 Hz**, ≤ 2 mm RMS position, < 5° RMS orientation, ≤ 10 ms latency |\n| Derived hand model | 21-keypoint skeleton (MediaPipe topology), 21 joint angles in radians, per-finger confidence |\n| IMU | 6-axis on the back of the hand, **800 Hz** (usable for tremor / movement smoothness) |\n| Weight | **67.5 g** glove, 192.6 g with cable |\n| Connection | USB-C power (5 V / 1 A) + RJ45 Ethernet data via adapter — tethered, not wireless |\n| Size | One size listed (215 × 195 mm); no hand-size range given |\n| Environment | −5 to 40 °C, humidity < 55% RH; cleaning / washing guidance: not published |\n\n- **Status / price / availability:** ✅ shipping. Price not public. Units on site: not confirmed.\n- **Developer interface:** Python and C SDK (`pip install wuji-sdk`). Subscribe to `tactile()`, `tactile_zones()`, `tactile_binary()`, `emf_poses()`, `hand_joint_angles()`, `hand_skeleton()` and IMU; set stream rate; record to MCAP. Calibration through the Wuji CLI (`wuji calib hand-model`, `wuji calib tactile`, health check `wuji doctor`); hand-model calibration needs a named user profile.\n\n### Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta)\n\n![Wuji Hand 2](../assets/wuji-hand-2.jpg)\n\n**Role in T04:** compliant robot hand for mirror-therapy / exercise demonstration on a desk stand, or as the end effector for daily-living tasks (caps, pill boxes, cups, handles) on a partner arm.\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Degrees of freedom | **20 active**, 4 per finger, thumb opposition |\n| Drive | Direct-drive, **back-drivable** joints (can be pushed by hand when gains are low) |\n| Control | **MIT force-position mode** (per-joint kp / kd, per-joint `effort_limit` in amperes) · position mode (Beta) · 1000 Hz |\n| Feedback | Joint states incl. effort, joint diagnostics, IMU. **No tactile sensors** in this beta. Docs say not to use joint current to judge contact force |\n| Weight / size | 650 g bare, **800 g** with pads and cables · 180 × 80 × 40 mm |\n| Power / data | 11–13 V DC (12 V 20 A adapter, ≥ 200 W) via XT30 · RJ45 Ethernet |\n| Environment | 15–30 °C, dry and clean; over-temperature protection with thermal derating |\n| Payload / fingertip force | Not committed for the beta (\"may change\") |\n\n- **Status / price / availability:** 🧪 beta prototype; parameters not final. Official price not public (third-party listings US$14,600–19,500 — ⚠️ unverified). Units on site: not confirmed.\n- **Developer interface:** joint-level only. You set targets, gains and effort limits per joint; there is no grasp planner. ROS 2 driver in `wuji-ros2` (official install targets Ubuntu 26.04 + ROS 2 Lyrical).\n- **Safety wording in the user notice:** keep hands and body away while it moves; no long high-load runs; do not grasp fragile or high-value objects; housing can get hot.\n\n### Wuji Hand (gen 1)\n\n![Wuji Hand](../assets/wuji-hand.jpg)\n\n**Role in T04:** the more mature hand; pick it when you need published force numbers and simple USB hookup rather than compliance.\n\n| Track-relevant spec | Value (official docs) |\n|---|---|\n| Degrees of freedom | **20 active**, serial direct-drive, self-locking joints |\n| Fingertip force / grasp | **15 N** fingertip · **10 kg** whole-hand static grasp load |\n| Speed | Open / close ≈ 0.3 s |\n| Control | Position control, 1000 Hz |\n| Weight / size | **580 g** · 201 × 75 × 50 mm |\n| Power / data | 12–20 V DC · USB 2.0 |\n| Protection | IP40 (indoor, dry) |\n\n- **Status / price / availability:** ✅ shipping. Official price not public (reseller \"from US$5,500\" — ⚠️ unverified).\n- **Developer interface:** joint position targets through the unified SDK; retargeting supports it (`HandModel.WujiHand`).\n\n### Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI\n\n![Wuji SDK + Wuji CLI](../assets/wuji-sdk.jpg)\n\n**Role in T04:** the glue for every concept — streaming, retargeting, recording, calibration.\n\n| Capability | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Languages / install | Python + C · `pip install wuji-sdk` · free, MIT repo |\n| Platforms | Linux x86_64 / arm64; Windows and Apple-silicon macOS added in the 2026-11-10 release (per profile research) |\n| Retargeting | `RetargetSession.for_hand(model, side)` → `step(keypoints)`: 21 MediaPipe-format keypoints in, 20 joint angles out; works for Hand 2 and Hand gen 1; only needs `numpy` |\n| Ready example | `examples/python/retargeting/1.teleop_real.py` in `wuji-sdk`: glove → retarget → real hand |\n| Recording | `TopicRecorder` writes MCAP (LZ4 / Zstd), one file per episode, with live quality metrics. Documented channels: hand `joint_states`, `joint_diagnostics`, glove `emf_poses`, `imu_raw/palm`. Tactile recording to MCAP is not listed on that page — ⚠️ unverified |\n| Visualisation | Wuji CLI live visualisation; tactile contact grid view |\n\n## What WUJI already does in this domain\n\n**Nothing public.** No deployment, pilot, clinical study, healthcare partner or care demo was found.\n\n- The official glove page lists four application scenarios: robot-hand teleoperation, tactile data collection and research, human-computer interaction experiments, VR / AR gesture input. Rehabilitation, medical or elderly care are not mentioned.\n- The official docs index (about 167 English pages) contains no healthcare, prosthetics or rehabilitation page.\n- No product is described as a medical device, and no medical certification is published.\n- Research note: the general web search quota was exhausted during this run, so this section rests on the official docs, the GitHub organisation and the profile research (which also found no named customers in any sector). Treat \"nothing public\" as \"nothing found\", and ask WUJI staff on site.\n\n## What they are building next in this domain\n\n- 🔭 **Tactile Hand 2** — inference: the docs call 2.2 a \"non-tactile prototype\", which implies a tactile version later. No date. A tactile robot hand would matter for safe handling of objects around people.\n- ✅ **Unified SDK / CLI across platforms** (Windows and macOS in the 2026-11-10 release) — lowers the barrier for a clinic-style laptop app.\n- ✅ **Glove → retarget → hand → record → train loop** (RL and pi0 / pi0.5 fine-tuning repos) — aimed at humanoid dexterity, not care. Inference: the same loop is what a future home-assist robot would need for daily-living tasks.\n- Healthcare-specific roadmap: **not public**.\n\n## Software, models and data that help for this track\n\n| Asset | Use in a 48-hour T04 build | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| [wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk) | Glove streams, retargeting, MCAP recording; glove → hand teleop example | ✅ MIT, updated 2026-11-10 |\n| [wuji-cli](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-cli) | Device discovery, `wuji doctor`, calibration, live plots | ✅ MIT |\n| [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description) | URDF / MJCF / MJX / USD hand models — build a simulated \"ghost hand\" or test before hardware time | ✅ MIT |\n| [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2) | ROS 2 drivers for Hand 2 and Glove when combining with a ROS-based arm | ✅ MIT (ROS 2 Lyrical target) |\n| [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi) | Fine-tune pi0 / pi0.5 on your own teleop demos (needs GPU and time) | ✅ code only, no checkpoints |\n| [toporetarget](https://github.com/wuji-technology/toporetarget) | Human hand-object motion → Wuji Hand; research-grade | ✅ MIT |\n| Pretrained care / rehab models, datasets | — | none published |\n\nWebcam + MediaPipe produces the same 21-keypoint format as the glove skeleton, so the pose part of any concept can be developed without a glove.\n\n## Gaps and limits for this track\n\n- **No clinical validity.** Pressure comes out normalized (0–1); the ±6% repeatability and lack of a newton mapping in the SDK make it a relative, not a diagnostic, measure.\n- **Fit and hygiene.** One glove size; no guidance for small, swollen or contracted hands; no cleaning instructions. Putting a glove on an arthritic or post-stroke hand may be hard.\n- **Calibration burden.** Hand-model and tactile calibration use guided hand motions; whether a person with limited range of motion can complete them is unknown.\n- **EMF tracking.** Needs ≥ 3 cm clearance from metal (rings, wheelchair or rollator frames, bed rails). Compatibility with pacemakers or other implants is not addressed in the docs — ask before putting it on anyone with an implant.\n- **Tethered.** USB-C power plus Ethernet cable on the wrist.\n- **Robot hands are not people-safe by certification.** No tactile sensing on Hand 2 beta, contact force cannot be inferred from current, housing can get hot, fingers and flex cables are fragile, IP40 / dry only.\n- **No arm, no mobile base, no perception, no grasp planner, no on-board compute** — all must come from your team or another vendor.\n- **Scarcity.** Expect shared, supervised access to hands and gloves.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — tactile data reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/tactile.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — hand tracking data reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/hand-tracking.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — calibration and configuration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/calibration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 — user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 — effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 (2.2 Beta) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/overview.md) (specs taken via the profile research)\n- [Wuji Hand (gen 1) product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/v1/overview.md) (specs taken via the profile research)\n- [Wuji SDK — hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji SDK — data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [Wuji Docs release notes](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/release-notes.md) (via the profile research)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology)\n","WUJI-T04-3-Playbook":"---\ntype: challenge-playbook\ncompany: \"WUJI\"\nslug: WUJI\nchallenge: T04\nupdated: 2026-11-14\ntags: [leukerbad-hackathon, t04, playbook]\n---\n# WUJI × T04 — Hackathon Playbook\n\n⬆ [WUJI profile](../WUJI.md) · [Brief](WUJI-T04-1-Brief.md) · [Products and solutions](WUJI-T04-2-Products-and-Solutions.md)\n\n**Read first:** WUJI brings hands and a glove, not a robot. Concepts 1 and 2 need **no partner arm**; 3 and 4 do. Nothing here is a medical device — present every demo as a prototype tested on team members, not patients.\n\n| # | Concept | WUJI hardware | Partner robot needed | Risk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | GripCheck — glove hand-function check and exercise game | Glove | No | Low |\n| 2 | Mirror Hand — robot hand as exercise partner / tele-therapist | Glove + Hand on a stand | No | Low–medium |\n| 3 | Helping Hand — tele-operated dexterous daily-living tasks | Glove + Hand | Yes (arm) | Medium–high |\n| 4 | Learned daily-living skill from glove demonstrations | Glove + Hand | Yes (arm) + GPU | High |\n\n## Solution approaches\n\n### Concept 1 — GripCheck: glove-based hand-function check and exercise coach\n\n- **Problem → value:** Hand therapy after stroke, fracture or arthritis relies on short clinic sessions and subjective scoring; home exercise is unmonitored. A glove that scores grip pattern and finger mobility gives patient and therapist an objective trend line.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + laptop with Ethernet. Optional: XREAL glasses as a hands-free display; D-Robotics RDK as a standalone host (SDK supports Linux arm64 — ⚠️ untested on RDK).\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Perception: `tactile_zones()` (per-finger and palm pressure, 120 FPS), `hand_joint_angles()` / `hand_skeleton()` (120 Hz), IMU (800 Hz).\n  - Features: per-finger peak and mean pressure (normalized), left / right or finger-to-finger balance, range of motion per joint, open / close time, tremor band power from the IMU.\n  - Logic: 3–4 standard-style tasks (full fist, finger opposition, cylinder grasp, pinch) → score against the user's own baseline → adaptive exercise game (squeeze / stretch to steer).\n  - Output: web dashboard (FastAPI + browser) and a one-page session summary; an LLM can phrase the summary but must not diagnose.\n  - Compute: laptop only.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: book a glove; `wuji doctor`, calibration, stream all channels; log to file. Build pose features on webcam + MediaPipe in parallel (same 21-keypoint format).\n  - H6–24: feature extraction, baseline + scoring, one game, dashboard.\n  - H24–40: test on 5+ people (include older volunteers if available and willing), tune thresholds, session report, trend view.\n  - H40–48: polish, record backup video, rehearse.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (0:00) the problem in one sentence with a Leukerbad rehab-clinic framing → (0:30) volunteer puts glove on, live pressure map and skeleton → (1:15) runs two test tasks, score appears vs baseline → (2:00) 30-second game → (2:30) therapist report and week-over-week trend (pre-recorded data) → (2:50) limits and next step.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** glove unavailable or does not fit → webcam + MediaPipe for pose, drop pressure. Normalized pressure only → present relative scores, never newtons. EMF glitches near metal → clear the table, remove rings.\n- **Judging angles:** impact and Leukerbad relevance are strong (rehab clinics, older guests); technical depth is moderate — raise it with validated features and a clean longitudinal data model; innovation is moderate (data gloves for rehab exist; the dense palm pressure map is the differentiator).\n\n### Concept 2 — Mirror Hand: robot hand as exercise partner and tele-therapist\n\n- **Problem → value:** Therapists cannot be in every room or every valley. A robot hand on the patient's table physically shows the exercise (driven live by a remote therapist's glove, or replayed), while the patient's own movement is scored. Variant: the healthy hand drives a mirrored robot hand as a 3D take on mirror therapy (an established stroke-rehab technique; the robot variant is a hypothesis, not evidence).\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + one Wuji Hand (gen 1 or Hand 2) on a desk stand. Patient side: webcam or a second glove. Optional: XREAL for the patient view.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Therapist glove `hand_skeleton()` → `RetargetSession` → hand joint targets (start from the official `1.teleop_real.py`).\n  - Mirroring: flip handedness / mirror keypoints before retargeting.\n  - Record exercises (joint trajectories) and replay them at reduced speed; Hand 2 in MIT mode with low kp and a low `effort_limit` so it stays soft.\n  - Patient tracking: webcam + MediaPipe → compare joint-angle trajectories with the demonstrated exercise (DTW or simple per-joint error) → feedback.\n  - Remote link: send the 21 keypoints over WebSocket / WebRTC data channel; compute on two laptops.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: run glove → hand teleop from the official example; confirm which hand generation you get.\n  - H6–24: record / replay library of 5 exercises; mirroring; patient-side tracking and similarity score.\n  - H24–40: remote link between two laptops, latency check, soft-gain tuning, UI.\n  - H40–48: polish, backup video, rehearse.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (0:00) \"one therapist, many patients, steep valley\" → (0:30) therapist across the room moves gloved hand, robot hand follows → (1:10) patient copies, live similarity score → (1:50) therapist leaves, robot replays the prescribed set, patient continues → (2:30) mirror-mode in 15 seconds → (2:45) limits.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** no hand available → render the hand in MuJoCo from `wuji-description` (works fully in simulation). Retargeting artefacts on thumb → restrict to exercises that look right. Hand overheating on long runs → short sets, pauses.\n- **Judging angles:** innovation is higher than Concept 1 (physical demonstration + tele-care); technical depth from retargeting, compliant control and trajectory comparison; impact story is tele-rehab for mountain regions.\n\n### Concept 3 — Helping Hand: tele-operated dexterous assistance for daily living\n\n- **Problem → value:** Many daily tasks that defeat weak or arthritic hands are dexterity tasks: bottle caps, pill organisers, blister packs, zips. A remote caregiver wearing a glove operates a robot hand to do them — one caregiver can serve several residents without travelling.\n- **Hardware:** Wuji Glove + Wuji Hand on a partner arm — Flexiv Rizon or ROKAE xMate (force-controlled, good near people), or Dobot CR / Nova. Check flange adapter, payload (Hand 2 is 800 g with cables) and 12 V / 20 A power routing. Camera for the operator view.\n- **Architecture / stack:**\n  - Fingers: glove → `RetargetSession` → hand (1000 Hz joint interface).\n  - Arm: keep it simple — hand-guide and store 4–6 poses (above pill box, above bottle, handover zone) and let the operator switch between them, with small jog offsets. Full wrist-pose teleop needs an external tracker (the archived `wuji-hand-teleop` used Vive Tracker / PICO 4) and is a time sink.\n  - Safety: arm in low-speed collaborative mode with force limits; handover only by placing objects on a tray, not hand-to-hand.\n  - Compute: one laptop (WUJI SDK) + arm controller; ROS 2 optional (`wuji-ros2` targets ROS 2 Lyrical — check before committing).\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6: secure arm + hand + adapter; mount; move both from one script.\n  - H6–24: finger teleop on the arm, taught arm poses, operator camera view; pick two tasks that work (for example open a flip-top pill box, lift a cup).\n  - H24–40: reliability runs (target 8 / 10), operator UI, e-stop routine, optional remote link.\n  - H40–48: polish, backup video, rehearse.\n- **3-minute demo script:** (0:00) resident cannot open the pill organiser → (0:30) caregiver \"at another site\" puts on the glove → (0:50) arm moves to the box, fingers open the lid and pick the day's compartment → (1:50) arm places it on the tray, resident takes it → (2:20) second task or log of \"medication given\" → (2:45) path to autonomy (Concept 4).\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** no adapter or no arm slot → fall back to Concept 2 on a stand. No tactile on the robot hand and no force estimate from current → choose rigid, light, cheap objects; avoid anything fragile (the user notice says so). Hand 2 beta faults → use gen 1 (position control, 15 N fingertip).\n- **Judging angles:** strongest \"robot helps a person\" visual; technical depth from multi-vendor integration; impact is caregiver relief; be ready for the question \"why a 20-DoF hand instead of a gripper\" — answer with the cap / lid / blister tasks.\n\n### Concept 4 — Learned daily-living skill from glove demonstrations\n\n- **Problem → value:** Tele-operation does not scale; show that the same rig can learn one daily-living task from a few dozen demonstrations and then run it on request.\n- **Hardware:** Concept 3 rig + wrist / scene cameras + a GPU machine (on-site workstation or cloud).\n- **Architecture / stack:** collect 50–100 demonstrations with the Concept 3 teleop (record hand joint states with `TopicRecorder` to MCAP, plus arm states and camera frames with your own logger, synchronised on timestamps) → train a small imitation policy (ACT or diffusion policy), or fine-tune pi0 / pi0.5 with `wuji-openpi` if GPU time allows → run with a voice or button trigger and a tele-op takeover fallback.\n- **48-hour plan:**\n  - H0–6 and H6–24: as Concept 3, but lock the task and camera setup by H12 and start collecting by H18.\n  - H24–40: train, evaluate, collect more where it fails; keep teleop demo working in parallel.\n  - H40–48: decide honestly: autonomous run if ≥ 60% success, otherwise show teleop + learned sub-skill.\n- **3-minute demo script:** Concept 3 story, then \"now without the caregiver\": press the button, policy runs; show success rate and one failure honestly; takeover by glove.\n- **Risks and fallbacks:** highest risk — data pipeline and training time usually overrun 48 hours; no WUJI checkpoints exist to start from. Fallback is Concept 3 exactly as built.\n- **Judging angles:** top technical depth and innovation if it works; weakest reliability. Only for teams with prior imitation-learning experience.\n\n## Cross-vendor combos worth considering\n\n| Combo | What it enables | Integration effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wuji Glove + XREAL AR glasses | AR-guided therapy: ghost target hand, pressure heat-map and score in view | Medium (stream from laptop to glasses app) |\n| Wuji Glove + OriginFlow EMG | Muscle activity + ground-truth finger pose and pressure: fatigue / effort metrics, or an EMG → hand-pose decoder driving a Wuji Hand (prosthesis-style demo) | Medium–high (depends on OriginFlow's SDK — ⚠️ unverified) |\n| Wuji Hand + Flexiv Rizon / ROKAE xMate | Compliant arm + dexterous hand for lids, pill boxes, cups | High (adapter, power, two SDKs) |\n| Wuji Hand + Dobot CR / Nova | Same as above with a simpler cobot | Medium–high |\n| Wuji Glove + Galaxea R1 / Galbot G1 / UniX Wanda | Glove as an intuitive teleop input for an existing mobile manipulator's own grippers (map pinch aperture) | Medium |\n| Wuji Hand on a humanoid (Unitree, AGIBOT) | Dexterous hand on a walking platform | Very high — avoid unless adapters and drivers already exist on site |\n| WUJI stack + D-Robotics RDK | Laptop-free bedside unit running the glove app | Low–medium (Linux arm64 wheels exist; ⚠️ untested) |\n\n## Questions to ask the WUJI engineers on site\n\n1. How many gloves and hands are here, which sides and generations, and how is access booked?\n2. Does the glove fit small or stiff hands? Is there a liner or a cleaning procedure between users?\n3. Is the EMF tracker safe to use on people with pacemakers or other implants, and how badly do rings, wheelchair frames or bed rails disturb it?\n4. Can a person with limited finger range complete hand-model and tactile calibration, or can we use a default / therapist-made model?\n5. Is there a mapping from the normalized tactile value (0–1) to newtons, and can tactile streams be recorded to MCAP?\n6. Which arm flange adapters did you bring, and how should the 12 V / 20 A supply be routed along an arm?\n7. For Hand 2: recommended kp / kd and `effort_limit` values for a soft, people-adjacent demo, and how long can it run before thermal derating?\n8. Do glove calibration and the CLI work on macOS / Windows today, or should we plan for a Linux laptop? Is there a Docker image for ROS 2 Lyrical?\n9. Does WUJI have any healthcare or rehab customers, or plans in that direction?\n\n## Decision rule\n\n- **Pick WUJI for T04 if** your idea is about the hand itself — measuring, coaching or remotely lending hand function — and you can get a glove early; add a partner arm only if you have integration experience and a confirmed adapter.\n- **Avoid if** you need a mobile, whole-body or lifting assistant, autonomous behaviour out of the box, or anything that must touch or support a person with force.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [WUJI profile (this repo)](../WUJI.md)\n- [Wuji Glove product introduction](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/introduction.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — tactile data reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/tactile.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — hand tracking data reference](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/sdk-data-reference/hand-tracking.md)\n- [Wuji Glove — calibration and configuration](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-glove/latest/calibration.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 — user notice](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/user-notice.md)\n- [Wuji Hand 2 — effort and MIT parameters](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-hand/latest/sdk-reference/effort-and-mit.md)\n- [Wuji SDK — hand retargeting](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/retargeting.md)\n- [Wuji SDK — data recording](https://docs.wuji.tech/docs/en/wuji-sdk/latest/data-recording.md)\n- [Wuji Docs — English index](https://docs.wuji.tech/_llms/en.txt)\n- [GitHub: wuji-technology](https://github.com/wuji-technology) ([wuji-sdk](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-sdk), [wuji-description](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-description), [wuji-ros2](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-ros2), [wuji-openpi](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-openpi), [wuji-hand-teleop](https://github.com/wuji-technology/wuji-hand-teleop))\n"}});
